window.LEVEL_PACKS.b2p={"units": {"1": {"n": 1, "title": "Ethics and Moral Dilemmas", "ar": "الأخلاق والمعضلات الأخلاقية — Hedging Language", "icon": "⚖️", "cover": "img/b2p/u1.jpg", "intro": "اتكلم عن الصح والغلط والمواقف الصعبة اللي مفيهاش إجابة سهلة، واستخدم الـ Hedging Language عشان تعبّر عن رأيك بأدب ومن غير ما تكون حاد: It could be argued that… / It seems that… / tend to.", "videos": [{"id": "b2pv1", "title": "The AI Essay", "ar": "المقال اللي كتبه الذكاء الاصطناعي — ليلى وآدم", "src": "video/b2p/u1v1.mp4", "poster": "img/b2p/u1v1.jpg", "sp": {"a": {"n": "Layla", "g": "f"}, "b": {"n": "Adam", "g": "m"}}, "lines": [["a", "Adam, can I ask your opinion? I have a bit of a moral dilemma.", "آدم، ممكن آخد رأيك؟ عندي معضلة أخلاقية صغيرة."], ["b", "Sure. What happened?", "أكيد. إيه اللي حصل؟"], ["a", "My friend Rana used AI to write her whole essay, and she got the highest grade in the class. I worked on mine for two weeks.", "صاحبتي رنا استخدمت الذكاء الاصطناعي يكتبلها المقال كله، وخدت أعلى درجة في الفصل. وأنا اشتغلت على بتاعي أسبوعين."], ["b", "That's frustrating. Are you thinking of telling the teacher?", "ده يضايق. بتفكري تقولي للمدرّسة؟"], ["a", "That's the problem. It could be argued that it's unfair to everyone else. But she's my friend.", "دي المشكلة. ممكن يتقال إن ده ظلم لكل الباقيين. بس هي صاحبتي."], ["b", "I see. It seems to me that honesty matters, but maybe there are better ways than reporting her straight away.", "فاهم. أنا شايف إن الأمانة مهمة، بس يمكن في طرق أحسن من إنك تبلّغي عنها على طول."], ["a", "Like what?", "زي إيه؟"], ["b", "You could talk to her first. People tend to admit mistakes more easily when they are not attacked.", "ممكن تكلميها الأول. الناس غالبًا بيعترفوا بأخطائهم أسهل لما محدش بيهاجمهم."], ["a", "That's true. Apparently, the school is introducing new rules about AI next term anyway.", "صح. وعلى ما يبدو، المدرسة هتعمل قواعد جديدة عن الذكاء الاصطناعي الترم الجاي أصلًا."], ["b", "Then it's arguably a good moment to discuss it openly. Maybe AI isn't the problem — it's how we use it.", "يبقى غالبًا ده وقت مناسب نتكلم فيه بصراحة. يمكن الذكاء الاصطناعي مش هو المشكلة — المشكلة في إزاي بنستخدمه."], ["a", "You're right. I'll talk to Rana tomorrow. I'd rather be honest than just stay silent.", "عندك حق. هكلم رنا بكرة. أفضّل أكون صريحة بدل ما أسكت وخلاص."], ["b", "Good decision. Doing the right thing isn't always easy, but it's usually worth it.", "قرار كويس. إنك تعمل الصح مش دايمًا سهل، بس غالبًا بيستاهل."]], "quiz": [{"q": "What did Layla's friend do?", "o": ["used AI to write her whole essay", "copied from Layla", "missed the exam"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Why is Layla frustrated?", "o": ["She worked hard for two weeks but got a lower grade.", "She failed the exam.", "Her friend stopped talking to her."], "a": 0}, {"q": "What does Adam suggest?", "o": ["talking to her friend first", "reporting her immediately", "doing nothing"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What is the school planning?", "o": ["new rules about AI next term", "banning computers", "cancelling essays"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What is Layla's final decision?", "o": ["to talk to Rana tomorrow", "to tell the teacher today", "to use AI herself"], "a": 0}], "fill": [[0, "moral dilemma"], [2, "highest grade"], [4, "It could be argued"], [4, "unfair"], [5, "It seems to me"], [5, "honesty"], [7, "tend to"], [7, "admit"], [8, "Apparently"], [9, "arguably"], [10, "honest"], [11, "right thing"]]}], "vocab": [{"t": "Right & wrong", "ar": "الصح والغلط", "items": [["⚖️", "ethics", "Business ethics are taught at university."], ["🤔", "moral dilemma", "Should I tell the truth? It's a moral dilemma."], ["✅", "ethical", "Is it ethical to test products on animals?"], ["❌", "unethical", "Copying someone's work is unethical."], ["🧭", "conscience", "My conscience told me to return the money."], ["🤝", "integrity", "She is a person of great integrity."], ["💬", "honesty", "Honesty is the best policy."], ["🙈", "cheat", "Cheating in exams is never acceptable."]]}, {"t": "Judging actions", "ar": "الحكم على التصرفات", "items": [["⚖️", "fair", "It's not fair to punish everyone."], ["🙅", "unfair", "The decision was unfair to the poor."], ["👍", "justify", "Can you justify your decision?"], ["🔍", "consequences", "Think about the consequences of your actions."], ["🎯", "principle", "I never lie — it's a matter of principle."], ["😔", "guilty", "I felt guilty for not helping him."], ["🙌", "responsible", "We are responsible for our choices."], ["🌗", "grey area", "Using AI for homework is a grey area."]]}, {"t": "Discussing opinions", "ar": "مناقشة الآراء", "items": [["🗣️", "argue", "Some people argue that lying is sometimes necessary."], ["📌", "point of view", "From my point of view, it was wrong."], ["🤷", "controversial", "It is a very controversial topic."], ["🧠", "reasonable", "That sounds like a reasonable idea."], ["🔁", "on the other hand", "On the other hand, she was trying to help."], ["📣", "admit", "He admitted that he was wrong."], ["🧩", "complex", "Ethical questions are often complex."], ["🌍", "society", "What kind of society do we want?"]]}], "talk": [{"title": "Let's Talk · Student A", "ar": "الطالب A", "list": [["Is it ever acceptable to lie? When?", "الكدب ممكن يكون مقبول؟ إمتى؟", "Arguably, a small lie to protect someone's feelings."], ["Would you report a friend who cheated in an exam?", "تبلّغ عن صاحبك لو غش في امتحان؟", "I would probably talk to him first."], ["Is using AI for homework cheating?", "استخدام الذكاء الاصطناعي في الواجب غش؟", "It depends on how you use it."], ["If you found a wallet with a lot of money, what would you do?", "لو لقيت محفظة فيها فلوس كتير، تعمل إيه؟", "I'd return it — it's a matter of principle."], ["Who taught you the difference between right and wrong?", "مين علّمك الفرق بين الصح والغلط؟", "My grandmother, mostly."]]}, {"title": "Let's Talk · Student B", "ar": "الطالب B", "list": [["Is it ethical to eat meat?", "أكل اللحوم أخلاقي؟", "Most people think so, but some disagree."], ["Should companies care about ethics or only about profit?", "الشركات لازم تهتم بالأخلاق ولا بالربح بس؟", "Both, because customers tend to trust ethical brands."], ["Is it right to break a rule to help someone?", "صح تكسر قاعدة عشان تساعد حد؟", "In some cases, it could be argued that it is."], ["Are people today more or less honest than in the past?", "الناس النهارده أصدق ولا أقل صدق من زمان؟", "Probably the same, but we hear about lies more."], ["What is the hardest decision you have ever made?", "إيه أصعب قرار خدته؟", "Choosing between two universities."]]}], "grammar": {"title": "Hedging Language", "ar": "لغة التحفّظ — إزاي تقول رأيك من غير ما تبقى حاد", "blocks": [{"type": "intro", "en": "Hedging means making your statements less direct and less absolute. We use it in discussions, academic writing and polite conversation to show that something is possible or likely — not 100% certain.", "ar": "الـ Hedging يعني إنك تخلي كلامك أقل حدة ومش مطلق. بنستخدمه في المناقشات والكتابة الأكاديمية والكلام المؤدب عشان نوضح إن الحاجة محتملة — مش أكيدة ١٠٠٪."}, {"type": "big", "items": [{"v": "It + passive verb + that…", "p": "impersonal hedging", "c": 1, "eg": ["It could be argued that this is unfair.", "It is often said that money cannot buy happiness.", "It has been suggested that AI will change education."]}, {"v": "seem / appear / tend to", "p": "softening verbs", "c": 2, "eg": ["It seems that most people agree.", "She appears to be telling the truth.", "People tend to forgive honest mistakes."]}, {"v": "may / might / could + adverbs", "p": "possibility & adverbs", "c": 3, "eg": ["This might be the best solution.", "It is arguably the most difficult decision.", "Apparently, the rules will change next year."]}]}, {"type": "table", "title": "📋 Direct vs hedged", "head": ["Direct (strong)", "Hedged (softer)"], "rows": [["This is wrong.", "It could be argued that this is wrong."], ["Everyone agrees.", "Most people seem to agree."], ["Students cheat.", "Some students tend to cheat."], ["AI will destroy jobs.", "AI may lead to the loss of some jobs."], ["He is lying.", "He appears not to be telling the truth."]]}, {"type": "uses", "title": "💡 Useful hedging words", "ar": "كلمات تحفّظ مفيدة", "items": [["🤏", "quantifiers", "some, many, most, a number of", "بدل all/everyone"], ["📉", "frequency", "often, usually, generally, in some cases", "بدل always"], ["🔮", "probability", "probably, possibly, likely, arguably", "احتمال"], ["💬", "opinion", "To some extent… / As far as I know…", "رأي بأدب"]]}, {"type": "tip", "en": "Don't over-hedge! 'It might perhaps possibly be true' sounds weak. One hedge is usually enough. And remember: tend to + base verb (People tend to agree ✔ — not tend to agreeing ✖).", "ar": "متكترش التحفظ! جملة فيها might وperhaps وpossibly مع بعض شكلها ضعيفة. تحفظ واحد كفاية. وtend to بعدها فعل مجرد: tend to agree."}]}, "exercises": [{"type": "mcq", "title": "Hedging — 10 MCQs", "ar": "اختار الصح", "speak": true, "items": [{"q": "It could be ___ that the rule is unfair.", "o": ["argued", "argue", "arguing", "argument"], "a": 0}, {"q": "People ___ to forgive honest mistakes.", "o": ["tend", "seem that", "appear that", "tends"], "a": 0}, {"q": "It ___ that most students use AI sometimes.", "o": ["seems", "tends", "is seemed", "seem"], "a": 0}, {"q": "He ___ to be telling the truth, but I am not sure.", "o": ["appears", "appears that", "is appeared", "tends that"], "a": 0}, {"q": "___, the school will change the rules next year.", "o": ["Apparently", "Apparent", "Appear", "Appearing"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Which sentence is the most hedged (softest)?", "o": ["AI may lead to the loss of some jobs.", "AI will destroy all jobs.", "AI destroys jobs.", "AI is destroying every job."], "a": 0}, {"q": "It is often ___ that honesty is the best policy.", "o": ["said", "say", "saying", "says"], "a": 0}, {"q": "This is ___ the most difficult question in ethics.", "o": ["arguably", "argue", "arguable that", "argued"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Which word is NOT a hedging word?", "o": ["definitely", "probably", "possibly", "likely"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Which sentence is correct?", "o": ["Young people tend to use AI more.", "Young people tend using AI more.", "Young people tends to use AI more.", "Young people tend to used AI more."], "a": 0}]}, {"type": "mcq", "title": "Make it softer", "ar": "خلّيها ألطف", "items": [{"q": "\"Everyone cheats.\" → ___", "o": ["Some people seem to cheat.", "Everyone always cheats."], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"This is wrong.\" → ___", "o": ["It could be argued that this is wrong.", "This is completely wrong."], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"He is lying.\" → ___", "o": ["He might not be telling the truth.", "He is definitely lying."], "a": 0}, {"q": "tend to + ___", "o": ["base verb", "-ing"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Hedging is common in ___.", "o": ["academic writing and polite discussion", "angry arguments"], "a": 0}]}, {"type": "ord", "title": "Make sentences", "ar": "رتّب الكلمات", "items": [{"c": ["It could be", "argued that", "the rule", "is unfair"], "a": [0, 1, 2, 3]}, {"c": ["People", "tend to", "forgive", "honest mistakes"], "a": [0, 1, 2, 3]}, {"c": ["It seems", "that", "most people", "agree"], "a": [0, 1, 2, 3]}, {"c": ["This", "might be", "the best", "solution"], "a": [0, 1, 2, 3]}]}], "reading": {"title": "The Trolley Problem", "ar": "معضلة العربة", "g": "m", "lines": [["Imagine a runaway train is speeding towards five workers on the track. You are standing next to a lever. If you pull it, the train will change direction — but it will hit one worker on the other track. What would you do?", "تخيّل قطر فالت جاي بسرعة ناحية ٥ عمال على القضبان. وإنت واقف جنب ذراع. لو شديته، القطر هيغير اتجاهه — بس هيخبط عامل واحد على القضبان التانية. هتعمل إيه؟"], ["This famous thought experiment, known as \"the trolley problem\", has been discussed by philosophers for decades.", "التجربة الفكرية المشهورة دي، المعروفة باسم \"معضلة العربة\"، الفلاسفة بيناقشوها من عشرات السنين."], ["Surveys suggest that most people tend to choose to pull the lever. Saving five lives rather than one seems, to many, the logical choice.", "الاستطلاعات بتقول إن أغلب الناس بيميلوا يختاروا إنهم يشدوا الذراع. إنقاذ ٥ أرواح بدل واحدة شكله، لناس كتير، الاختيار المنطقي."], ["However, when the question is changed slightly, the answers change dramatically.", "لكن لما السؤال بيتغير شوية صغيرين، الإجابات بتتغير بشكل كبير."], ["If, instead of pulling a lever, you had to push a person onto the track to stop the train, very few people say they would do it — even though the result would be the same.", "لو بدل ما تشد ذراع، كان لازم تزق شخص على القضبان عشان توقف القطر، ناس قليلة جدًا بيقولوا إنهم هيعملوها — رغم إن النتيجة واحدة."], ["It could be argued that this shows how emotions, and not only logic, guide our moral decisions.", "ممكن يتقال إن ده بيوضح إن المشاعر، مش المنطق بس، هي اللي بتوجّه قراراتنا الأخلاقية."], ["Today, the trolley problem is no longer just a classroom exercise. Engineers designing self-driving cars face similar questions.", "النهارده، معضلة العربة مبقتش مجرد تمرين في الفصل. المهندسين اللي بيصمموا العربيات اللي بتسوق نفسها بيواجهوا أسئلة شبهها."], ["Should a car protect its passengers at any cost, or should it try to save the greatest number of people?", "العربية لازم تحمي ركابها مهما كان التمن، ولا تحاول تنقذ أكبر عدد من الناس؟"], ["Interestingly, studies appear to show that answers vary between cultures, ages and even genders.", "والمثير إن الدراسات شكلها بتوضح إن الإجابات بتختلف حسب الثقافات والأعمار وحتى الجنس."], ["Perhaps the real value of the trolley problem is not finding the \"right\" answer, but understanding why we disagree.", "يمكن القيمة الحقيقية لمعضلة العربة مش إننا نلاقي الإجابة \"الصح\"، لكن إننا نفهم إحنا ليه بنختلف."]], "keys": [["🚃", "runaway", "moving out of control"], ["🕹️", "lever", "a handle you pull to operate a machine"], ["💭", "thought experiment", "an imagined situation used to think about a question"], ["🧑‍🏫", "philosopher", "a person who studies deep questions about life and knowledge"], ["🚗", "self-driving car", "a car that drives without a human"], ["🔀", "vary", "to be different"]], "quiz": [{"q": "What happens if you pull the lever?", "o": ["The train hits one worker instead of five.", "The train stops.", "Nobody gets hurt."], "a": 0}, {"q": "What do most people choose in the first version?", "o": ["to pull the lever", "to do nothing", "to run away"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What happens when people must push a person instead?", "o": ["Very few say they would do it.", "Everyone agrees to do it.", "They pull the lever."], "a": 0}, {"q": "What could this show?", "o": ["Emotions guide our moral decisions too.", "People are always logical.", "Trains are dangerous."], "a": 0}, {"q": "Who faces similar questions today?", "o": ["engineers designing self-driving cars", "chefs", "football players"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What is perhaps the real value of the trolley problem?", "o": ["understanding why we disagree", "finding the one right answer", "learning about trains"], "a": 0}]}, "idioms": {"items": [["a slippery slope", "A small action that could lead to much worse things.", "بداية طريق خطير", "Copying one answer is a slippery slope — soon you copy everything.", "إنك تنقل إجابة واحدة بداية طريق خطير — بعدها هتنقل كل حاجة."], ["turn a blind eye", "To pretend not to see something wrong.", "يعمل نفسه مش شايف", "The manager turned a blind eye to the problem.", "المدير عمل نفسه مش شايف المشكلة."], ["the lesser of two evils", "The less bad of two bad choices.", "أهون الشرّين", "Both options were bad, so I chose the lesser of two evils.", "الاختيارين كانوا وحشين، فاخترت أهون الشرين."], ["practise what you preach", "To do what you tell other people to do.", "يعمل اللي بيقوله لغيره", "Don't tell me to be honest if you don't practise what you preach.", "متقوليش أكون صريح لو إنت مش بتعمل اللي بتقوله."]], "quiz": [{"q": "He tells everyone to save money, but he spends everything. He doesn't ___.", "o": ["practise what he preaches", "turn a blind eye", "take a slippery slope", "choose the lesser evil"], "a": 0}, {"q": "The teacher saw them cheating but ___.", "o": ["turned a blind eye", "practised what she preached", "was a slippery slope", "chose two evils"], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"The lesser of two evils\" means…", "o": ["the less bad of two bad choices", "two good choices", "a scary film", "a small mistake"], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"A slippery slope\" means…", "o": ["a small action that may lead to worse things", "a wet floor", "a ski trip", "a fast decision"], "a": 0}]}, "phrasal": {"items": [["own up to", "To admit that you did something wrong.", "يعترف بغلطته", "He owned up to breaking the window.", "اعترف إنه هو اللي كسر الشباك."], ["stand up for", "To defend something or someone.", "يدافع عن", "Always stand up for what you believe in.", "دايمًا دافع عن اللي إنت مؤمن بيه."], ["go along with", "To agree with or accept something, often without wanting to.", "يمشي مع / يوافق", "I didn't like the plan, but I went along with it.", "مكنتش حابب الخطة، بس مشيت معاها."], ["let someone down", "To disappoint someone.", "يخذل حد", "I promised to help, and I won't let you down.", "وعدتك أساعدك، ومش هخذلك."]], "quiz": [{"q": "It takes courage to ___ your mistakes.", "o": ["own up to", "let down", "go along with", "stand up"], "a": 0}, {"q": "She always ___ people who are treated unfairly.", "o": ["stands up for", "owns up to", "lets down", "goes along"], "a": 0}, {"q": "You promised to come! Don't ___ me ___.", "o": ["let / down", "own / up", "stand / up", "go / along"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Everyone agreed, so I just ___ the decision.", "o": ["went along with", "stood up for", "owned up to", "let down"], "a": 0}]}, "slang": {"items": [["shady", "Dishonest or suspicious.", "مشبوه / مش نضيف", "Selling fake reviews is pretty shady.", "بيع تقييمات مزيفة ده شغل مشبوه.", "بين الصحاب"], ["big yikes", "Very bad or embarrassing.", "يا ساتر! / فضيحة", "He lied to his teacher and got caught? Big yikes.", "كدب على المدرس واتقفش؟ يا ساتر.", "رد فعل بهزار"], ["keep it real", "Be honest and genuine.", "خليك على طبيعتك وصريح", "I like her — she always keeps it real.", "بحبها — دايمًا صريحة وعلى طبيعتها.", "مدح"], ["red flag", "A warning sign that something is wrong.", "علامة خطر", "A friend who asks you to lie for him? Red flag.", "صاحب بيطلب منك تكدب عشانه؟ علامة خطر.", "منتشرة جدًا"], ["that's on you", "That's your responsibility / your fault.", "دي مسؤوليتك إنت", "You didn't study — that's on you.", "إنت مذاكرتش — دي مسؤوليتك.", "صريحة شوية — قولها بلطف"]], "quiz": [{"q": "\"Red flag\" means…", "o": ["a warning sign", "a football card", "a country flag", "a red T-shirt"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Someone who is always honest and genuine ___.", "o": ["keeps it real", "is shady", "is a red flag", "big yikes"], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"Big yikes\" shows that something is…", "o": ["very bad or embarrassing", "very big", "very cheap", "very easy"], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"You were late again? That's on you.\" means…", "o": ["It's your responsibility.", "It's on the table.", "It's my fault.", "It's on TV."], "a": 0}]}, "story": {"title": "The Envelope", "ar": "الظرف", "g": "f", "lines": [["Youssef worked as a cashier in a small supermarket. One evening, an old man paid for his shopping and left — but he forgot a brown envelope on the counter.", "يوسف كان شغال كاشير في سوبر ماركت صغير. في ليلة، راجل كبير دفع حساب مشترياته ومشي — بس نسي ظرف بني على الكاونتر."], ["Inside were five thousand pounds and a note that said: \"For my granddaughter's operation.\"", "جواه كان فيه ٥ آلاف جنيه وورقة مكتوب فيها: \"عشان عملية حفيدتي.\""], ["At that moment, Youssef was struggling. His rent was late, and his own mother needed medicine.", "في اللحظة دي، يوسف كان بيعاني. الإيجار متأخر، ووالدته محتاجة دوا."], ["\"Nobody saw it,\" his colleague whispered. \"It could be argued that you need it more.\"", "\"محدش شافه،\" زميله وشوش. \"ممكن تقول إنك محتاجه أكتر.\""], ["For a moment, Youssef considered it. It seemed like the answer to all his problems.", "للحظة، يوسف فكّر فيها. كانت باينة إنها حل كل مشاكله."], ["But then he imagined the old man arriving home and realising the money was gone.", "بس بعدين تخيّل الراجل الكبير وهو بيوصل البيت ويكتشف إن الفلوس ضاعت."], ["He refused to turn a blind eye to his conscience. He checked the CCTV, found the man's face, and asked the manager for help.", "رفض يتجاهل ضميره. راجع كاميرات المراقبة، ولقى وش الراجل، وطلب مساعدة من المدير."], ["The next morning, the old man returned, pale and desperate. When Youssef handed him the envelope, he burst into tears.", "تاني يوم الصبح، الراجل الكبير رجع، وشه أصفر ويائس. لما يوسف اداله الظرف، انفجر في العياط."], ["A week later, a letter arrived at the supermarket. The man's son owned a company — and he was offering Youssef a job with twice the salary.", "بعد أسبوع، جه جواب للسوبر ماركت. ابن الراجل كان عنده شركة — وكان بيعرض على يوسف شغلانة بضعف المرتب."], ["Youssef smiled. He hadn't done the right thing for a reward, but apparently, honesty does tend to come back to you.", "يوسف ابتسم. معملش الصح عشان مكافأة، بس على ما يبدو، الأمانة فعلًا بترجعلك."]], "quiz": [{"q": "What did the old man forget?", "o": ["a brown envelope with money", "his phone", "his shopping"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What was the money for?", "o": ["his granddaughter's operation", "a new car", "rent"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What did Youssef's colleague suggest?", "o": ["keeping the money", "calling the police", "giving it to the manager"], "a": 0}, {"q": "How did Youssef find the man?", "o": ["He checked the CCTV.", "He followed him home.", "He called his family."], "a": 0}, {"q": "What happened a week later?", "o": ["The man's son offered Youssef a better job.", "Youssef lost his job.", "The man came back angry."], "a": 0}]}, "challenge": {"title": "What Would You Do?", "ar": "تعمل إيه؟ — جاوب وسجّل", "qs": ["Describe a time you had to choose between two difficult options.", "Is it ever right to break the law? Give an example.", "Would you lie to protect a friend? Why or why not?", "Should AI be allowed in schools and universities?", "Is it ethical for companies to collect our data to show us ads?", "Would you take a well-paid job at a company you think is unethical?", "Answer the trolley problem: would you pull the lever? Explain using hedging language.", "Is it fair that some people earn millions while others are poor?", "What is one principle you would never break?", "Is honesty always the best policy?"]}, "games": {"pairs": [["⚖️", "ethics"], ["🧭", "conscience"], ["🤝", "integrity"], ["🌗", "grey area"], ["🙈", "cheat"], ["🎯", "principle"]], "spell": [["✅", "ethical"], ["❌", "unethical"], ["💬", "honesty"], ["😔", "guilty"], ["🔍", "consequences"], ["👍", "justify"], ["🤷", "controversial"], ["🧩", "complex"]], "speed": [["It could be argued that this is unfair.", true], ["People tend agreeing with him.", false], ["It seems that most people agree.", true], ["He appears to be telling the truth.", true], ["Apparent, the rules will change.", false], ["This might be the best solution.", true], ["It is often said that time is money.", true], ["She tends to helps others.", false], ["It is arguably the hardest question.", true], ["It seems me that he is right.", false], ["Integrity means being honest and having strong principles.", true], ["A moral dilemma has one easy answer.", false], ["\"Turn a blind eye\" means to ignore something wrong.", true], ["\"Own up to\" means to admit a mistake.", true], ["\"Red flag\" means a good sign.", false], ["\"Let someone down\" means to disappoint them.", true]]}, "test": {"pass": 60, "sections": [{"id": "voc", "title": "Vocabulary", "ar": "المفردات", "icon": "📚", "qs": [{"q": "The inner voice that tells you right from wrong = your ___.", "o": ["conscience", "principle", "society"], "a": 0, "pic": "🧭"}, {"q": "A situation where every choice has a problem = a moral ___.", "o": ["dilemma", "ethics", "grey"], "a": 0, "pic": "🤔"}, {"q": "Being honest and having strong principles = ___.", "o": ["integrity", "cheating", "consequences"], "a": 0, "pic": "🤝"}, {"q": "Something not clearly right or wrong = a grey ___.", "o": ["area", "zone", "line"], "a": 0, "pic": "🌗"}, {"q": "Causing a lot of disagreement = ___.", "o": ["controversial", "reasonable", "fair"], "a": 0, "pic": "🤷"}, {"q": "\"ضمير\" in English is…", "o": ["conscience", "conscious", "consequence"], "a": 0, "say": "Choose the correct word."}]}, {"id": "gra", "title": "Grammar", "ar": "القواعد", "icon": "📘", "qs": [{"q": "It could be ___ that the test was too difficult.", "o": ["argued", "argue", "arguing"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Teenagers ___ to sleep later than adults.", "o": ["tend", "tends", "seem that"], "a": 0}, {"q": "It ___ that the plan has failed.", "o": ["appears", "appears to", "tends"], "a": 0}, {"q": "___, the new law starts next month.", "o": ["Apparently", "Apparent", "Appear"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Which is the softest?", "o": ["This may cause some problems.", "This causes problems.", "This will definitely cause problems."], "a": 0}, {"q": "Which is correct?", "o": ["She seems to be happy.", "She seems be happy.", "She seems that happy."], "a": 0}]}, {"id": "con", "title": "Conversation", "ar": "المحادثة", "icon": "💬", "qs": [{"q": "\"Should I tell the teacher?\" — Best answer:", "o": ["It might be better to talk to your friend first.", "Teacher is a job.", "Yes, I tell."], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"Is using AI cheating?\" — Best answer:", "o": ["It could be argued that it depends on how you use it.", "AI is a computer.", "Yes, it is AI."], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"He saw the mistake but said nothing.\" — Best answer:", "o": ["So he turned a blind eye.", "So he has blind eyes.", "So he is a doctor."], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"I broke your phone. I'm sorry.\" — Best answer:", "o": ["Thanks for owning up to it.", "Own up the phone.", "Let me down."], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"She asked me to lie for her.\" — Best answer:", "o": ["That's a red flag.", "Red is a colour.", "Big flag!"], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"What's your opinion?\" — Best answer:", "o": ["It seems to me that both sides have a point.", "My opinion is a noun.", "I seems happy."], "a": 0}]}, {"id": "rea", "title": "Reading", "ar": "القراءة", "icon": "📖", "passage": ["A recent survey asked 2,000 students whether using AI to write homework is cheating.", "It appears that opinions are divided. About 40% said it is cheating, while 35% said it depends on the situation.", "Younger students tended to be more relaxed about AI than university students.", "Many teachers argue that AI could be a useful tool, provided that students do the thinking themselves.", "It could be argued that schools should teach students how to use AI ethically, rather than simply banning it."], "qs": [{"q": "How many students were asked?", "o": ["2,000", "200", "20,000"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What percentage said it is cheating?", "o": ["about 40%", "about 90%", "about 10%"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Who tended to be more relaxed about AI?", "o": ["younger students", "university students", "teachers"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What do many teachers argue?", "o": ["AI could be a useful tool if students do the thinking.", "AI should be banned forever.", "AI is always cheating."], "a": 0}, {"q": "What could schools do, according to the text?", "o": ["teach students to use AI ethically", "stop homework", "buy more computers"], "a": 0}]}, {"id": "wri", "title": "Writing", "ar": "الكتابة", "icon": "✍️", "writing": true, "prompt": "Write an opinion paragraph (80–120 words): \"Is it ever acceptable to lie?\" Use at least three hedging expressions (it could be argued, tend to, seem, may, arguably…).", "promptAr": "اكتب فقرة رأي (٨٠–١٢٠ كلمة): \"الكدب ممكن يكون مقبول؟\" استخدم ٣ تعبيرات تحفظ على الأقل.", "checks": [["⚖️", "Ethics words", "x", "\\b(lie|lying|lies|honest|honesty|truth|ethical|wrong|right|moral|fair|unfair|conscience)\\b"], ["🌫️", "Hedging", "x", "\\b(it could be argued|tends? to|seems?|appears?|arguably|apparently|may|might|probably|likely)\\b"], ["🔁", "Contrast", "x", "\\b(however|on the other hand|although|whereas|nevertheless)\\b"], ["💬", "At least 70 words", "len70"]]}]}, "watch": [{"yt": "AfNSMykrG1I", "title": "Would You Pay More for 'Ethical' Coffee?", "ar": "تدفع أكتر في قهوة \"أخلاقية\"؟ — 6 Minute English", "by": "BBC Learning English", "lines": [["Dan asks Catherine how she likes her coffee in the morning. He drinks instant coffee with a dash of milk.", "دان بيسأل كاثرين بتحب قهوتها إزاي الصبح. هو بيشرب قهوة سريعة التحضير مع شوية لبن صغيرين."], ["Catherine prefers strong coffee made from freshly ground beans, so Dan calls her a coffee aficionado.", "كاثرين بتفضل القهوة التقيلة من بن مطحون طازة، فدان بيسميها عاشقة قهوة."], ["The quiz: kopi luwak, one of the most expensive coffees, is made from beans that pass through an animal. Which animal?", "السؤال: قهوة كوبي لواك، من أغلى أنواع القهوة، بتتعمل من بن بيعدي جوه حيوان. أنهي حيوان؟"], ["Catherine says she prefers quality and will pay a little more for good coffee instead of buying something as cheap as chips.", "كاثرين بتقول إنها بتفضل الجودة وهتدفع شوية زيادة في قهوة حلوة بدل ما تشتري حاجة رخيصة جدًا."], ["She would even pay more so that farmers get a fairer price, because she thinks that matters.", "وكمان مستعدة تدفع أكتر عشان المزارعين ياخدوا سعر أعدل، لأنها شايفة إن ده مهم."], ["Many customers in Western cafés are now happy to pay more for coffee that is produced in an ethical way.", "زباين كتير في كافيهات الغرب بقوا مبسوطين يدفعوا أكتر في قهوة متنتجة بطريقة أخلاقية."], ["Ethical means morally right — treating people and the planet fairly.", "Ethical يعني صح أخلاقيًا — إنك تعامل الناس والكوكب بعدل."], ["A UN report found that better processing, branding and marketing have changed life for coffee farmers and their communities.", "تقرير للأمم المتحدة لقى إن التصنيع والبراندنج والتسويق الأحسن غيّروا حياة مزارعين البن ومجتمعاتهم."], ["Green coffee beans are cheap until they are roasted, so the companies that roast them usually take most of the profit.", "حبوب البن الخضرا رخيصة لحد ما تتحمص، فالشركات اللي بتحمصها غالبًا بتاخد أغلب الربح."], ["But when customers buy premium coffee, the price paid to the farmer goes up too — about three and a half times as much.", "بس لما الزباين يشتروا قهوة بريميوم، السعر اللي بياخده المزارع بيزيد هو كمان — حوالي ٣ مرات ونص."], ["Higher incomes mean a better quality of life for farmers, their families and their communities.", "دخل أعلى يعني جودة حياة أحسن للمزارعين وعيلاتهم ومجتمعاتهم."], ["The answer to the quiz is a weasel! Catherine says she will look for ethical coffee from now on.", "إجابة السؤال هي ابن عرس! وكاثرين بتقول إنها هتدور على قهوة أخلاقية من دلوقتي."]], "words": ["dash", "aficionado", "expensive", "as cheap as chips", "quality", "fairer price", "ethical", "morally right", "marketing", "roasted", "premium", "quality of life"], "quiz": [{"q": "How does Dan take his coffee?", "o": ["instant, with a dash of milk", "strong and black", "with lots of sugar"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What is an \"aficionado\"?", "o": ["someone very enthusiastic about a subject", "a coffee farmer", "a cheap coffee"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Why would Catherine pay more?", "o": ["so farmers get a fairer price", "because she is rich", "because coffee is cheap"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Who usually takes most of the profit?", "o": ["the companies that roast the beans", "the farmers", "the cafés"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What happens when customers buy premium coffee?", "o": ["Farmers earn about three and a half times as much.", "Farmers earn less.", "Nothing changes."], "a": 0}, {"q": "Which animal is the quiz answer?", "o": ["a weasel", "a cat", "an elephant"], "a": 0}]}]}, "2": {"n": 2, "title": "Globalization", "ar": "العولمة — Nominalisation", "icon": "🌐", "cover": "img/b2p/u2.jpg", "intro": "اتكلم عن العولمة: التجارة والشركات العالمية والثقافة والسفر وتأثيرها على البلاد المحلية، واتعلم الـ Nominalisation — إزاي تحوّل الأفعال لأسماء عشان كتابتك تبقى رسمية وأكاديمية.", "videos": [{"id": "b2pv2", "title": "The Same Everywhere", "ar": "نفس الحاجة في كل حتة — نور وكريم", "src": "video/b2p/u2v1.mp4", "poster": "img/b2p/u2v1.jpg", "sp": {"a": {"n": "Nour", "g": "f"}, "b": {"n": "Karim", "g": "m"}}, "lines": [["b", "Nour, you just came back from your trip to Asia. How was it?", "نور، إنتي لسه راجعة من رحلتك لآسيا. كانت عاملة إيه؟"], ["a", "Amazing, but strange in a way. Every city had the same coffee chains, the same clothes shops, even the same songs!", "تحفة، بس غريبة شوية. كل مدينة كان فيها نفس سلاسل القهوة، ونفس محلات اللبس، وحتى نفس الأغاني!"], ["b", "That's globalization for you. The growth of international companies has made the world more connected.", "دي العولمة. نمو الشركات العالمية خلى العالم مترابط أكتر."], ["a", "True. And the expansion of the internet means we all watch the same series and follow the same trends.", "صح. وانتشار الإنترنت معناه إننا كلنا بنتفرج على نفس المسلسلات ونتابع نفس الترندات."], ["b", "There are real benefits, though. The reduction in trade barriers has made products cheaper for everyone.", "بس في فوايد حقيقية. تقليل حواجز التجارة خلى المنتجات أرخص للكل."], ["a", "Maybe, but at what cost? The disappearance of small local shops really worries me.", "يمكن، بس بأي تمن؟ اختفاء المحلات المحلية الصغيرة ده بجد بيقلقني."], ["b", "I understand. My uncle's tailor shop closed last year. People prefer cheap fast fashion now.", "فاهم. محل الخياطة بتاع خالي قفل السنة اللي فاتت. الناس بقت بتفضل الموضة السريعة الرخيصة."], ["a", "Exactly. And the production of those cheap clothes often depends on very low wages in poorer countries.", "بالظبط. وإنتاج اللبس الرخيص ده غالبًا بيعتمد على أجور قليلة جدًا في دول أفقر."], ["b", "On the other hand, globalization created millions of jobs in those countries. It's complicated.", "من ناحية تانية، العولمة عملت ملايين وظايف في الدول دي. الموضوع معقد."], ["a", "It is. I think the solution is a balance — the protection of local culture alongside global trade.", "فعلًا. أنا شايفة إن الحل توازن — حماية الثقافة المحلية جنب التجارة العالمية."], ["b", "Agreed. Starting today, I'm buying my coffee from the small café on our street!", "موافق. من النهارده، هشتري قهوتي من الكافيه الصغير اللي في شارعنا!"], ["a", "Ha! That's a small step for globalization, but a big one for the café owner!", "هههه! خطوة صغيرة للعولمة، بس كبيرة لصاحب الكافيه!"]], "quiz": [{"q": "What surprised Nour on her trip?", "o": ["Every city had the same chains and shops.", "There was no internet.", "Everything was very expensive."], "a": 0}, {"q": "What has made products cheaper, according to Karim?", "o": ["the reduction in trade barriers", "local shops", "higher wages"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What worries Nour?", "o": ["the disappearance of small local shops", "travelling too much", "learning languages"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What happened to Karim's uncle's shop?", "o": ["It closed last year.", "It became famous.", "It moved to Asia."], "a": 0}, {"q": "What solution does Nour suggest?", "o": ["a balance between local culture and global trade", "stopping all trade", "closing big companies"], "a": 0}], "fill": [[1, "coffee chains"], [2, "globalization"], [2, "growth"], [3, "expansion"], [3, "trends"], [4, "reduction"], [4, "trade barriers"], [5, "disappearance"], [6, "fast fashion"], [7, "production"], [7, "wages"], [9, "protection"]]}], "vocab": [{"t": "The global economy", "ar": "الاقتصاد العالمي", "items": [["🌐", "globalization", "Globalization has connected the world."], ["🏭", "multinational", "Multinational companies operate in many countries."], ["🚢", "trade", "International trade has increased."], ["📦", "import", "Egypt imports wheat from many countries."], ["📤", "export", "China exports electronics worldwide."], ["💵", "wages", "Workers demand higher wages."], ["🧱", "trade barrier", "Removing trade barriers lowers prices."], ["🔗", "supply chain", "The pandemic broke many supply chains."]]}, {"t": "Culture & society", "ar": "الثقافة والمجتمع", "items": [["🍔", "chain", "Fast-food chains are everywhere."], ["🏪", "local business", "Support your local businesses."], ["🎭", "cultural identity", "Globalization may threaten cultural identity."], ["🧬", "diversity", "Big cities celebrate cultural diversity."], ["🔄", "influence", "American films influence young people worldwide."], ["🌍", "worldwide", "The song became popular worldwide."], ["🧳", "migration", "Migration has changed many cities."], ["🗣️", "lingua franca", "English is the lingua franca of business."]]}, {"t": "Effects", "ar": "التأثيرات", "items": [["📈", "benefit", "Cheaper products are one benefit."], ["📉", "drawback", "The main drawback is pollution."], ["⚖️", "inequality", "Globalization can increase inequality."], ["🏭", "exploitation", "The exploitation of workers is a serious issue."], ["🌱", "sustainable", "We need more sustainable production."], ["👕", "fast fashion", "Fast fashion creates a lot of waste."], ["🤝", "interconnected", "The world is more interconnected than ever."], ["🔀", "homogenisation", "Some fear the homogenisation of culture."]]}], "talk": [{"title": "Let's Talk · Student A", "ar": "الطالب A", "list": [["How many products around you were made in other countries?", "كام منتج حواليك اتعمل في بلاد تانية؟", "Almost everything — my phone, my shoes, even my pen!"], ["Is globalization good for your country?", "العولمة كويسة لبلدك؟", "In some ways yes, in others no."], ["Do you prefer international brands or local ones?", "بتفضل البراندات العالمية ولا المحلية؟", "Local food, international technology."], ["Is your culture changing because of globalization?", "ثقافتك بتتغير بسبب العولمة؟", "Yes, especially how young people dress and talk."], ["Should English be the world's common language?", "الإنجليزي لازم يبقى لغة العالم المشتركة؟", "It already is, but we should protect our own languages."]]}, {"title": "Let's Talk · Student B", "ar": "الطالب B", "list": [["Who benefits most from globalization?", "مين أكتر واحد بيستفيد من العولمة؟", "Big companies, mostly."], ["Would you work for a multinational company? Why?", "تشتغل في شركة متعددة الجنسيات؟", "Yes, for the experience and travel."], ["How can we protect local businesses?", "إزاي نحمي المحلات المحلية؟", "By buying from them and promoting them online."], ["Is fast fashion a problem? Why?", "الموضة السريعة مشكلة؟ ليه؟", "Yes, because of waste and low wages."], ["Will the world become one single culture in the future?", "العالم هيبقى ثقافة واحدة في المستقبل؟", "I hope not. Diversity is beautiful."]]}], "grammar": {"title": "Nominalisation", "ar": "تحويل الأفعال والصفات لأسماء — الأسلوب الرسمي", "blocks": [{"type": "intro", "en": "Nominalisation means turning verbs and adjectives into nouns. It makes writing more formal, more concise and more academic — perfect for essays, reports and presentations.", "ar": "الـ Nominalisation يعني إنك تحوّل الأفعال والصفات لأسماء. ده بيخلي الكتابة رسمية أكتر ومختصرة وأكاديمية — ممتاز للمقالات والتقارير والعروض."}, {"type": "big", "items": [{"v": "verb → noun", "p": "grow → growth", "c": 1, "eg": ["Companies grew quickly. → The rapid growth of companies…", "Prices were reduced. → The reduction in prices…", "Small shops disappeared. → The disappearance of small shops…"]}, {"v": "adjective → noun", "p": "important → importance", "c": 2, "eg": ["Local culture is important. → The importance of local culture…", "People are unequal. → Inequality…", "Products are available everywhere. → The availability of products…"]}]}, {"type": "table", "title": "🔤 Common noun endings", "head": ["Ending", "Examples"], "rows": [["-tion / -sion", "produce → production · expand → expansion · decide → decision"], ["-ment", "develop → development · improve → improvement · invest → investment"], ["-ance / -ence", "important → importance · depend → dependence · differ → difference"], ["-ity", "equal → equality · available → availability · diverse → diversity"], ["-th / -al / -ure", "grow → growth · arrive → arrival · fail → failure"]]}, {"type": "table", "title": "✍️ Everyday → formal", "head": ["Everyday English", "Nominalised (formal)"], "rows": [["Because prices went up, people bought less.", "The increase in prices led to a decrease in sales."], ["The government decided to cut taxes.", "The government's decision to cut taxes…"], ["When companies expanded, they created jobs.", "The expansion of companies created jobs."], ["We need to protect local culture.", "The protection of local culture is essential."]]}, {"type": "tip", "en": "Use 'of' after the noun: the growth OF trade, the protection OF culture. Don't overuse nominalisation in speaking — it can sound heavy. It's best for writing.", "ar": "استخدم of بعد الاسم: the growth of trade. ومتكترش منها في الكلام العادي — بتبقى تقيلة. أحسن استخدامها في الكتابة."}]}, "exercises": [{"type": "mcq", "title": "Nominalisation — 10 MCQs", "ar": "اختار الصح", "speak": true, "items": [{"q": "grow → the ___ of international trade", "o": ["growth", "growing", "grown", "grew"], "a": 0}, {"q": "reduce → a ___ in prices", "o": ["reduction", "reducement", "reducing", "reduce"], "a": 0}, {"q": "disappear → the ___ of local shops", "o": ["disappearance", "disappearing", "disappearment", "disappeared"], "a": 0}, {"q": "expand → the ___ of the internet", "o": ["expansion", "expandment", "expanding", "expandation"], "a": 0}, {"q": "important → the ___ of education", "o": ["importance", "importancy", "importment", "importation"], "a": 0}, {"q": "equal → gender ___", "o": ["equality", "equalness", "equalment", "equalance"], "a": 0}, {"q": "develop → economic ___", "o": ["development", "developation", "developance", "developing"], "a": 0}, {"q": "decide → the government's ___", "o": ["decision", "decidement", "deciding", "decidance"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Which sentence is nominalised (formal)?", "o": ["The increase in prices led to a fall in sales.", "Prices went up, so people bought less.", "People bought less because things were expensive.", "Prices increase and sales falling."], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"The protection ___ local culture is essential.\"", "o": ["of", "for", "about", "to"], "a": 0}]}, {"type": "mcq", "title": "Find the noun", "ar": "هات الاسم", "items": [{"q": "produce → ___", "o": ["production", "producement"], "a": 0}, {"q": "improve → ___", "o": ["improvement", "improvation"], "a": 0}, {"q": "available → ___", "o": ["availability", "availableness"], "a": 0}, {"q": "depend → ___", "o": ["dependence", "dependment"], "a": 0}, {"q": "arrive → ___", "o": ["arrival", "arrivation"], "a": 0}]}, {"type": "ord", "title": "Make formal sentences", "ar": "رتّب الكلمات", "items": [{"c": ["The growth", "of trade", "has created", "millions of jobs"], "a": [0, 1, 2, 3]}, {"c": ["The disappearance", "of local shops", "is", "a serious problem"], "a": [0, 1, 2, 3]}, {"c": ["The protection", "of culture", "is", "essential"], "a": [0, 1, 2, 3]}, {"c": ["A reduction", "in prices", "led to", "higher sales"], "a": [0, 1, 2, 3]}]}], "reading": {"title": "A Smaller World", "ar": "عالم أصغر", "g": "f", "lines": [["In the past, a cup of coffee, a T-shirt and a smartphone would have had very little in common. Today, all three are likely to be the result of a global journey.", "زمان، فنجان القهوة والتيشيرت والموبايل مكانش بينهم حاجة مشتركة تقريبًا. النهارده، التلاتة غالبًا نتيجة رحلة عالمية."], ["The beans in your coffee may come from Ethiopia, the cotton in your shirt from India, and the parts of your phone from a dozen different countries.", "البن اللي في قهوتك ممكن يكون من إثيوبيا، والقطن اللي في قميصك من الهند، وقطع موبايلك من دستة دول مختلفة."], ["This interconnection is known as globalization: the increasing movement of goods, money, people and ideas across borders.", "الترابط ده اسمه العولمة: الحركة المتزايدة للبضايع والفلوس والناس والأفكار عبر الحدود."], ["Supporters point to its many benefits. The expansion of trade has lifted millions of people out of poverty, particularly in Asia.", "المؤيدين بيشاوروا على فوايدها الكتير. توسع التجارة طلّع ملايين الناس من الفقر، خصوصًا في آسيا."], ["The availability of cheaper products has improved living standards, and the exchange of ideas has accelerated scientific progress.", "توفر منتجات أرخص حسّن مستوى المعيشة، وتبادل الأفكار سرّع التقدم العلمي."], ["Critics, however, highlight the drawbacks. The relocation of factories to countries with lower wages has led to job losses in some regions.", "لكن المنتقدين بيركزوا على العيوب. نقل المصانع لدول أجورها أقل أدى لفقدان وظايف في بعض المناطق."], ["There are also concerns about the exploitation of workers and the environmental impact of transporting goods around the world.", "وفي كمان قلق من استغلال العمال والأثر البيئي لنقل البضايع حوالين العالم."], ["Perhaps the most emotional debate concerns culture. Some fear the homogenisation of the world, where every high street looks the same.", "ويمكن أكتر نقاش عاطفي هو عن الثقافة. في ناس خايفين إن العالم يبقى نسخة واحدة، كل شارع شكله زي التاني."], ["Others argue that globalization has, in fact, encouraged the spread of local cultures — think of the worldwide popularity of K-pop or Egyptian cuisine.", "وغيرهم بيقولوا إن العولمة في الحقيقة شجعت انتشار الثقافات المحلية — فكّر في شعبية الكيبوب أو الأكل المصري حوالين العالم."], ["The challenge for the future is not to stop globalization, but to manage it in a way that is fair, sustainable and respectful of diversity.", "التحدي في المستقبل مش إننا نوقف العولمة، لكن إننا نديرها بطريقة عادلة ومستدامة وبتحترم التنوع."]], "keys": [["🔗", "interconnection", "a connection between many parts"], ["🧱", "border", "the line between two countries"], ["🚀", "accelerate", "to make something happen faster"], ["🏭", "relocation", "moving something to a new place"], ["🔀", "homogenisation", "making things the same"], ["🍲", "cuisine", "a style of cooking"]], "quiz": [{"q": "What is globalization, according to the text?", "o": ["the movement of goods, money, people and ideas across borders", "a type of coffee", "a new phone"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What is one benefit mentioned?", "o": ["Millions of people have been lifted out of poverty.", "Everyone earns the same.", "Prices are higher."], "a": 0}, {"q": "What has the relocation of factories led to?", "o": ["job losses in some regions", "more jobs everywhere", "cleaner air"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What do some people fear about culture?", "o": ["that every high street will look the same", "that K-pop will disappear", "that people will stop travelling"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Which examples show local cultures spreading?", "o": ["K-pop and Egyptian cuisine", "coffee and T-shirts", "phones and factories"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What is the challenge for the future?", "o": ["to manage globalization fairly and sustainably", "to stop globalization", "to close all borders"], "a": 0}]}, "idioms": {"items": [["a global village", "The world seen as one small community because of technology.", "قرية صغيرة (العالم كله)", "Thanks to the internet, we live in a global village.", "بفضل الإنترنت، إحنا عايشين في قرية عالمية."], ["the tip of the iceberg", "A small visible part of a much bigger problem.", "رأس جبل الجليد", "Low wages are just the tip of the iceberg.", "الأجور القليلة دي مجرد رأس جبل الجليد."], ["a level playing field", "A fair situation where everyone has the same chances.", "فرص متساوية للكل", "Small shops need a level playing field to compete with big chains.", "المحلات الصغيرة محتاجة فرص متساوية عشان تنافس السلاسل الكبيرة."], ["think outside the box", "To think in a creative, new way.", "يفكر برة الصندوق", "Local businesses must think outside the box to survive.", "المحلات المحلية لازم تفكر برة الصندوق عشان تعيش."]], "quiz": [{"q": "The pollution we can see is only ___. The real problem is much bigger.", "o": ["the tip of the iceberg", "a global village", "a level playing field", "outside the box"], "a": 0}, {"q": "With video calls, the world has become ___.", "o": ["a global village", "the tip of the iceberg", "a playing field", "a box"], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"A level playing field\" means…", "o": ["a fair situation for everyone", "a football pitch", "a flat garden", "an easy game"], "a": 0}, {"q": "To find new solutions, we need to ___.", "o": ["think outside the box", "level the field", "tip the iceberg", "build a village"], "a": 0}]}, "phrasal": {"items": [["take over", "To get control of a company or a place.", "يستحوذ على / يسيطر على", "A big chain took over the small café.", "سلسلة كبيرة استحوذت على الكافيه الصغير."], ["shut down", "To close a business permanently.", "يقفل نهائيًا", "Many factories shut down after the crisis.", "مصانع كتير قفلت نهائيًا بعد الأزمة."], ["catch on", "To become popular.", "ينتشر / يبقى موضة", "The trend caught on all over the world.", "الترند انتشر في العالم كله."], ["phase out", "To stop using something gradually.", "يلغي تدريجيًا", "The country is phasing out plastic bags.", "البلد بتلغي الأكياس البلاستيك تدريجيًا."]], "quiz": [{"q": "The company plans to ___ the old models by 2030.", "o": ["phase out", "catch on", "take over", "shut down"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Bubble tea ___ quickly in Cairo.", "o": ["caught on", "phased out", "took over", "shut down"], "a": 0}, {"q": "The old cinema ___ last year because nobody came.", "o": ["shut down", "caught on", "phased out", "took over"], "a": 0}, {"q": "An international company ___ the local brand.", "o": ["took over", "caught on", "phased out", "shut down"], "a": 0}]}, "slang": {"items": [["basic", "Ordinary, mainstream, not original.", "عادي جدًا / مالوش طعم", "Same coffee chain in every city? That's so basic.", "نفس سلسلة القهوة في كل مدينة؟ ده عادي جدًا.", "بهزار — ممكن تبقى قلة ذوق لو قلتها على شخص"], ["mid", "Average, not very good.", "متوسط / مش قد كده", "The new burger place is mid, honestly.", "محل البرجر الجديد بصراحة مش قد كده.", "سلانج حديث"], ["hidden gem", "A great place that few people know about.", "مكان حلو مستخبي", "This little local restaurant is a hidden gem.", "المطعم المحلي الصغير ده جوهرة مستخبية.", "إيجابي جدًا"], ["go global", "To become known all over the world.", "يوصل للعالمية", "Egyptian food is going global!", "الأكل المصري بيوصل للعالمية!", "عادي"], ["FOMO", "Fear Of Missing Out.", "الخوف إن حاجة تفوتك", "Everyone was buying the new phone, so I got FOMO.", "كل الناس كانت بتشتري الموبايل الجديد، فخفت يفوتني.", "منتشرة جدًا"]], "quiz": [{"q": "A great place that few people know = a ___.", "o": ["hidden gem", "mid", "basic", "FOMO"], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"The film was mid.\" means it was…", "o": ["average, not very good", "in the middle of the city", "excellent", "very long"], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"FOMO\" stands for…", "o": ["Fear Of Missing Out", "Friends Of My Office", "Free Online Music Offer", "Fast Order Mobile Option"], "a": 0}, {"q": "When a local brand becomes famous worldwide, it ___.", "o": ["goes global", "gets basic", "is mid", "has FOMO"], "a": 0}]}, "story": {"title": "Grandma's Recipe Goes Global", "ar": "وصفة تيتة بقت عالمية", "g": "m", "lines": [["When the big supermarket chain opened in their neighbourhood, Salma's family bakery started to struggle.", "لما سلسلة السوبر ماركت الكبيرة فتحت في حيهم، مخبز عيلة سلمى بدأ يعاني."], ["People preferred the cheap, packaged bread from the supermarket. Every month, sales fell.", "الناس فضّلت العيش المغلّف الرخيص من السوبر ماركت. كل شهر، المبيعات كانت بتقل."], ["\"We might have to shut down,\" her father said sadly one evening.", "\"ممكن نضطر نقفل،\" أبوها قال بحزن في ليلة."], ["Salma, a computer science student, decided to think outside the box. She filmed her grandmother making her famous date pastries.", "سلمى، طالبة علوم حاسب، قررت تفكر برة الصندوق. صوّرت تيتها وهي بتعمل الكحك بالعجوة المشهور بتاعها."], ["Grandma explained every step in Arabic, and Salma added English subtitles.", "تيتة شرحت كل خطوة بالعربي، وسلمى ضافت ترجمة إنجليزي."], ["The video caught on immediately. Within a week, it had been watched by people in forty countries.", "الفيديو انتشر على طول. في خلال أسبوع، اتشاف من ناس في ٤٠ دولة."], ["Messages arrived from Canada, Malaysia and Brazil: \"Can you ship them to us?\"", "رسايل جت من كندا وماليزيا والبرازيل: \"ممكن تشحنوها لينا؟\""], ["With the help of an online platform, the small bakery started exporting boxes of pastries around the world.", "بمساعدة منصة أونلاين، المخبز الصغير بدأ يصدّر علب حلويات حوالين العالم."], ["Ironically, the same globalization that had nearly destroyed their business was now its greatest opportunity.", "والمفارقة إن نفس العولمة اللي كانت قربت تدمّر شغلهم بقت دلوقتي أكبر فرصة ليهم."], ["Today, Grandma has more followers than the supermarket — and she still refuses to share her secret ingredient.", "النهارده، تيتة عندها متابعين أكتر من السوبر ماركت — ولسه رافضة تقول المكون السري بتاعها."]], "quiz": [{"q": "Why did the bakery start to struggle?", "o": ["A big supermarket chain opened nearby.", "The oven broke.", "Grandma got sick."], "a": 0}, {"q": "What did Salma film?", "o": ["her grandmother making pastries", "the supermarket", "her university"], "a": 0}, {"q": "How many countries watched the video within a week?", "o": ["forty", "four", "four hundred"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What did people from other countries ask?", "o": ["if the pastries could be shipped to them", "for the secret ingredient", "for a job"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What is ironic in the story?", "o": ["Globalization nearly destroyed the bakery but then saved it.", "Grandma hates baking.", "The supermarket closed."], "a": 0}]}, "challenge": {"title": "One World, Many Cultures", "ar": "عالم واحد وثقافات كتير — جاوب وسجّل", "qs": ["Describe how globalization has changed your city in the last ten years.", "Is it better to buy local or international products? Why?", "What part of your culture would you like the world to know about?", "Should governments protect local businesses from big chains?", "What are the advantages and disadvantages of fast fashion?", "Use nominalisation to describe a problem in your country (e.g. the increase in…, the lack of…).", "Would you like to live in another country? Why or why not?", "Will English remain the global language in 50 years?", "Describe a local \"hidden gem\" in your area.", "How can young people protect their cultural identity in a global world?"]}, "games": {"pairs": [["🌐", "globalization"], ["🚢", "trade"], ["💵", "wages"], ["🧱", "trade barrier"], ["🔗", "supply chain"], ["🧬", "diversity"]], "spell": [["🏭", "multinational"], ["📦", "import"], ["📤", "export"], ["📉", "drawback"], ["⚖️", "inequality"], ["🌱", "sustainable"], ["🔄", "influence"], ["🌍", "worldwide"]], "speed": [["the growth of trade", true], ["the grow of trade", false], ["a reduction in prices", true], ["the disappearance of local shops", true], ["the importancy of culture", false], ["gender equality", true], ["economic development", true], ["the decidement of the government", false], ["the expansion of the internet", true], ["the protection for local culture", false], ["Globalization connects countries through trade and ideas.", true], ["To export means to buy from other countries.", false], ["\"The tip of the iceberg\" means a small part of a big problem.", true], ["\"Catch on\" means to become popular.", true], ["\"Shut down\" means to open a new shop.", false], ["A \"hidden gem\" is a great place few people know.", true]]}, "test": {"pass": 60, "sections": [{"id": "voc", "title": "Vocabulary", "ar": "المفردات", "icon": "📚", "qs": [{"q": "A company that works in many countries = a ___ company.", "o": ["multinational", "local", "sustainable"], "a": 0, "pic": "🏭"}, {"q": "Money paid to workers = ___.", "o": ["wages", "trade", "imports"], "a": 0, "pic": "💵"}, {"q": "To sell goods to other countries = to ___.", "o": ["export", "import", "influence"], "a": 0, "pic": "📤"}, {"q": "A disadvantage = a ___.", "o": ["drawback", "benefit", "chain"], "a": 0, "pic": "📉"}, {"q": "Many different cultures together = ___.", "o": ["diversity", "inequality", "migration"], "a": 0, "pic": "🧬"}, {"q": "\"العولمة\" in English is…", "o": ["globalization", "generalization", "globe"], "a": 0, "say": "Choose the correct word."}]}, {"id": "gra", "title": "Grammar", "ar": "القواعد", "icon": "📘", "qs": [{"q": "The rapid ___ of the city surprised everyone. (grow)", "o": ["growth", "growing", "grown"], "a": 0}, {"q": "There has been a ___ in unemployment. (reduce)", "o": ["reduction", "reducing", "reducement"], "a": 0}, {"q": "The ___ of clean water is a big problem. (available → lack of…)", "o": ["availability", "available", "availableness"], "a": 0}, {"q": "The government's ___ surprised the public. (decide)", "o": ["decision", "decidement", "deciding"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Economic ___ needs investment. (develop)", "o": ["development", "developance", "developation"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Which is the most formal?", "o": ["The increase in prices caused a fall in demand.", "Prices went up so people bought less.", "People bought less because stuff was expensive."], "a": 0}]}, {"id": "con", "title": "Conversation", "ar": "المحادثة", "icon": "💬", "qs": [{"q": "\"Every city has the same shops now.\" — Best answer:", "o": ["That's globalization. It has pros and cons.", "Shops are buildings.", "Same is same."], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"Is globalization good or bad?\" — Best answer:", "o": ["It's complicated. It created jobs but hurt some local businesses.", "It is a globe.", "Yes, it is."], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"This café is a hidden gem!\" — Best answer:", "o": ["I know! Not many people know about it.", "Where is the gem?", "Hide it!"], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"Low wages are the tip of the iceberg.\" — Best answer:", "o": ["Right, the real problem is much bigger.", "Is it cold?", "Icebergs are big."], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"Should we buy local?\" — Best answer:", "o": ["When possible, yes. It supports small businesses.", "Local is a place.", "I buy."], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"The new restaurant was mid.\" — Best answer:", "o": ["Oh, so it was just average?", "It was in the middle?", "Great, five stars!"], "a": 0}]}, {"id": "rea", "title": "Reading", "ar": "القراءة", "icon": "📖", "passage": ["Ten years ago, there were twenty small clothes shops on Hassan's street. Today, only three remain.", "The arrival of a huge international chain led to a dramatic fall in their sales.", "However, the remaining shops have found a solution: the production of high-quality, handmade clothes that the chain cannot offer.", "Their success shows the importance of creativity in a global economy.", "Many young customers now prefer to support local designers rather than buy fast fashion."], "qs": [{"q": "How many shops are left today?", "o": ["three", "twenty", "ten"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What led to a fall in sales?", "o": ["the arrival of an international chain", "bad weather", "high taxes"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What do the remaining shops produce?", "o": ["high-quality handmade clothes", "cheap clothes", "food"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What does their success show?", "o": ["the importance of creativity", "that chains are always better", "that clothes are expensive"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What do many young customers prefer now?", "o": ["supporting local designers", "buying fast fashion", "shopping online only"], "a": 0}]}, {"id": "wri", "title": "Writing", "ar": "الكتابة", "icon": "✍️", "writing": true, "prompt": "Write a formal paragraph (80–120 words) about the effects of globalization on your country. Use at least four nominalised forms (growth, reduction, development, importance…).", "promptAr": "اكتب فقرة رسمية (٨٠–١٢٠ كلمة) عن تأثير العولمة على بلدك، واستخدم ٤ أسماء على الأقل من الـ Nominalisation.", "checks": [["🌐", "Globalization words", "x", "\\b(globalization|globalisation|global|trade|international|multinational|culture|local|economy|wages|import|export)\\b"], ["🔤", "Nominalisation", "x", "\\b\\w+(tion|sion|ment|ance|ence|ity|th)\\s+of\\b"], ["📊", "Formal linker", "x", "\\b(furthermore|moreover|however|consequently|therefore|in addition|as a result)\\b"], ["💬", "At least 70 words", "len70"]]}]}, "watch": [{"yt": "3-icphihD6Y", "title": "Could You Give Up Fast Fashion?", "ar": "تقدر تبطّل الموضة السريعة؟ — 6 Minute English", "by": "BBC Learning English", "lines": [["Georgina and Neil talk about fast fashion: buying clothes, wearing them a few times, then buying more.", "جورجينا ونيل بيتكلموا عن الموضة السريعة: تشتري لبس، تلبسه كام مرة، وبعدين تشتري تاني."], ["Fast fashion feels good, but it is blamed for contributing to global warming.", "الموضة السريعة بتبسطك، بس بيتقال إنها بتساهم في الاحتباس الحراري."], ["Some people are pledging — publicly promising — not to buy any new clothes this year.", "في ناس بيتعهدوا — بيوعدوا قدام الناس — إنهم مش هيشتروا أي لبس جديد السنة دي."], ["The quiz: how many items of clothing were sent to landfill in the UK in 2017?", "السؤال: كام قطعة لبس اترمت في مقالب الزبالة في بريطانيا سنة ٢٠١٧؟"], ["Old clothes pile up in landfill, and tiny fibres from washing our clothes end up in the sea.", "اللبس القديم بيتكوّم في المقالب، وألياف صغيرة من غسيل هدومنا بتوصل للبحر."], ["On average, a piece of clothing is worn only about seven times before it is thrown away.", "في المتوسط، قطعة اللبس بتتلبس حوالي ٧ مرات بس قبل ما تترمي."], ["A fashion journalist explains that production was outsourced to countries like Bangladesh, India and China.", "صحفية موضة بتشرح إن الإنتاج اتنقل لشركات في دول زي بنجلاديش والهند والصين."], ["Companies keep undercutting each other — charging less for the same work — so prices keep falling.", "الشركات بتكسر أسعار بعض — بتطلب أقل في نفس الشغل — فالأسعار بتفضل تنزل."], ["The habit also stems from social media: many people feel they can't be seen in the same outfit twice.", "والعادة دي كمان جاية من السوشيال ميديا: ناس كتير حاسين إنهم مينفعش يتشافوا بنفس اللبس مرتين."], ["Neil thinks buying so much and wearing it so little is wasteful and illogical.", "نيل شايف إنك تشتري كتير وتلبس قليل ده إهدار ومش منطقي."], ["Now there is a backlash: people choose second-hand or vintage clothes and mend what they already have.", "ودلوقتي في رد فعل عكسي: الناس بتختار لبس مستعمل أو فينتدج وبتصلّح اللي عندها."], ["The answer: around 234 million items went to landfill — far more than Neil guessed.", "الإجابة: حوالي ٢٣٤ مليون قطعة راحت المقالب — أكتر بكتير من تخمين نيل."]], "words": ["fast fashion", "global warming", "pledging", "landfill", "fibres", "on average", "outsourced", "undercutting", "stems from", "illogical", "backlash", "second-hand"], "quiz": [{"q": "What is fast fashion?", "o": ["buying clothes, wearing them a few times, then buying more", "making clothes by hand", "wearing the same clothes for years"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What does \"pledging\" mean?", "o": ["publicly promising", "buying cheaply", "throwing away"], "a": 0}, {"q": "How many times is a piece of clothing worn on average?", "o": ["about seven", "about seventy", "once"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Why do prices keep falling?", "o": ["Companies keep undercutting each other.", "Clothes are made by hand.", "People buy less."], "a": 0}, {"q": "What is the \"backlash\"?", "o": ["people choosing second-hand clothes and mending them", "more shopping online", "higher prices"], "a": 0}, {"q": "How many items went to UK landfill in 2017?", "o": ["around 234 million", "23 million", "2.3 billion"], "a": 0}]}]}, "3": {"n": 3, "title": "Leadership and Power", "ar": "القيادة والسلطة — Inversion for Emphasis", "icon": "👑", "cover": "img/b2p/u3.jpg", "intro": "اتكلم عن القادة الناجحين والسلطة والمسؤولية وإزاي تقود فريق، واستخدم الـ Inversion عشان تأكد على كلامك بأسلوب قوي: Never have I… / Not only… but also… / Rarely do…", "videos": [{"id": "b2pv3", "title": "The New Team Leader", "ar": "قائد الفريق الجديد — مريم ويوسف", "src": "video/b2p/u3v1.mp4", "poster": "img/b2p/u3v1.jpg", "sp": {"a": {"n": "Mariam", "g": "f"}, "b": {"n": "Youssef", "g": "m"}}, "lines": [["b", "Mariam, congratulations! I heard you were promoted to team leader.", "مريم، مبروك! سمعت إنك اترقيتي لقائدة فريق."], ["a", "Thanks, Youssef. Honestly, I'm a bit nervous. Never have I managed so many people before.", "شكرًا يا يوسف. بصراحة، متوترة شوية. عمري ما أدرت ناس كتير كده قبل كده."], ["b", "You'll be great. Not only are you experienced, but you're also really good with people.", "هتكوني ممتازة. مش بس عندك خبرة، إنتي كمان شاطرة جدًا مع الناس."], ["a", "That's kind. But what makes a good leader, in your opinion?", "ده لطف منك. بس إيه اللي بيعمل قائد كويس، في رأيك؟"], ["b", "Listening. Rarely do bad managers ask their team for ideas. Good leaders make everyone feel heard.", "الاستماع. نادرًا ما المديرين الوحشين بيسألوا فريقهم على أفكار. القادة الكويسين بيخلوا الكل يحس إن صوته مسموع."], ["a", "I agree. My old boss was the opposite. Only when something went wrong did he talk to us.", "موافقة. مديري القديم كان العكس. محدش كان بيكلمنا غير لما حاجة تبوظ."], ["b", "Exactly. Power can change people. Some leaders start well, but then they stop listening.", "بالظبط. السلطة ممكن تغير الناس. في قادة بيبدأوا كويس، بس بعدين بيبطلوا يسمعوا."], ["a", "That's my biggest fear. Under no circumstances do I want to become that kind of boss.", "ده أكبر خوف عندي. مش عايزة أبدًا أبقى النوع ده من المديرين."], ["b", "Then ask for feedback regularly. And lead by example — if you want people to work hard, you work hard first.", "يبقى اطلبي ملاحظات بانتظام. وقودي بالقدوة — لو عايزة الناس تشتغل جامد، اشتغلي إنتي جامد الأول."], ["a", "Good advice. I'll also make sure the team gets credit when things go well.", "نصيحة حلوة. وهتأكد كمان إن الفريق ياخد التقدير لما الأمور تمشي كويس."], ["b", "That's the secret! A real leader takes a little more of the blame and a little less of the credit.", "ده السر! القائد الحقيقي بياخد شوية لوم أكتر وشوية تقدير أقل."], ["a", "I'll remember that. Thanks, Youssef — seldom have I received such useful advice!", "هفتكر ده. شكرًا يا يوسف — نادرًا ما خدت نصيحة مفيدة كده!"]], "quiz": [{"q": "What happened to Mariam?", "o": ["She was promoted to team leader.", "She lost her job.", "She moved to another city."], "a": 0}, {"q": "Why is she nervous?", "o": ["She has never managed so many people.", "She hates her team.", "She is ill."], "a": 0}, {"q": "What does Youssef think makes a good leader?", "o": ["listening", "shouting", "working alone"], "a": 0}, {"q": "When did her old boss talk to the team?", "o": ["only when something went wrong", "every morning", "never"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What is \"the secret\", according to Youssef?", "o": ["taking more blame and less credit", "taking all the credit", "never giving feedback"], "a": 0}], "fill": [[0, "promoted"], [0, "team leader"], [1, "Never have I managed"], [2, "Not only"], [4, "Rarely do"], [5, "Only when"], [6, "Power"], [7, "Under no circumstances"], [8, "feedback"], [8, "lead by example"], [9, "credit"], [10, "blame"]]}], "vocab": [{"t": "Leaders", "ar": "القادة", "items": [["👑", "leader", "A good leader listens to the team."], ["🧑‍💼", "manager", "The manager organised a meeting."], ["🎖️", "authority", "The police have the authority to stop cars."], ["⚡", "power", "Power can change people."], ["📈", "promote", "She was promoted to team leader."], ["🧭", "vision", "A leader needs a clear vision."], ["🌟", "inspire", "Great leaders inspire people."], ["🤝", "trust", "You have to earn your team's trust."]]}, {"t": "Leadership skills", "ar": "مهارات القيادة", "items": [["👂", "listen", "Leaders should listen more than they speak."], ["🤲", "delegate", "Good leaders delegate tasks."], ["💪", "motivate", "How do you motivate your team?"], ["🎯", "decisive", "A leader must be decisive in a crisis."], ["🧘", "calm under pressure", "She stays calm under pressure."], ["🗣️", "communicate", "Communicate your goals clearly."], ["🌈", "empathy", "Empathy helps you understand your team."], ["🏆", "lead by example", "He leads by example — he works hardest."]]}, {"t": "Power & responsibility", "ar": "السلطة والمسؤولية", "items": [["🙋", "responsibility", "With power comes responsibility."], ["👏", "credit", "Give credit to the team."], ["👉", "blame", "Don't blame others for your mistakes."], ["🧱", "abuse of power", "Abuse of power is a serious problem."], ["🗳️", "accountable", "Leaders should be accountable for their actions."], ["🎭", "charisma", "He has natural charisma."], ["🦁", "bossy", "Don't be bossy — be a leader."], ["🤔", "humble", "The best leaders are humble."]]}], "talk": [{"title": "Let's Talk · Student A", "ar": "الطالب A", "list": [["Who is the best leader you know personally?", "مين أحسن قائد تعرفه شخصيًا؟", "My football coach — he believed in every player."], ["Are leaders born or made?", "القادة بيتولدوا قادة ولا بيتعلموا؟", "I think they are mostly made through experience."], ["Would you like to be a leader? Why or why not?", "نفسك تبقى قائد؟", "Yes, but I'm afraid of the responsibility."], ["What is the difference between a boss and a leader?", "إيه الفرق بين المدير والقائد؟", "A boss gives orders; a leader inspires."], ["Does power change people? How?", "السلطة بتغير الناس؟ إزاي؟", "Sometimes it makes them forget where they came from."]]}, {"title": "Let's Talk · Student B", "ar": "الطالب B", "list": [["Which qualities are most important in a leader?", "إيه أهم صفات القائد؟", "Honesty, empathy and courage."], ["Should leaders be young or experienced?", "القادة يكونوا شباب ولا أصحاب خبرة؟", "A mix of both is ideal."], ["How would you motivate a lazy team?", "إزاي تحفّز فريق كسلان؟", "I'd find out what really interests them."], ["Is it possible to be a leader without a title?", "ينفع تبقى قائد من غير منصب؟", "Yes, anyone can lead by example."], ["Describe a time you led a group.", "احكي عن مرة قدت فيها مجموعة.", "I organised a school trip for 30 students."]]}], "grammar": {"title": "Inversion for Emphasis", "ar": "القلب للتأكيد — Never have I… / Not only… / Rarely do…", "blocks": [{"type": "intro", "en": "After certain negative or restrictive words at the start of a sentence, we invert the subject and the auxiliary verb (like in a question). This makes the sentence sound dramatic, formal and emphatic.", "ar": "لما نبدأ الجملة بكلمات نفي أو تقييد معينة، بنقلب الفاعل والفعل المساعد (زي السؤال). ده بيخلي الجملة قوية ورسمية وفيها تأكيد."}, {"type": "big", "items": [{"v": "Never / Rarely / Seldom + auxiliary + subject", "p": "frequency", "c": 1, "eg": ["Never have I managed so many people.", "Rarely do bad managers ask for ideas.", "Seldom have I received such useful advice."]}, {"v": "Not only + auxiliary + subject…, but (also)…", "p": "addition", "c": 2, "eg": ["Not only are you experienced, but you're also good with people.", "Not only did she win, but she also broke the record.", "Not only does he lead, but he also listens."]}, {"v": "Only when / Under no circumstances / Hardly…when", "p": "time & condition", "c": 3, "eg": ["Only when something went wrong did he talk to us.", "Under no circumstances should you share the password.", "Hardly had I arrived when the meeting started."]}]}, {"type": "table", "title": "🔄 Normal → Inverted", "head": ["Normal", "Inverted (emphatic)"], "rows": [["I have never seen such a mess.", "Never have I seen such a mess."], ["He rarely smiles.", "Rarely does he smile."], ["She won and she broke the record.", "Not only did she win, but she also broke the record."], ["He only spoke when it was too late.", "Only when it was too late did he speak."], ["You mustn't open this door.", "Under no circumstances must you open this door."]]}, {"type": "uses", "title": "🎤 Where do we use it?", "ar": "بنستخدمها فين؟", "items": [["🎙️", "speeches", "Never before have we faced such a challenge.", "خطابات"], ["📰", "formal writing", "Not only does pollution harm health, but it also costs money.", "كتابة رسمية"], ["📖", "storytelling", "Hardly had she left when the phone rang.", "حكايات"], ["💥", "strong emotion", "Never have I been so proud!", "مشاعر قوية"]]}, {"type": "tip", "en": "Use do/does/did when there is no other auxiliary: Rarely he smiles ✖ → Rarely does he smile ✔. And the main verb goes back to base form: Not only did she won ✖ → Not only did she win ✔.", "ar": "لو مفيش فعل مساعد استخدم do/does/did: Rarely does he smile. والفعل الأساسي يرجع لأصله: Not only did she win."}]}, "exercises": [{"type": "mcq", "title": "Inversion — 10 MCQs", "ar": "اختار الصح", "speak": true, "items": [{"q": "Never ___ so many people before.", "o": ["have I managed", "I have managed", "I managed", "managed I"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Rarely ___ bad managers ask for ideas.", "o": ["do", "are", "have", "does"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Not only ___ experienced, but you are also kind.", "o": ["are you", "you are", "do you", "you do"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Only when something went wrong ___ to us.", "o": ["did he talk", "he talked", "he did talk", "talked he"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Under no circumstances ___ share your password.", "o": ["should you", "you should", "you shouldn't", "shouldn't you"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Seldom ___ such useful advice.", "o": ["have I received", "I have received", "I received", "received I"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Not only did she win, but she ___ broke the record.", "o": ["also", "too", "either", "as well as"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Hardly ___ arrived when the meeting started.", "o": ["had I", "I had", "have I", "I have"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Which sentence is correct?", "o": ["Rarely does he smile.", "Rarely he smiles.", "Rarely does he smiles.", "Rarely he does smile."], "a": 0}, {"q": "Which sentence is correct?", "o": ["Not only did she win, but she also broke the record.", "Not only she won, but also broke the record.", "Not only did she won, but she also broke the record.", "Not only she did win, but she also broke the record."], "a": 0}]}, {"type": "mcq", "title": "Normal or inverted?", "ar": "عادي ولا مقلوب؟", "items": [{"q": "\"I have never felt so proud.\" → ___", "o": ["Never have I felt so proud.", "Never I have felt so proud."], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"He rarely makes mistakes.\" → ___", "o": ["Rarely does he make mistakes.", "Rarely he makes mistakes."], "a": 0}, {"q": "Inversion makes a sentence more ___.", "o": ["emphatic and formal", "casual and short"], "a": 0}, {"q": "After \"Only when…\", we invert the ___ clause.", "o": ["second (main)", "first"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Inversion is common in ___.", "o": ["speeches and formal writing", "text messages to friends"], "a": 0}]}, {"type": "ord", "title": "Make sentences", "ar": "رتّب الكلمات", "items": [{"c": ["Never", "have I", "seen", "such a mess"], "a": [0, 1, 2, 3]}, {"c": ["Rarely", "does", "he", "smile"], "a": [0, 1, 2, 3]}, {"c": ["Not only", "is she", "smart,", "but she is also kind"], "a": [0, 1, 2, 3]}, {"c": ["Under no circumstances", "should you", "open", "this door"], "a": [0, 1, 2, 3]}]}], "reading": {"title": "The Servant Leader", "ar": "القائد الخادم", "g": "m", "lines": [["When we imagine a powerful leader, we often picture someone at the top of a pyramid, giving orders to the people below.", "لما بنتخيل قائد قوي، غالبًا بنتخيل حد على قمة هرم، بيدي أوامر للناس اللي تحته."], ["However, a growing number of experts believe that the most effective leaders turn this pyramid upside down.", "لكن عدد متزايد من الخبراء شايفين إن أكثر القادة تأثيرًا بيقلبوا الهرم ده."], ["The idea is called \"servant leadership\". Rather than asking \"How can my team serve me?\", servant leaders ask \"How can I serve my team?\"", "الفكرة اسمها \"القيادة الخادمة\". بدل ما يسأل \"فريقي يخدمني إزاي؟\"، القائد الخادم بيسأل \"أنا أخدم فريقي إزاي؟\""], ["They focus on removing obstacles, developing people's skills and making sure everyone has what they need to succeed.", "بيركزوا على إزالة العقبات، وتطوير مهارات الناس، والتأكد إن كل واحد عنده اللي محتاجه عشان ينجح."], ["Not only does this approach make employees happier, but research suggests it also improves results.", "مش بس الأسلوب ده بيخلي الموظفين أسعد، لكن الأبحاث بتقول إنه كمان بيحسّن النتايج."], ["Teams led by servant leaders tend to show higher levels of trust, creativity and loyalty.", "الفرق اللي بيقودها قادة خادمين غالبًا بيبقى عندها مستويات أعلى من الثقة والإبداع والولاء."], ["People are more willing to take risks and share new ideas when they know their leader will support them.", "الناس بيبقوا مستعدين أكتر ياخدوا مخاطرات ويشاركوا أفكار جديدة لما يعرفوا إن قائدهم هيدعمهم."], ["Of course, servant leadership has its critics. Some argue that, in a crisis, a team needs a decisive leader who can act quickly without asking everyone's opinion.", "طبعًا، القيادة الخادمة ليها منتقدين. في ناس بيقولوا إن في الأزمات، الفريق محتاج قائد حاسم يقدر يتصرف بسرعة من غير ما ياخد رأي الكل."], ["Others warn that leaders who try too hard to please everyone may avoid difficult decisions.", "وغيرهم بيحذروا إن القادة اللي بيحاولوا يرضوا الكل زيادة ممكن يتهربوا من القرارات الصعبة."], ["Perhaps the best leaders know when to serve and when to steer. Rarely is there one perfect style for every situation.", "يمكن أحسن القادة هما اللي عارفين إمتى يخدموا وإمتى يوجّهوا. نادرًا ما بيكون في أسلوب واحد مثالي لكل موقف."]], "keys": [["🔺", "pyramid", "a shape with a wide base and a point at the top"], ["🙃", "upside down", "with the top at the bottom"], ["🧱", "obstacle", "something that makes progress difficult"], ["🤝", "loyalty", "strong support and faithfulness"], ["🎯", "decisive", "able to make decisions quickly"], ["🧭", "steer", "to guide or direct"]], "quiz": [{"q": "How do we often imagine a powerful leader?", "o": ["at the top of a pyramid giving orders", "working alone", "as a servant"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What question do servant leaders ask?", "o": ["How can I serve my team?", "How can my team serve me?", "How much will I earn?"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What do servant leaders focus on?", "o": ["removing obstacles and developing skills", "giving orders", "taking credit"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What do teams led by servant leaders show?", "o": ["higher trust, creativity and loyalty", "lower results", "more conflict"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What do critics say about crises?", "o": ["A team needs a decisive leader.", "Teams should vote on everything.", "Leaders should do nothing."], "a": 0}, {"q": "What is the main idea of the last paragraph?", "o": ["Good leaders know when to serve and when to steer.", "There is one perfect leadership style.", "Servant leadership always fails."], "a": 0}]}, "idioms": {"items": [["call the shots", "To be the person who makes the important decisions.", "هو اللي بيقرر", "In this company, the CEO calls the shots.", "في الشركة دي، المدير التنفيذي هو اللي بيقرر."], ["take the lead", "To start leading or controlling a situation.", "ياخد زمام المبادرة", "Nobody knew what to do, so Mariam took the lead.", "محدش كان عارف يعمل إيه، فمريم خدت زمام المبادرة."], ["the buck stops here", "I accept final responsibility.", "المسؤولية النهائية عليّا", "As the manager, the buck stops with me.", "كمدير، المسؤولية النهائية عليّا."], ["rule with an iron fist", "To control people in a very strict, harsh way.", "يحكم بإيد من حديد", "The old director ruled with an iron fist.", "المدير القديم كان بيحكم بإيد من حديد."]], "quiz": [{"q": "She's the boss — she ___.", "o": ["calls the shots", "rules the buck", "takes the iron", "stops the lead"], "a": 0}, {"q": "When the problem happened, the manager said, \"___.\"", "o": ["The buck stops here", "Call the shots", "Iron fist", "Take the lead"], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"Rule with an iron fist\" means…", "o": ["control people very strictly", "be very kind", "fight with your hands", "build things"], "a": 0}, {"q": "In the group project, Ahmed ___ and organised everyone.", "o": ["took the lead", "called the buck", "stopped the shots", "ruled the iron"], "a": 0}]}, "phrasal": {"items": [["step up", "To take more responsibility, especially when needed.", "يتقدم ويتحمل المسؤولية", "When the manager got sick, Ali stepped up.", "لما المدير تعب، علي اتقدم واتحمل المسؤولية."], ["step down", "To leave an important position.", "يتنحى / يسيب منصبه", "The CEO stepped down after the scandal.", "المدير التنفيذي اتنحى بعد الفضيحة."], ["take charge", "To take control and responsibility.", "يمسك زمام الأمور", "She took charge of the project.", "مسكت زمام المشروع."], ["win over", "To persuade someone to support you.", "يكسب تأييد حد", "The new leader won over the team quickly.", "القائد الجديد كسب تأييد الفريق بسرعة."]], "quiz": [{"q": "After 20 years, the president decided to ___.", "o": ["step down", "step up", "win over", "take charge"], "a": 0}, {"q": "We need someone to ___ and organise the event.", "o": ["take charge", "step down", "win over", "step off"], "a": 0}, {"q": "It took months to ___ the sceptical employees ___.", "o": ["win / over", "step / up", "take / charge", "step / down"], "a": 0}, {"q": "When the captain was injured, the young player ___.", "o": ["stepped up", "stepped down", "won over", "took off"], "a": 0}]}, "slang": {"items": [["boss move", "A confident, impressive action.", "حركة معلّم", "Asking for a raise with a full report? Boss move.", "تطلب علاوة ومعاك تقرير كامل؟ حركة معلّم.", "مدح"], ["GOAT", "Greatest Of All Time.", "أعظم واحد في التاريخ", "Salah is the GOAT of Egyptian football.", "صلاح أعظم لاعب في تاريخ الكورة المصرية.", "منتشرة في الرياضة"], ["power trip", "When someone enjoys controlling others too much.", "متسلط ومستمتع بالسلطة", "Since he became class monitor, he's been on a power trip.", "من ساعة ما بقى ألفة الفصل، بقى متسلط.", "انتقاد"], ["run the show", "To be in charge.", "هو اللي ماسك كل حاجة", "Everyone knows Mona runs the show here.", "الكل عارف إن منى هي اللي ماسكة كل حاجة هنا.", "عادي"], ["carry the team", "To do most of the work for a group.", "شايل الفريق", "In the group project, I literally carried the team.", "في المشروع الجماعي، أنا كنت شايل الفريق حرفيًا.", "من لغة الجيمرز"]], "quiz": [{"q": "\"He's on a power trip.\" means he…", "o": ["enjoys controlling others too much", "is travelling", "has a lot of energy", "is a pilot"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Doing most of the work for your group = ___.", "o": ["carrying the team", "a power trip", "GOAT", "boss move"], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"GOAT\" stands for…", "o": ["Greatest Of All Time", "Good Old Amazing Team", "Get Out And Try", "Game Over At Ten"], "a": 0}, {"q": "The person in charge ___.", "o": ["runs the show", "carries a goat", "trips the power", "moves the boss"], "a": 0}]}, "story": {"title": "The Captain Who Sat on the Bench", "ar": "الكابتن اللي قعد على الدكة", "g": "f", "lines": [["Omar had been captain of the school football team for three years. He was the best player, and everybody knew it — especially Omar.", "عمر كان كابتن فريق كورة المدرسة ٣ سنين. كان أحسن لاعب، والكل عارف ده — خصوصًا عمر."], ["He called the shots on and off the pitch. He chose who played, shouted at mistakes, and never passed the ball when he could score himself.", "كان هو اللي بيقرر جوه الملعب وبرّه. بيختار مين يلعب، ويزعق على الأخطاء، وعمره ما باصي الكورة لو يقدر يجيب جول بنفسه."], ["The team won many matches, but nobody enjoyed playing anymore.", "الفريق كسب ماتشات كتير، بس محدش كان مستمتع بالعب خلاص."], ["Then, just before the final, Omar broke his ankle. Never had he felt so helpless.", "وبعدين، قبل النهائي على طول، عمر كسر كاحله. عمره ما حس بالعجز ده قبل كده."], ["The coach asked quiet Hassan, a defender, to take charge. Omar laughed. \"Him? He never even speaks!\"", "المدرب طلب من حسن الهادي، لاعب الدفاع، يمسك زمام الأمور. عمر ضحك. \"هو؟ ده عمره ما بيتكلم!\""], ["From the bench, Omar watched something surprising. Hassan didn't shout. He asked each player what they needed. He encouraged the youngest players and passed the ball to whoever had the best chance.", "من على الدكة، عمر شاف حاجة غريبة. حسن مزعقش. سأل كل لاعب محتاج إيه. شجّع اللاعيبة الأصغر، وباصي الكورة لأي حد عنده فرصة أحسن."], ["Not only did the team play better, but they were smiling again.", "مش بس الفريق لعب أحسن، لكن رجعوا يبتسموا تاني."], ["They won the final 2–1. The winning goal was scored by a fourteen-year-old who had never started a match before.", "كسبوا النهائي ٢–١. جول الفوز جابه لاعب عنده ١٤ سنة عمره ما لعب أساسي قبل كده."], ["That night, Omar sent Hassan a message: \"Only now do I understand what a real captain is. You're the GOAT.\"", "بالليل، عمر بعت لحسن رسالة: \"دلوقتي بس فهمت يعني إيه كابتن حقيقي. إنت الأعظم.\""], ["When Omar returned the next season, he asked Hassan to stay captain — and for the first time, Omar learned to pass.", "لما عمر رجع الموسم اللي بعده، طلب من حسن يفضل الكابتن — ولأول مرة، عمر اتعلم يباصي."]], "quiz": [{"q": "What kind of captain was Omar?", "o": ["He called the shots and shouted at mistakes.", "He was quiet and kind.", "He never played."], "a": 0}, {"q": "What happened before the final?", "o": ["Omar broke his ankle.", "Hassan left the team.", "The coach quit."], "a": 0}, {"q": "How did Hassan lead the team?", "o": ["He listened and encouraged the players.", "He shouted at everyone.", "He scored all the goals."], "a": 0}, {"q": "Who scored the winning goal?", "o": ["a fourteen-year-old player", "Hassan", "Omar"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What did Omar learn?", "o": ["what a real captain is", "how to shoot", "how to win alone"], "a": 0}]}, "challenge": {"title": "Take the Lead", "ar": "خد زمام المبادرة — جاوب وسجّل", "qs": ["Describe a great leader from history and explain why they were successful.", "Use inversion to describe your proudest moment: \"Never have I…\"", "Would you rather be a leader or a follower? Why?", "What would you do if your team refused to follow your plan?", "Should leaders be friends with the people they manage?", "Not only… but also…: describe two qualities of a good teacher.", "Is it possible to have too much power? Give an example.", "How should a leader react to a big mistake?", "If you were president of your country for one day, what would you change?", "Describe a time when someone \"stepped up\" in a difficult situation."]}, "games": {"pairs": [["👑", "leader"], ["⚡", "power"], ["🎖️", "authority"], ["🧭", "vision"], ["👏", "credit"], ["👉", "blame"]], "spell": [["🌟", "inspire"], ["🤝", "trust"], ["💪", "motivate"], ["🎯", "decisive"], ["🌈", "empathy"], ["🙋", "responsibility"], ["🎭", "charisma"], ["🤔", "humble"]], "speed": [["Never have I seen such a mess.", true], ["Never I have seen such a mess.", false], ["Rarely does he smile.", true], ["Rarely he smiles.", false], ["Not only did she win, but she also broke the record.", true], ["Not only did she won the race.", false], ["Only when it rained did we stop.", true], ["Under no circumstances should you open it.", true], ["Seldom have I received such advice.", true], ["Hardly I had arrived when it started.", false], ["A humble leader shows off a lot.", false], ["Empathy helps you understand others.", true], ["\"Call the shots\" means to make the decisions.", true], ["\"Step down\" means to leave a position.", true], ["\"Power trip\" means a holiday.", false], ["\"Lead by example\" means to do what you expect others to do.", true]]}, "test": {"pass": 60, "sections": [{"id": "voc", "title": "Vocabulary", "ar": "المفردات", "icon": "📚", "qs": [{"q": "The power to give orders = ___.", "o": ["authority", "empathy", "loyalty"], "a": 0, "pic": "🎖️"}, {"q": "Able to make decisions quickly = ___.", "o": ["decisive", "humble", "bossy"], "a": 0, "pic": "🎯"}, {"q": "Praise for something good you did = ___.", "o": ["credit", "blame", "power"], "a": 0, "pic": "👏"}, {"q": "Understanding how others feel = ___.", "o": ["empathy", "charisma", "vision"], "a": 0, "pic": "🌈"}, {"q": "Not proud; modest = ___.", "o": ["humble", "bossy", "decisive"], "a": 0, "pic": "🤔"}, {"q": "\"مسؤولية\" in English is…", "o": ["responsibility", "response", "reputation"], "a": 0, "say": "Choose the correct word."}]}, {"id": "gra", "title": "Grammar", "ar": "القواعد", "icon": "📘", "qs": [{"q": "Never ___ such a beautiful view.", "o": ["have I seen", "I have seen", "I saw"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Rarely ___ late for work.", "o": ["is she", "she is", "does she"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Not only ___ the exam, but he also got the top mark.", "o": ["did he pass", "he passed", "did he passed"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Only when I got home ___ I had lost my keys.", "o": ["did I realise", "I realised", "I did realise"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Under no circumstances ___ the building.", "o": ["should you leave", "you should leave", "leave you"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Which is correct?", "o": ["Seldom do we see such talent.", "Seldom we see such talent.", "Seldom do we sees such talent."], "a": 0}]}, {"id": "con", "title": "Conversation", "ar": "المحادثة", "icon": "💬", "qs": [{"q": "\"I was promoted to team leader!\" — Best answer:", "o": ["Congratulations! You'll be great.", "Promote is a verb.", "Leader is a person."], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"What makes a good leader?\" — Best answer:", "o": ["Listening and leading by example.", "Shouting a lot.", "A big office."], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"Who makes the decisions here?\" — Best answer:", "o": ["The director calls the shots.", "The shots are called.", "Decisions are made of paper."], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"The project failed. Whose fault is it?\" — Best answer:", "o": ["As the leader, the buck stops with me.", "The buck is a deer.", "Not mine, ever!"], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"Since he became captain, he orders everyone around.\" — Best answer:", "o": ["Sounds like he's on a power trip.", "Is he travelling?", "Captains fly planes."], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"How was the speech?\" — Best answer:", "o": ["Never have I heard such a powerful speech!", "Never I have heard it.", "Speech is talking."], "a": 0}]}, {"id": "rea", "title": "Reading", "ar": "القراءة", "icon": "📖", "passage": ["When Dina became the manager of a small bookshop, sales were falling.", "Rather than giving orders, she asked each employee for ideas. Not only did they suggest a reading club, but they also offered to run it themselves.", "Within six months, the club had over a hundred members.", "Rarely had the staff felt so motivated. \"She makes us feel part of the team,\" said one employee.", "Dina says, \"Leadership isn't about being the boss. It's about helping others succeed.\""], "qs": [{"q": "What problem did the bookshop have?", "o": ["Sales were falling.", "It was too small.", "It had no books."], "a": 0}, {"q": "What did Dina do instead of giving orders?", "o": ["asked employees for ideas", "fired people", "closed the shop"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What did the employees suggest?", "o": ["a reading club", "a café", "lower prices"], "a": 0}, {"q": "How many members did the club have after six months?", "o": ["over a hundred", "ten", "fifty"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What is leadership, according to Dina?", "o": ["helping others succeed", "being the boss", "making money"], "a": 0}]}, {"id": "wri", "title": "Writing", "ar": "الكتابة", "icon": "✍️", "writing": true, "prompt": "Write a short speech (80–120 words) as a new class or team leader. Tell people what kind of leader you will be. Use at least three inversions (Never have I…, Not only…, Rarely…, Under no circumstances…).", "promptAr": "اكتب خطاب قصير (٨٠–١٢٠ كلمة) كقائد جديد لفصل أو فريق، ووضّح هتبقى قائد إزاي. استخدم ٣ جمل Inversion على الأقل.", "checks": [["👑", "Leadership words", "x", "\\b(leader|leadership|team|lead|responsibility|trust|listen|power|decision|decisions|support)\\b"], ["🔄", "Negative inversion", "x", "\\b(never|rarely|seldom|hardly)\\s+(have|has|had|do|does|did|am|is|are|was|were|will|can|should)\\s+\\w+"], ["➕", "Not only… but also", "x", "\\bnot only\\s+(do|does|did|is|are|was|were|have|has|had|will|can)\\b"], ["💬", "At least 70 words", "len70"]]}]}, "watch": [{"yt": "ktgDXNML2uI", "title": "No More Bosses", "ar": "من غير مديرين — 6 Minute English", "by": "BBC Learning English", "lines": [["Neil and Georgina say they make a great team, but most people have had a bad boss they just could not get on with.", "نيل وجورجينا بيقولوا إنهم فريق ممتاز، بس أغلب الناس قابلوا مدير وحش مقدروش يتفاهموا معاه."], ["This often happens because workers feel managers don't listen, and most companies are hierarchies.", "ده غالبًا بيحصل عشان الموظفين حاسين إن المديرين مش بيسمعوهم، وأغلب الشركات عبارة عن تسلسل هرمي."], ["A hierarchy puts managers at the top and workers at the bottom.", "التسلسل الهرمي بيحط المديرين فوق والموظفين تحت."], ["Some companies have got rid of managers and say they now work better, feel happier and save money.", "في شركات اتخلصت من المديرين وبتقول إنها بقت بتشتغل أحسن وأسعد وبتوفّر فلوس."], ["The quiz: how much does too much management and bureaucracy cost the US economy every year?", "السؤال: الإدارة الزيادة والبيروقراطية بتكلّف الاقتصاد الأمريكي قد إيه كل سنة؟"], ["Morning Star, a tomato company in California, is a famous self-managing company with no bosses.", "مورنينج ستار، شركة طماطم في كاليفورنيا، شركة مشهورة بتدير نفسها من غير مديرين."], ["It has two main rules: don't use force on other people, and keep the commitments you make.", "عندها قاعدتين أساسيين: متستخدمش الضغط على حد، والتزم بالوعود اللي بتديها."], ["Decisions are made by all employees equally, without coercion. Nobody can order a colleague around.", "القرارات بياخدها كل الموظفين بالتساوي، من غير إجبار. محدش يقدر يأمر زميله."], ["This empowers workers and gives everyone a voice — but they must be accountable for their results.", "ده بيقوّي الموظفين وبيدي كل واحد صوت — بس لازم يكونوا مسؤولين عن نتايجهم."], ["Having no boss sounds great, but the extra responsibility can create more work and stress.", "إنك تشتغل من غير مدير شكلها حلو، بس المسؤولية الزيادة ممكن تعمل شغل وضغط أكتر."], ["Some employees may be left behind, while others take advantage of the freedom and do brilliantly.", "في موظفين ممكن يتأخروا عن الباقيين، وغيرهم بيستغلوا الحرية وينجحوا جدًا."], ["The answer: three trillion dollars a year — and the cost keeps rising as companies add more managers.", "الإجابة: ٣ تريليون دولار في السنة — والتكلفة بتزيد كل ما الشركات تزوّد مديرين."]], "words": ["get on with", "hierarchies", "managers", "got rid of", "bureaucracy", "self-managing", "commitments", "coercion", "empowers", "accountable", "responsibility", "left behind"], "quiz": [{"q": "What is a hierarchy?", "o": ["a system with managers at the top and workers below", "a company with no rules", "a type of meeting"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What does Morning Star produce?", "o": ["tomatoes", "coffee", "cars"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What are its two main rules?", "o": ["no force on others, and keep your commitments", "work hard and obey the boss", "arrive early and leave late"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What is \"coercion\"?", "o": ["using force to make someone do something", "working as a team", "making a promise"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What is a disadvantage of having no boss?", "o": ["extra responsibility can cause stress", "everyone earns less", "there are no decisions"], "a": 0}, {"q": "How much does too much management cost the US each year?", "o": ["three trillion dollars", "three million dollars", "three billion dollars"], "a": 0}]}]}, "4": {"n": 4, "title": "The Art of Persuasion", "ar": "فن الإقناع — Cleft Sentences", "icon": "🎯", "cover": "img/b2p/u4.jpg", "intro": "اتعلم إزاي تقنع الناس في البيع والمناقشات والعروض، وإزاي تاخد بالك من حيل الإقناع حواليك، واستخدم الـ Cleft Sentences عشان تركز على أهم معلومة: What really matters is… / It was… that…", "videos": [{"id": "b2pv4", "title": "The Pitch", "ar": "عرض الفكرة — هنا وعلي", "src": "video/b2p/u4v1.mp4", "poster": "img/b2p/u4v1.jpg", "sp": {"a": {"n": "Hana", "g": "f"}, "b": {"n": "Ali", "g": "m"}}, "lines": [["a", "Ali, I have to pitch my app idea to investors tomorrow, and I'm terrified.", "علي، لازم أعرض فكرة الأبلكيشن بتاعي على مستثمرين بكرة، وأنا مرعوبة."], ["b", "Don't worry. Show me your first slide.", "متقلقيش. وريني أول سلايد."], ["a", "It's about the technology: the database, the design, the features…", "هو عن التكنولوجيا: قاعدة البيانات، والتصميم، والمميزات…"], ["b", "That's the problem. What investors want to hear first isn't the technology. It's the problem you're solving.", "دي المشكلة. اللي المستثمرين عايزين يسمعوه الأول مش التكنولوجيا. هو المشكلة اللي إنتي بتحليها."], ["a", "Hmm. The problem is that students waste hours looking for reliable tutors.", "امم. المشكلة إن الطلاب بيضيعوا ساعات يدوروا على مدرسين موثوقين."], ["b", "Perfect! Start with a story. It was a story about a real student that convinced me to buy my first course.", "تمام! ابدئي بقصة. اللي أقنعني أشتري أول كورس ليا كانت قصة عن طالب حقيقي."], ["a", "A story… like my cousin who failed maths because he couldn't find help?", "قصة… زي ابن خالتي اللي سقط في الرياضة عشان ملقاش حد يساعده؟"], ["b", "Exactly. What really persuades people is emotion first, then logic. Then show your numbers.", "بالظبط. اللي بيقنع الناس بجد هو المشاعر الأول، وبعدين المنطق. وبعدين اعرضي أرقامك."], ["a", "And what about my voice? I always speak too fast when I'm nervous.", "وصوتي؟ أنا دايمًا بتكلم بسرعة لما ببقى متوترة."], ["b", "Pause after important points. What makes a speaker sound confident is silence, not speed.", "اقفي بعد النقط المهمة. اللي بيخلي المتكلم يبان واثق هو السكوت، مش السرعة."], ["a", "Great tips. One last thing — how do I end?", "نصايح حلوة. آخر حاجة — أختم إزاي؟"], ["b", "With a clear call to action. Tell them exactly what you need. It's confidence that closes the deal.", "بطلب واضح. قوليلهم بالظبط إنتي محتاجة إيه. الثقة هي اللي بتقفل الصفقة."]], "quiz": [{"q": "What does Hana have to do tomorrow?", "o": ["pitch her app idea to investors", "take an exam", "start a new job"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What do investors want to hear first, according to Ali?", "o": ["the problem you are solving", "the technology", "the price"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What convinced Ali to buy his first course?", "o": ["a story about a real student", "a discount", "a famous actor"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What makes a speaker sound confident, according to Ali?", "o": ["silence (pausing)", "speaking fast", "shouting"], "a": 0}, {"q": "How should Hana end her pitch?", "o": ["with a clear call to action", "with a joke", "with a question about the weather"], "a": 0}], "fill": [[0, "pitch"], [0, "investors"], [3, "What investors want to hear"], [4, "reliable"], [5, "It was a story"], [5, "convinced"], [7, "What really persuades people"], [7, "emotion"], [7, "logic"], [9, "confident"], [11, "call to action"], [11, "closes the deal"]]}], "vocab": [{"t": "Persuasion", "ar": "الإقناع", "items": [["🎯", "persuade", "She persuaded me to join the club."], ["🤝", "convince", "His story convinced the investors."], ["💬", "argument", "That's a strong argument."], ["📊", "evidence", "Support your opinion with evidence."], ["❤️", "emotional appeal", "Adverts often use emotional appeal."], ["🧠", "logic", "Use logic and facts to persuade people."], ["🗣️", "rhetoric", "Politicians are experts in rhetoric."], ["🎤", "pitch", "He gave a great pitch to the investors."]]}, {"t": "Marketing & influence", "ar": "التسويق والتأثير", "items": [["📢", "advertisement", "The advertisement was very clever."], ["🏷️", "slogan", "The company has a catchy slogan."], ["🎁", "special offer", "Hurry! Special offer ends today."], ["⏳", "limited time", "Limited time only — buy now!"], ["⭐", "review", "I always read reviews before buying."], ["👥", "social proof", "Seeing others buy something is social proof."], ["🧲", "appeal to", "The ad appeals to young people."], ["🪤", "manipulate", "Some ads manipulate our emotions."]]}, {"t": "Presenting", "ar": "العرض والتقديم", "items": [["📽️", "slide", "Keep each slide simple."], ["⏸️", "pause", "Pause after important points."], ["👁️", "audience", "Know your audience before you speak."], ["🎬", "call to action", "End with a clear call to action."], ["💡", "key point", "Repeat your key point at the end."], ["📖", "storytelling", "Storytelling makes ideas memorable."], ["🙌", "engage", "Ask questions to engage the audience."], ["🤞", "credible", "Use credible sources."]]}], "talk": [{"title": "Let's Talk · Student A", "ar": "الطالب A", "list": [["Who is the most persuasive person you know?", "مين أكتر شخص مقنع تعرفه؟", "My mother — she always wins arguments!"], ["Have you ever bought something because of an advert?", "اشتريت حاجة قبل كده بسبب إعلان؟", "Yes, a pair of shoes I never wear!"], ["What makes an advert memorable?", "إيه اللي بيخلي الإعلان يفضل في الذاكرة؟", "A funny story or a catchy song."], ["Is it easier to persuade people with facts or with emotions?", "أسهل تقنع الناس بالحقايق ولا بالمشاعر؟", "Emotions, usually."], ["How do you persuade your parents to let you do something?", "بتقنع أهلك إزاي يسيبوك تعمل حاجة؟", "I prepare good reasons and choose the right moment."]]}, {"title": "Let's Talk · Student B", "ar": "الطالب B", "list": [["Should advertising to children be banned?", "لازم نمنع الإعلانات الموجهة للأطفال؟", "Some of it, yes, especially for junk food."], ["Do you trust online reviews?", "بتثق في التقييمات أونلاين؟", "Not completely. Some are fake."], ["What is the difference between persuading and manipulating?", "إيه الفرق بين الإقناع والتلاعب؟", "Persuasion is honest; manipulation is not."], ["Which famous speech do you find inspiring?", "أنهي خطاب مشهور بيلهمك؟", "\"I Have a Dream\" by Martin Luther King."], ["If you had to sell this pen to me, what would you say?", "لو لازم تبيعلي القلم ده، تقول إيه؟", "What you need is a pen that never lets you down…"]]}], "grammar": {"title": "Cleft Sentences", "ar": "الجمل المقسومة — What… is / It was… that…", "blocks": [{"type": "intro", "en": "A cleft sentence splits one idea into two parts to put the focus on the most important information. They are very common in persuasive speaking and writing.", "ar": "الـ Cleft sentence بتقسم الفكرة لجزئين عشان تركز على أهم معلومة. ومنتشرة جدًا في الكلام والكتابة الإقناعية."}, {"type": "big", "items": [{"v": "What + clause + is/was + focus", "p": "wh-cleft", "c": 1, "eg": ["What investors want is a clear problem.", "What really persuades people is emotion.", "What I need is more time."]}, {"v": "It is/was + focus + that/who + clause", "p": "it-cleft", "c": 2, "eg": ["It was a story that convinced me.", "It's confidence that closes the deal.", "It was Ali who helped me."]}, {"v": "All / The thing / The reason… + is", "p": "other clefts", "c": 3, "eg": ["All I want is a chance.", "The thing I love most is the design.", "The reason I failed is that I didn't prepare."]}]}, {"type": "table", "title": "🔄 Normal → Cleft", "head": ["Normal", "Cleft (with focus)"], "rows": [["Emotion persuades people.", "What persuades people is emotion."], ["A story convinced me.", "It was a story that convinced me."], ["I need a holiday.", "What I need is a holiday."], ["Ali helped me, not Omar.", "It was Ali who helped me, not Omar."], ["I only want to help.", "All I want is to help."]]}, {"type": "uses", "title": "🎯 Why use clefts?", "ar": "ليه نستخدمها؟", "items": [["🔦", "focus", "What matters most is your health.", "تركيز"], ["✋", "correct someone", "It wasn't me who broke it — it was Omar!", "تصحيح"], ["🎤", "persuade", "What you need is this course.", "إقناع"], ["📝", "explain reasons", "The reason I called is to say thank you.", "شرح السبب"]]}, {"type": "tip", "en": "With 'What…' clefts, use a singular verb (is/was): What I need are ideas ✖ (informal) → What I need is ideas/some ideas ✔ is the safer choice. With it-clefts, use 'who' for people and 'that' for things (or both).", "ar": "في What… غالبًا الفعل مفرد is/was. وفي It is…، استخدم who للناس وthat للحاجات (أو للاتنين)."}]}, "exercises": [{"type": "mcq", "title": "Cleft Sentences — 10 MCQs", "ar": "اختار الصح", "speak": true, "items": [{"q": "___ investors want to hear is a clear problem.", "o": ["What", "That", "Which", "It"], "a": 0}, {"q": "It was a story ___ convinced me.", "o": ["that", "what", "where", "how"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What really persuades people ___ emotion.", "o": ["is", "are", "be", "being"], "a": 0}, {"q": "It was Ali ___ helped me with my pitch.", "o": ["who", "what", "which", "where"], "a": 0}, {"q": "___ I want is a fair chance.", "o": ["All", "Every", "That", "It"], "a": 0}, {"q": "The reason I called ___ to say thank you.", "o": ["is", "was it", "that", "being"], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"Confidence closes the deal.\" → It's confidence ___ closes the deal.", "o": ["that", "what", "it", "is"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What makes a speaker confident ___ silence, not speed.", "o": ["is", "are", "it is", "that"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Which is a cleft sentence?", "o": ["What I need is a holiday.", "I need a holiday.", "I need a holiday, don't I?", "Do I need a holiday?"], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"It wasn't me who broke it.\" is used to ___.", "o": ["correct someone", "ask a question", "give an order", "describe a habit"], "a": 0}]}, {"type": "mcq", "title": "Choose the focus", "ar": "اختار التركيز", "items": [{"q": "Focus on WHO: \"Mona organised the event.\" → ___", "o": ["It was Mona who organised the event.", "What Mona organised was the event."], "a": 0}, {"q": "Focus on WHAT: \"I love the design.\" → ___", "o": ["What I love is the design.", "It was I who love the design."], "a": 0}, {"q": "What-clefts usually use ___.", "o": ["is / was", "are / were"], "a": 0}, {"q": "It-clefts use ___ for people.", "o": ["who", "what"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Clefts are useful for ___.", "o": ["emphasis and persuasion", "asking for directions"], "a": 0}]}, {"type": "ord", "title": "Make sentences", "ar": "رتّب الكلمات", "items": [{"c": ["What", "investors want", "is", "a clear problem"], "a": [0, 1, 2, 3]}, {"c": ["It was", "a story", "that", "convinced me"], "a": [0, 1, 2, 3]}, {"c": ["All", "I want", "is", "a chance"], "a": [0, 1, 2, 3]}, {"c": ["It was", "Ali", "who", "helped me"], "a": [0, 1, 2, 3]}]}], "reading": {"title": "The Science of Yes", "ar": "علم كلمة \"أيوه\"", "g": "f", "lines": [["Why do we say yes to some requests and no to others? According to psychologist Robert Cialdini, it is often not the request itself that persuades us, but the way it is presented.", "ليه بنقول أيوه لطلبات ولأ لطلبات تانية؟ حسب عالم النفس روبرت تشالديني، غالبًا مش الطلب نفسه اللي بيقنعنا، لكن الطريقة اللي بيتعرض بيها."], ["After years of research, he identified several principles of persuasion that influence our decisions every day.", "بعد سنين من البحث، حدد كذا مبدأ للإقناع بيأثروا على قراراتنا كل يوم."], ["The first is reciprocity: when someone gives us something, we feel we should give something back. That is why restaurants often bring a free sweet with the bill — tips tend to increase.", "الأول هو المعاملة بالمثل: لما حد يدينا حاجة، بنحس إننا لازم نرد. وعشان كده المطاعم كتير بتجيب حلويات ببلاش مع الفاتورة — والبقشيش غالبًا بيزيد."], ["The second is scarcity. What people want most is often what they think they cannot have. \"Only two left!\" and \"Offer ends tonight!\" are classic examples.", "التاني هو الندرة. اللي الناس عايزاه أكتر غالبًا هو اللي فاكرين إنهم مش هيقدروا ياخدوه. \"فاضل اتنين بس!\" و\"العرض بيخلص النهارده!\" أمثلة كلاسيكية."], ["Another powerful principle is social proof. When we are unsure, we look at what others are doing. It is the long queue outside a restaurant that convinces us the food must be good.", "ومبدأ قوي تاني هو الدليل الاجتماعي. لما بنبقى مش متأكدين، بنبص الناس التانية بتعمل إيه. الطابور الطويل قدام المطعم هو اللي بيقنعنا إن الأكل أكيد حلو."], ["We are also more easily persuaded by people we like and by people who seem to have authority, such as doctors or experts in uniforms.", "وكمان بنقتنع بسهولة أكتر من الناس اللي بنحبهم، ومن الناس اللي شكلهم عندهم سلطة، زي الدكاترة أو الخبراء اللي لابسين زي رسمي."], ["Marketers use these principles constantly, which raises an important question: where does persuasion end and manipulation begin?", "المسوّقين بيستخدموا المبادئ دي على طول، وده بيطرح سؤال مهم: الإقناع بيخلص فين والتلاعب بيبدأ فين؟"], ["The difference, many experts agree, is honesty. Persuasion helps people make a choice that is good for them; manipulation tricks them into a choice that benefits someone else.", "الفرق، وده رأي خبراء كتير، هو الأمانة. الإقناع بيساعد الناس ياخدوا قرار كويس ليهم؛ والتلاعب بيضحك عليهم عشان ياخدوا قرار في مصلحة حد تاني."], ["So, the next time you feel a sudden urge to buy something, stop and ask yourself: what is it that is really persuading me?", "فالمرة الجاية لما تحس برغبة مفاجئة تشتري حاجة، وقف واسأل نفسك: إيه اللي بيقنعني بجد؟"]], "keys": [["🔁", "reciprocity", "giving something back when you receive something"], ["⏳", "scarcity", "when something is rare or limited"], ["👥", "social proof", "following what other people do"], ["🎖️", "authority", "the power or expertise that makes people trust you"], ["🪤", "manipulation", "controlling someone in an unfair or dishonest way"], ["⚡", "urge", "a strong sudden wish"]], "quiz": [{"q": "According to Cialdini, what often persuades us?", "o": ["the way a request is presented", "only the price", "only the product"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What is reciprocity?", "o": ["feeling we should give something back", "buying more than we need", "following other people"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Which is an example of scarcity?", "o": ["\"Only two left!\"", "a free sweet", "a doctor's uniform"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What does a long queue outside a restaurant show?", "o": ["social proof", "reciprocity", "scarcity"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What is the difference between persuasion and manipulation?", "o": ["honesty", "price", "speed"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What does the writer suggest at the end?", "o": ["asking what is really persuading you", "never buying anything", "trusting every advert"], "a": 0}]}, "idioms": {"items": [["twist someone's arm", "To persuade someone to do something they don't want to do.", "يضغط على حد / يقنعه بالعافية", "OK, you've twisted my arm — I'll come to the party.", "خلاص، أقنعتني بالعافية — هاجي الحفلة."], ["sell like hot cakes", "To sell very quickly and in large numbers.", "يتباع زي الرز", "The new phones are selling like hot cakes.", "الموبايلات الجديدة بتتباع زي الرز."], ["bring someone round", "To persuade someone to change their opinion.", "يقنع حد يغير رأيه", "My dad didn't like the idea, but I brought him round.", "بابا مكانش عاجبه الفكرة، بس أقنعته يغير رأيه."], ["the hard sell", "A very forceful way of selling.", "البيع بالإلحاح", "I hate shops that give you the hard sell.", "بكره المحلات اللي بتبيعلك بالإلحاح."]], "quiz": [{"q": "The tickets ___ — they were gone in ten minutes!", "o": ["sold like hot cakes", "twisted my arm", "gave the hard sell", "brought round"], "a": 0}, {"q": "He didn't want to come, but I ___.", "o": ["twisted his arm", "sold like hot cakes", "gave a hard sell", "cake"], "a": 0}, {"q": "The salesman kept pushing me to buy. It was ___.", "o": ["the hard sell", "a hot cake", "an arm twist", "round"], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"Bring someone round\" means…", "o": ["persuade them to change their opinion", "invite them home", "drive them around", "wake them up"], "a": 0}]}, "phrasal": {"items": [["talk into", "To persuade someone to do something.", "يقنع حد يعمل حاجة", "She talked me into buying the expensive phone.", "أقنعتني أشتري الموبايل الغالي."], ["talk out of", "To persuade someone not to do something.", "يقنع حد ميعملش حاجة", "My friend talked me out of quitting my job.", "صاحبي أقنعني مسيبش شغلي."], ["come across", "To seem / give an impression.", "يبان / يدي انطباع", "You come across as very confident in your pitch.", "إنت بتبان واثق جدًا في العرض بتاعك."], ["fall for", "To be tricked into believing something.", "ينضحك عليه / يصدق", "Don't fall for those 'free gift' messages.", "متصدقش رسايل \"الهدية المجانية\" دي."]], "quiz": [{"q": "I didn't want to go, but my sister ___ me ___ it.", "o": ["talked / into", "fell / for", "came / across", "talked / out"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Many people ___ the fake advert and lost money.", "o": ["fell for", "talked into", "came across", "talked out of"], "a": 0}, {"q": "He was going to drop out, but his teacher ___ him ___ it.", "o": ["talked / out of", "fell / for", "talked / into", "came / across"], "a": 0}, {"q": "In interviews, try to ___ as calm and friendly.", "o": ["come across", "fall for", "talk into", "talk out"], "a": 0}]}, "slang": {"items": [["sold", "Completely convinced.", "اقتنعت خلاص", "\"It has free delivery?\" — \"Sold!\"", "\"والتوصيل ببلاش؟\" — \"اقتنعت!\"", "بهزار"], ["clickbait", "A title made only to make you click.", "عنوان خادع عشان تدوس", "\"You won't believe what happened next!\" — classic clickbait.", "\"مش هتصدق اللي حصل بعدها!\" — عنوان خادع كلاسيكي.", "منتشرة جدًا"], ["a steal", "Very cheap for its value.", "لُقطة", "This jacket was only 200 pounds — a steal!", "الجاكيت ده بـ٢٠٠ جنيه بس — لُقطة!", "عادي جدًا"], ["hype", "Excitement created around something.", "ضجة", "The film didn't live up to the hype.", "الفيلم مكانش على قد الضجة.", "منتشرة"], ["pitch it to me", "Explain your idea and why I should like it.", "اشرحلي فكرتك وأقنعني", "\"I have an idea for a business.\" — \"OK, pitch it to me.\"", "\"عندي فكرة مشروع.\" — \"يلا اشرحهالي وأقنعني.\"", "بين الصحاب والشغل"]], "quiz": [{"q": "A very cheap price for something great = ___.", "o": ["a steal", "clickbait", "hype", "sold"], "a": 0}, {"q": "A title like \"Doctors HATE this trick!\" is ___.", "o": ["clickbait", "a steal", "sold", "a pitch"], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"Free pizza with every ticket? Sold!\" means…", "o": ["I'm convinced!", "It's sold out.", "I sold it.", "I'm not interested."], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"It didn't live up to the hype.\" means it was…", "o": ["not as good as people said", "better than expected", "very cheap", "clickbait"], "a": 0}]}, "story": {"title": "The Last Lemonade", "ar": "آخر ليمونادة", "g": "m", "lines": [["Every summer, ten-year-old Nour sold lemonade outside her house. Most days, she sold about ten cups.", "كل صيف، نور اللي عندها ١٠ سنين كانت بتبيع ليمونادة قدام بيتها. أغلب الأيام، كانت بتبيع حوالي ١٠ أكواب."], ["One day, her uncle, a marketing manager, watched her for a while. \"What you need,\" he said, \"is a little persuasion.\"", "في يوم، خالها، مدير تسويق، اتفرج عليها شوية. \"اللي إنتي محتاجاه،\" قال، \"شوية إقناع.\""], ["First, he suggested giving every customer a free tiny cup to taste. \"People like to give back,\" he explained.", "الأول، اقترح تدي كل زبون كوباية صغيرة يدوقها ببلاش. \"الناس بتحب ترد الجميل،\" شرح."], ["Next, she changed her sign from \"Lemonade 10 pounds\" to \"Grandma's Secret Recipe — Only 20 cups a day!\"", "بعدين، غيرت اليافطة من \"ليمونادة بـ١٠ جنيه\" لـ\"وصفة تيتة السرية — ٢٠ كوباية بس في اليوم!\""], ["Then she asked her happy customers to stand and drink near the stand. Soon, there was a small queue.", "بعدين طلبت من زباينها المبسوطين يقفوا يشربوا جنب الكشك. بسرعة، بقى في طابور صغير."], ["It was the queue, more than the lemonade, that attracted more people.", "الطابور، أكتر من الليمونادة، هو اللي جذب ناس أكتر."], ["By noon, she had sold all twenty cups — and people were asking her to make more.", "مع الضهر، كانت باعت العشرين كوباية — والناس بتطلب منها تعمل أكتر."], ["But that evening, Nour felt something was wrong. \"Uncle, the recipe isn't really secret. It's just lemons and sugar.\"", "بس بالليل، نور حست إن في حاجة غلط. \"يا خالو، الوصفة مش سرية بجد. دي لمون وسكر بس.\""], ["Her uncle smiled proudly. \"Then tomorrow, tell them the truth. What makes a business last isn't clever tricks — it's trust.\"", "خالها ابتسم بفخر. \"يبقى بكرة قوليلهم الحقيقة. اللي بيخلي المشروع يعيش مش الحيل الذكية — هي الثقة.\""], ["The next day, her sign said: \"Simple, fresh and honest lemonade.\" She sold thirty cups.", "تاني يوم، اليافطة قالت: \"ليمونادة بسيطة وطازة وصادقة.\" وباعت ٣٠ كوباية."]], "quiz": [{"q": "How many cups did Nour usually sell?", "o": ["about ten", "about fifty", "none"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What did her uncle suggest first?", "o": ["giving a free taste", "lowering the price", "closing early"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What attracted more people, according to the story?", "o": ["the queue", "the price", "the music"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Why did Nour feel something was wrong?", "o": ["The recipe wasn't really secret.", "She was tired.", "The lemons were bad."], "a": 0}, {"q": "What did her uncle say makes a business last?", "o": ["trust", "clever tricks", "high prices"], "a": 0}]}, "challenge": {"title": "Convince Me!", "ar": "أقنعني! — جاوب وسجّل", "qs": ["Persuade me to visit your city. Use at least two cleft sentences.", "Describe an advert that you think is very persuasive. Why does it work?", "Is it ever acceptable to manipulate people? Explain.", "Sell me something on your desk in one minute.", "What is it that makes a speech powerful?", "Should influencers always say when they are paid to promote a product?", "Persuade your parents to let you go on a trip with friends.", "Have you ever fallen for a trick or a fake offer? What happened?", "What I need most in my life right now is… (explain)", "Which is more persuasive: facts, stories or famous people? Why?"]}, "games": {"pairs": [["🎯", "persuade"], ["🗣️", "rhetoric"], ["🏷️", "slogan"], ["⭐", "review"], ["🎤", "pitch"], ["🎬", "call to action"]], "spell": [["🤝", "convince"], ["💬", "argument"], ["📊", "evidence"], ["🧠", "logic"], ["🪤", "manipulate"], ["👁️", "audience"], ["📖", "storytelling"], ["🤞", "credible"]], "speed": [["What I need is more time.", true], ["What I need are time more.", false], ["It was a story that convinced me.", true], ["It was Ali who helped me.", true], ["It was Ali what helped me.", false], ["All I want is a chance.", true], ["What really persuades people is emotion.", true], ["The reason I called is to say thanks.", true], ["What investors want hear is a problem.", false], ["It's confidence that closes the deal.", true], ["Scarcity means something is rare or limited.", true], ["Manipulation is always honest.", false], ["\"Sell like hot cakes\" means to sell quickly.", true], ["\"Fall for\" means to be tricked.", true], ["\"A steal\" means very expensive.", false], ["A call to action tells people what to do next.", true]]}, "test": {"pass": 60, "sections": [{"id": "voc", "title": "Vocabulary", "ar": "المفردات", "icon": "📚", "qs": [{"q": "To make someone agree with you = to ___.", "o": ["persuade", "manipulate", "pause"], "a": 0, "pic": "🎯"}, {"q": "A short, catchy phrase used in ads = a ___.", "o": ["slogan", "pitch", "review"], "a": 0, "pic": "🏷️"}, {"q": "People who listen to a speech = the ___.", "o": ["audience", "evidence", "slide"], "a": 0, "pic": "👁️"}, {"q": "Believable and trustworthy = ___.", "o": ["credible", "emotional", "limited"], "a": 0, "pic": "🤞"}, {"q": "To control people in a dishonest way = to ___.", "o": ["manipulate", "engage", "convince"], "a": 0, "pic": "🪤"}, {"q": "\"إقناع\" in English is…", "o": ["persuasion", "permission", "pressure"], "a": 0, "say": "Choose the correct word."}]}, {"id": "gra", "title": "Grammar", "ar": "القواعد", "icon": "📘", "qs": [{"q": "___ I love about this city is the food.", "o": ["What", "That", "It"], "a": 0}, {"q": "It was my teacher ___ encouraged me.", "o": ["who", "what", "which"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What makes a good ad ___ a simple message.", "o": ["is", "are", "it is"], "a": 0}, {"q": "All I need ___ a good night's sleep.", "o": ["is", "are", "it"], "a": 0}, {"q": "It's the price ___ worries me, not the quality.", "o": ["that", "what", "where"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Which is correct?", "o": ["What I want is a fair chance.", "What I want it is a fair chance.", "That I want is a fair chance."], "a": 0}]}, {"id": "con", "title": "Conversation", "ar": "المحادثة", "icon": "💬", "qs": [{"q": "\"How should I start my pitch?\" — Best answer:", "o": ["With the problem you are solving.", "With a slide.", "Pitch is a field."], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"I'm so nervous I speak too fast.\" — Best answer:", "o": ["Pause after important points.", "Speak faster!", "Nervous is a feeling."], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"This jacket is only 150 pounds!\" — Best answer:", "o": ["That's a steal!", "That's clickbait!", "That's hype!"], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"Who helped you with the project?\" — Best answer:", "o": ["It was Omar who helped me.", "It was Omar what helped me.", "Omar was helping it."], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"OK, you've twisted my arm.\" means…", "o": ["I agree, even though I didn't want to.", "My arm hurts.", "I want to fight."], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"Free delivery and a gift?\" — Best answer:", "o": ["Sold!", "Steal!", "Hype!"], "a": 0}]}, {"id": "rea", "title": "Reading", "ar": "القراءة", "icon": "📖", "passage": ["A small café in Alexandria was struggling to attract customers.", "Then the owner put a sign outside: \"Only 30 croissants baked each morning.\"", "Within a week, there was a queue every morning. It was the limited number that made people want them.", "The owner also started giving a free mini cookie with every coffee. Customers began leaving bigger tips.", "What really made the difference, though, was quality — people came back because the croissants were excellent."], "qs": [{"q": "What was the café's problem?", "o": ["It was struggling to attract customers.", "It was too crowded.", "It had no coffee."], "a": 0}, {"q": "What did the sign say?", "o": ["Only 30 croissants baked each morning.", "Buy one, get one free.", "Closed on Fridays."], "a": 0}, {"q": "Which principle made people want the croissants?", "o": ["scarcity", "authority", "logic"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What happened after the free cookie?", "o": ["Customers left bigger tips.", "Customers complained.", "Prices went up."], "a": 0}, {"q": "What really made the difference?", "o": ["quality", "the sign", "the cookie"], "a": 0}]}, {"id": "wri", "title": "Writing", "ar": "الكتابة", "icon": "✍️", "writing": true, "prompt": "Write a persuasive advert or short speech (80–120 words) for a product, place or idea you believe in. Use at least three cleft sentences (What… is…, It is… that…, All… is…).", "promptAr": "اكتب إعلان أو خطاب إقناعي قصير (٨٠–١٢٠ كلمة) عن منتج أو مكان أو فكرة مؤمن بيها، واستخدم ٣ cleft sentences على الأقل.", "checks": [["🎯", "Persuasion words", "x", "\\b(you|your|need|best|try|imagine|offer|only|now|today|chance|why)\\b"], ["🔦", "What-cleft", "x", "\\bwhat\\s+[^.?!]*\\s+(is|was)\\s+"], ["🔦", "It-cleft", "x", "\\b(it is|it's|it was)\\s+[^.?!]*\\s+(that|who)\\s+"], ["💬", "At least 70 words", "len70"]]}]}, "watch": [{"yt": "K-Nps59NeBA", "title": "Rhetoric: How Persuasive Are You?", "ar": "البلاغة: إنت مقنع قد إيه؟ — 6 Minute English", "by": "BBC Learning English", "lines": [["Neil opens with a famous line from Shakespeare's Julius Caesar, spoken by Mark Antony to the crowd.", "نيل بيبدأ بجملة مشهورة من مسرحية يوليوس قيصر لشكسبير، قالها مارك أنطوني للجمهور."], ["Using words to persuade people to accept your argument is called rhetoric.", "إنك تستخدم الكلام عشان تقنع الناس يقبلوا حجتك اسمه البلاغة (rhetoric)."], ["Rhetoric began with the ancient Greek philosophers, and Roman politicians used it in speeches in the public square.", "البلاغة بدأت مع فلاسفة اليونان القدام، والسياسيين الرومان استخدموها في خطاباتهم في الساحات."], ["Modern politicians prefer social media, but they still use soundbites — short, memorable phrases.", "السياسيين النهارده بيفضلوا السوشيال ميديا، بس لسه بيستخدموا جمل قصيرة سهلة تتحفظ."], ["The quiz: what does the Roman phrase \"argumentum ad baculum\" mean?", "السؤال: العبارة الرومانية \"argumentum ad baculum\" معناها إيه؟"], ["A former advertising expert says rhetoric can simplify complex ideas, inspire people and influence opinion.", "خبير إعلانات سابق بيقول إن البلاغة ممكن تبسّط الأفكار المعقدة وتلهم الناس وتأثر على آرائهم."], ["It can rally people together — for example, when leaders described the coronavirus as an \"enemy\".", "ممكن تجمع الناس حوالين هدف — زي لما القادة وصفوا فيروس كورونا بإنه \"عدو\"."], ["But rhetoric can also pull the wool over people's eyes, making complicated issues sound too simple.", "بس البلاغة كمان ممكن تضحك على الناس، وتخلي المواضيع المعقدة تبان أبسط من الحقيقة."], ["A professor argues that tweets are too short for logical arguments, and hashtags can divide people into groups.", "بروفيسور بيقول إن التغريدات أقصر من إنها تحمل حجج منطقية، والهاشتاجات ممكن تقسّم الناس لمجموعات."], ["A logical argument starts from a premise — something accepted as true — and moves to a conclusion.", "الحجة المنطقية بتبدأ من مقدمة — حاجة متفق إنها صح — وتوصل لنتيجة."], ["Online debates are often polemical: people argue very strongly for or against an idea.", "النقاشات أونلاين غالبًا حادة: الناس بتجادل بقوة جدًا مع أو ضد فكرة."], ["The answer: \"argumentum ad baculum\" means an argument with a stick — persuading by force, not logic!", "الإجابة: \"argumentum ad baculum\" معناها حجة بالعصاية — إقناع بالقوة مش بالمنطق!"]], "words": ["rhetoric", "persuade", "argument", "philosophers", "soundbites", "influence", "rally", "pull the wool over", "logical", "premise", "conclusion", "polemical"], "quiz": [{"q": "What is rhetoric?", "o": ["using words to persuade people", "a kind of poem", "a Roman building"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Who started the art of rhetoric?", "o": ["ancient Greek philosophers", "modern politicians", "advertising companies"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What is a soundbite?", "o": ["a short, memorable phrase", "a long speech", "a loud noise"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What does \"pull the wool over someone's eyes\" mean?", "o": ["to trick or deceive them", "to keep them warm", "to help them see"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Why are tweets a problem for logical arguments, according to the professor?", "o": ["They are too short.", "They are too long.", "They are too formal."], "a": 0}, {"q": "What does \"argumentum ad baculum\" mean?", "o": ["an argument with a stick", "an argument based on logic", "an argument with friends"], "a": 0}]}]}, "5": {"n": 5, "title": "Privacy and Surveillance", "ar": "الخصوصية والمراقبة — Passive with Modals & Infinitives", "icon": "🔐", "cover": "img/b2p/u5.jpg", "intro": "اتكلم عن البيانات الشخصية والكاميرات والتطبيقات اللي بتراقبنا وإزاي نحمي خصوصيتنا، واستخدم المبني للمجهول مع الـ modals والـ infinitives: should be protected / can be tracked / don't want to be watched.", "videos": [{"id": "b2pv5", "title": "The App That Knew Too Much", "ar": "الأبلكيشن اللي عارف كتير — سلمى وعمر", "src": "video/b2p/u5v1.mp4", "poster": "img/b2p/u5v1.jpg", "sp": {"a": {"n": "Salma", "g": "f"}, "b": {"n": "Omar", "g": "m"}}, "lines": [["a", "Omar, this is creepy. I talked about running shoes yesterday, and now I see shoe adverts everywhere!", "عمر، ده مخيف. اتكلمت عن جزم الجري امبارح، ودلوقتي شايفة إعلانات جزم في كل حتة!"], ["b", "Your phone might be listening. Or your searches could have been tracked.", "ممكن موبايلك يكون بيسمع. أو عمليات البحث بتاعتك ممكن تكون اتراقبت."], ["a", "That's scary. I don't want to be watched all the time.", "ده مرعب. مش عايزة أبقى متراقبة طول الوقت."], ["b", "Let's check your settings. Look — this torch app has access to your location, contacts and microphone.", "خلينا نشوف الإعدادات. بصي — أبلكيشن الكشاف ده واخد صلاحية للموقع وجهات الاتصال والمايك."], ["a", "A torch app? Why would it need my contacts?", "أبلكيشن كشاف؟ ليه محتاج جهات الاتصال بتاعتي؟"], ["b", "It doesn't. Your data is probably being sold to advertisers. Permissions like this should be turned off.", "مش محتاج. بياناتك غالبًا بتتباع للمعلنين. الصلاحيات دي لازم تتقفل."], ["a", "I never read the terms and conditions. They're too long.", "أنا عمري ما بقرا الشروط والأحكام. طويلة جدًا."], ["b", "Nobody does! That's why laws must be introduced to protect users.", "محدش بيقراها! وعشان كده لازم قوانين تتعمل تحمي المستخدمين."], ["a", "But some surveillance is useful, isn't it? Criminals can be caught by CCTV.", "بس في مراقبة مفيدة، مش كده؟ المجرمين ممكن يتقبض عليهم بالكاميرات."], ["b", "True. Security is important. But our private information shouldn't be collected without our permission.", "صح. الأمان مهم. بس معلوماتنا الخاصة مينفعش تتجمع من غير إذننا."], ["a", "Agreed. OK — torch app deleted, location turned off. I feel better already.", "موافقة. تمام — أبلكيشن الكشاف اتمسح، والموقع اتقفل. حاسة إني أحسن خلاص."], ["b", "And use stronger passwords! Your password is your birthday, isn't it?", "واستخدمي باسوردات أقوى! الباسورد بتاعك هو عيد ميلادك، صح؟"], ["a", "…It's being changed right now!", "…بيتغير حالًا!"]], "quiz": [{"q": "What is creepy, according to Salma?", "o": ["She sees shoe adverts after talking about shoes.", "Her phone broke.", "Someone called her at night."], "a": 0}, {"q": "What does the torch app have access to?", "o": ["location, contacts and microphone", "only the camera", "nothing"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What does Omar think is happening to her data?", "o": ["It is probably being sold to advertisers.", "It is being deleted.", "It is safe."], "a": 0}, {"q": "What does Salma admit?", "o": ["She never reads the terms and conditions.", "She hates technology.", "She uses no passwords."], "a": 0}, {"q": "What is Salma's password?", "o": ["her birthday", "her name", "her pet's name"], "a": 0}], "fill": [[0, "creepy"], [0, "adverts"], [1, "could have been tracked"], [2, "to be watched"], [3, "access"], [3, "location"], [5, "is probably being sold"], [5, "should be turned off"], [6, "terms and conditions"], [7, "must be introduced"], [8, "can be caught"], [9, "shouldn't be collected"], [9, "permission"], [12, "being changed"]]}], "vocab": [{"t": "Privacy", "ar": "الخصوصية", "items": [["🔐", "privacy", "Everyone has a right to privacy."], ["📂", "personal data", "Companies collect our personal data."], ["✅", "permission", "Ask for permission before taking photos."], ["⚙️", "settings", "Check your privacy settings."], ["📍", "location", "Turn off your location when you don't need it."], ["📜", "terms and conditions", "Nobody reads the terms and conditions."], ["🔑", "password", "Use a strong password."], ["🛡️", "secure", "Is this website secure?"]]}, {"t": "Surveillance", "ar": "المراقبة", "items": [["📹", "surveillance", "Surveillance cameras are everywhere."], ["👁️", "monitor", "The company monitors employees' emails."], ["📡", "track", "Apps can track your location."], ["🧑‍💻", "hacker", "A hacker stole thousands of passwords."], ["🧾", "data breach", "The bank had a serious data breach."], ["😨", "creepy", "It's creepy when ads know too much."], ["🗃️", "collect", "The app collects data about your habits."], ["🎭", "identity theft", "Identity theft is a growing crime."]]}, {"t": "Protection & rights", "ar": "الحماية والحقوق", "items": [["⚖️", "regulation", "New regulations protect online users."], ["🔏", "encrypt", "Messages are encrypted for safety."], ["🙅", "opt out", "You can opt out of marketing emails."], ["🧱", "firewall", "A firewall blocks dangerous connections."], ["🕵️", "anonymous", "You can stay anonymous online."], ["📢", "consent", "They used my data without my consent."], ["🚨", "scam", "Don't click links in scam messages."], ["🧠", "digital footprint", "Think about your digital footprint."]]}], "talk": [{"title": "Let's Talk · Student A", "ar": "الطالب A", "list": [["Do you read the terms and conditions before you accept them?", "بتقرا الشروط والأحكام قبل ما توافق؟", "Honestly, never."], ["How many apps on your phone know your location?", "كام أبلكيشن على موبايلك عارف مكانك؟", "Probably too many!"], ["Have you ever felt that an app was listening to you?", "حسيت قبل كده إن أبلكيشن بيسمعك؟", "Yes, after I talked about holidays."], ["Should parents be allowed to read their children's messages?", "الأهل ينفع يقروا رسايل أولادهم؟", "Only if there is a real danger."], ["How do you keep your passwords safe?", "بتحافظ على باسورداتك إزاي؟", "I use a password manager."]]}, {"title": "Let's Talk · Student B", "ar": "الطالب B", "list": [["Are CCTV cameras in streets a good idea?", "كاميرات الشوارع فكرة كويسة؟", "Yes, but they should be controlled by law."], ["Should companies be allowed to sell our data?", "الشركات ينفع تبيع بياناتنا؟", "Not without our clear consent."], ["Would you give up some privacy for more security?", "تتنازل عن شوية خصوصية مقابل أمان أكتر؟", "A little, maybe."], ["What information should never be shared online?", "إيه المعلومات اللي متتشاركش أونلاين أبدًا؟", "Your address and bank details."], ["Is it possible to be completely private today?", "ممكن تبقى خصوصيتك كاملة النهارده؟", "Not really, but we can reduce the risks."]]}], "grammar": {"title": "Passive with Modals & Infinitives", "ar": "المبني للمجهول مع الـ modals والـ infinitive", "blocks": [{"type": "intro", "en": "We use the passive when the action is more important than the person who does it. At B2+, we combine the passive with modals (can, should, must, might…) and with infinitives (to be done) and gerunds (being done).", "ar": "بنستخدم المبني للمجهول لما الفعل أهم من اللي عمله. في B2+ بنجمع المبني للمجهول مع الـ modals ومع to be done و being done."}, {"type": "big", "items": [{"v": "modal + be + p.p.", "p": "present / future passive", "c": 1, "eg": ["Permissions like this should be turned off.", "Criminals can be caught by CCTV.", "New laws must be introduced."]}, {"v": "modal + have been + p.p.", "p": "past passive", "c": 2, "eg": ["Your searches could have been tracked.", "The data might have been stolen.", "This should have been reported earlier."]}, {"v": "to be + p.p. / being + p.p.", "p": "infinitive & gerund passive", "c": 3, "eg": ["I don't want to be watched all the time.", "Nobody likes being tracked.", "Our data needs to be protected."]}]}, {"type": "table", "title": "📋 Active → Passive", "head": ["Active", "Passive"], "rows": [["They should protect our data.", "Our data should be protected."], ["Someone might have hacked the account.", "The account might have been hacked."], ["People can track your phone.", "Your phone can be tracked."], ["I hate it when people watch me.", "I hate being watched."], ["They need to change the law.", "The law needs to be changed."]]}, {"type": "uses", "title": "💡 Common uses", "ar": "استخدامات شائعة", "items": [["📜", "rules & advice", "Passwords must not be shared.", "قواعد"], ["🔮", "possibility", "Your data may be sold.", "احتمال"], ["🕰️", "past possibility", "The email could have been read.", "احتمال في الماضي"], ["😟", "feelings", "I hate being followed online.", "مشاعر"]]}, {"type": "tip", "en": "After a modal, always use 'be' (base form): should is protected ✖ → should be protected ✔. After 'want', 'need', 'expect' use 'to be + p.p.'; after 'like', 'hate', 'avoid' use 'being + p.p.'.", "ar": "بعد الـ modal استخدم be: should be protected. وبعد want / need استخدم to be + p.p.، وبعد like / hate / avoid استخدم being + p.p."}]}, "exercises": [{"type": "mcq", "title": "Passive with Modals — 10 MCQs", "ar": "اختار الصح", "speak": true, "items": [{"q": "Permissions like this ___ off.", "o": ["should be turned", "should turned", "should be turn", "should turning"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Criminals ___ by CCTV.", "o": ["can be caught", "can caught", "can be catch", "can catching"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Your searches ___ tracked.", "o": ["could have been", "could been", "could have be", "could be have"], "a": 0}, {"q": "I don't want ___ all the time.", "o": ["to be watched", "being watch", "to watched", "be watched"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Nobody likes ___.", "o": ["being tracked", "to tracked", "be tracked", "been tracked"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Our data needs ___.", "o": ["to be protected", "to protect", "being protect", "protected be"], "a": 0}, {"q": "New laws ___ to protect users.", "o": ["must be introduced", "must introduced", "must be introduce", "must introducing"], "a": 0}, {"q": "The account ___ hacked last night.", "o": ["might have been", "might be have", "might been", "might have be"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Which sentence is correct?", "o": ["Passwords must not be shared.", "Passwords must not shared.", "Passwords must be not share.", "Passwords not must be shared."], "a": 0}, {"q": "Active: \"They should have told us.\" → Passive: \"We ___.\"", "o": ["should have been told", "should be told have", "should have told", "should been told"], "a": 0}]}, {"type": "mcq", "title": "to be or being?", "ar": "to be ولا being؟", "items": [{"q": "I hate ___ photographed without permission.", "o": ["being", "to be"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Everyone wants ___ respected.", "o": ["to be", "being"], "a": 0}, {"q": "The report needs ___ checked.", "o": ["to be", "being"], "a": 0}, {"q": "She avoids ___ seen in public.", "o": ["being", "to be"], "a": 0}, {"q": "modal + ___ + p.p.", "o": ["be", "being"], "a": 0}]}, {"type": "ord", "title": "Make sentences", "ar": "رتّب الكلمات", "items": [{"c": ["Our data", "should be", "protected", "by law"], "a": [0, 1, 2, 3]}, {"c": ["The account", "might have been", "hacked", "last night"], "a": [0, 1, 2, 3]}, {"c": ["I", "don't want", "to be", "watched"], "a": [0, 1, 2, 3]}, {"c": ["Nobody", "likes", "being", "tracked"], "a": [0, 1, 2, 3]}]}], "reading": {"title": "The Price of Free", "ar": "تمن الحاجة الببلاش", "g": "m", "lines": [["Most of the apps we use every day — social networks, search engines, maps — are completely free. Or are they?", "أغلب الأبلكيشنات اللي بنستخدمها كل يوم — السوشيال ميديا ومحركات البحث والخرايط — ببلاش تمامًا. ولا مش كده؟"], ["There is a famous saying in the technology industry: \"If you're not paying for the product, you are the product.\"", "في مقولة مشهورة في صناعة التكنولوجيا: \"لو مش بتدفع تمن المنتج، يبقى إنت المنتج.\""], ["Instead of money, these services are paid for with our personal data: what we search for, where we go, what we buy and even how long we look at a photo.", "بدل الفلوس، الخدمات دي بتتدفع ببياناتنا الشخصية: بندور على إيه، وبنروح فين، وبنشتري إيه، وحتى بنبص على صورة قد إيه."], ["This information can be analysed by powerful algorithms and sold to advertisers, who use it to show us highly targeted ads.", "المعلومات دي ممكن تتحلل بخوارزميات قوية وتتباع للمعلنين، اللي بيستخدموها عشان يورونا إعلانات موجهة جدًا."], ["Many people say they have \"nothing to hide\". However, privacy experts warn that data can be used in ways we never expected.", "ناس كتير بيقولوا \"معنديش حاجة أخبيها\". لكن خبراء الخصوصية بيحذروا إن البيانات ممكن تتستخدم بطرق عمرنا ما توقعناها."], ["It might be used to decide the price we pay for insurance, whether we get a loan, or even which job adverts we are shown.", "ممكن تتستخدم عشان تحدد السعر اللي بندفعه للتأمين، أو إذا كنا هناخد قرض، أو حتى أنهي إعلانات وظايف بتظهرلنا."], ["Data breaches are another danger. In recent years, the personal details of hundreds of millions of users have been stolen by hackers.", "تسريب البيانات خطر تاني. في السنين الأخيرة، البيانات الشخصية لمئات الملايين من المستخدمين اتسرقت على إيد الهاكرز."], ["Some governments have responded with new laws. In Europe, for example, companies must now ask for clear consent before personal data is collected.", "بعض الحكومات ردت بقوانين جديدة. في أوروبا مثلًا، الشركات لازم دلوقتي تاخد موافقة واضحة قبل ما البيانات الشخصية تتجمع."], ["But laws cannot do everything. Experts say users should also be educated about privacy settings, strong passwords and the risks of over-sharing.", "بس القوانين مش هتعمل كل حاجة. الخبراء بيقولوا إن المستخدمين لازم كمان يتعلموا عن إعدادات الخصوصية والباسوردات القوية ومخاطر المشاركة الزايدة."], ["After all, privacy is not about having something to hide. It is about having something to protect.", "في الآخر، الخصوصية مش إن عندك حاجة تخبيها. هي إن عندك حاجة تحميها."]], "keys": [["🔍", "search engine", "a website that helps you find information online"], ["🎯", "targeted ads", "adverts chosen for a specific person"], ["🙈", "nothing to hide", "having no secrets"], ["💳", "loan", "money borrowed from a bank"], ["🧾", "data breach", "when private data is stolen or leaked"], ["📢", "over-sharing", "sharing too much personal information"]], "quiz": [{"q": "What does \"If you're not paying for the product, you are the product\" mean?", "o": ["Free services are paid for with our data.", "All apps are expensive.", "Users make apps."], "a": 0}, {"q": "What happens to our data, according to the text?", "o": ["It can be analysed and sold to advertisers.", "It is always deleted.", "Nobody uses it."], "a": 0}, {"q": "What do privacy experts warn?", "o": ["Data can be used in unexpected ways.", "People have nothing to hide.", "Apps are always safe."], "a": 0}, {"q": "What could data be used to decide?", "o": ["insurance prices or loans", "the weather", "school holidays"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What must companies in Europe do now?", "o": ["ask for clear consent", "stop using the internet", "give users money"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What is privacy about, according to the last line?", "o": ["having something to protect", "having something to hide", "being alone"], "a": 0}]}, "idioms": {"items": [["Big Brother is watching", "Someone powerful is watching everything you do.", "في حد بيراقبك", "Cameras on every corner — Big Brother is watching!", "كاميرات في كل ركن — في حد بيراقبنا!"], ["keep something under wraps", "To keep something secret.", "يخبّي حاجة / يخليها سر", "The company kept the data breach under wraps for months.", "الشركة خبّت تسريب البيانات شهور."], ["let the cat out of the bag", "To reveal a secret by mistake.", "يفشي السر بالغلط", "I let the cat out of the bag about the surprise party.", "فشيت سر الحفلة المفاجأة بالغلط."], ["an open book", "A person who hides nothing about themselves.", "كتاب مفتوح", "My sister is an open book — she posts everything online.", "أختي كتاب مفتوح — بتنزل كل حاجة أونلاين."]], "quiz": [{"q": "He tells everyone everything about his life. He's ___.", "o": ["an open book", "under wraps", "Big Brother", "a cat"], "a": 0}, {"q": "The new product is secret. Keep it ___.", "o": ["under wraps", "an open book", "out of the bag", "watching"], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"Let the cat out of the bag\" means…", "o": ["reveal a secret by mistake", "free a pet", "go shopping", "tell a lie"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Every website tracks you. ___!", "o": ["Big Brother is watching", "An open book", "Under wraps", "Out of the bag"], "a": 0}]}, "phrasal": {"items": [["log in / log out", "To enter / leave an account.", "يدخل / يخرج من الحساب", "Always log out on shared computers.", "دايمًا اعمل log out من الكمبيوترات المشتركة."], ["hack into", "To enter a computer system illegally.", "يخترق", "Someone hacked into the school's system.", "حد اخترق نظام المدرسة."], ["turn off", "To stop a function or device.", "يقفل", "Turn off location tracking.", "اقفل تتبع الموقع."], ["give away", "To reveal information, often by mistake.", "يكشف / يفضح معلومة", "Your photos can give away where you live.", "صورك ممكن تكشف إنت ساكن فين."]], "quiz": [{"q": "Criminals ___ the bank's computers.", "o": ["hacked into", "logged out", "turned off", "gave away"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Don't forget to ___ of your email at the library.", "o": ["log out", "hack into", "give away", "turn off"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Posting your ticket photo can ___ your flight details.", "o": ["give away", "log in", "hack into", "turn off"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Please ___ the microphone permission for this app.", "o": ["turn off", "hack into", "give away", "log out"], "a": 0}]}, "slang": {"items": [["creepy", "Strange in a way that makes you uncomfortable.", "مخيف / بيقلق", "It's creepy how ads follow me around.", "حاجة مخيفة إزاي الإعلانات بتمشي ورايا.", "عادي جدًا"], ["stalk", "To look at someone's social media a lot (informal).", "يراقب حساب حد كتير", "I may have stalked his Instagram before the date.", "يمكن كنت براقب الإنستجرام بتاعه قبل الميعاد.", "بهزار — بس المراقبة الحقيقية جريمة"], ["finsta", "A secret, private Instagram account.", "حساب إنستجرام سري", "She posts funny stuff on her finsta for close friends only.", "بتنزل حاجات مضحكة على حسابها السري للصحاب القريبين بس.", "من لغة المراهقين"], ["TMI", "Too Much Information.", "معلومات أكتر من اللازم", "\"I had a stomach ache all night…\" — \"TMI!\"", "\"بطني كانت بتوجعني طول الليل…\" — \"معلومات زيادة!\"", "بهزار"], ["ghost mode", "Hiding your location or activity online.", "وضع الاختفاء", "I put my map on ghost mode.", "خليت الخريطة على وضع الاختفاء.", "من سناب شات"]], "quiz": [{"q": "A secret Instagram account = a ___.", "o": ["finsta", "ghost", "TMI", "stalk"], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"TMI\" stands for…", "o": ["Too Much Information", "Tell Me Instantly", "The Main Idea", "Time Means It"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Hiding your location on an app = ___.", "o": ["ghost mode", "finsta", "creepy", "TMI"], "a": 0}, {"q": "It feels ___ when a stranger knows your name.", "o": ["creepy", "finsta", "TMI", "ghost"], "a": 0}]}, "story": {"title": "The Photo", "ar": "الصورة", "g": "f", "lines": [["Laila was excited about her first trip abroad. Before leaving, she posted a photo of her boarding pass with the caption \"Paris, here I come!\"", "ليلى كانت متحمسة لأول سفرية ليها برة. قبل ما تمشي، نزّلت صورة كارت الصعود للطيارة وكتبت \"باريس، أنا جاية!\""], ["She didn't notice that the barcode on the pass could be read by anyone.", "مخدتش بالها إن الباركود اللي على الكارت ممكن أي حد يقراه."], ["Two hours later, she received an email: her flight had been changed and her seat had been cancelled.", "بعد ساعتين، جالها إيميل: رحلتها اتغيرت ومقعدها اتلغى."], ["Panicking, she called the airline. \"Someone logged into your booking and changed it,\" the agent explained. \"Your details must have been taken from the internet.\"", "وهي مرعوبة، كلمت شركة الطيران. \"حد دخل على الحجز بتاعك وغيّره،\" الموظف شرح. \"بياناتك أكيد اتاخدت من الإنترنت.\""], ["Luckily, the problem was solved before her flight, but Laila had learned an important lesson.", "لحسن الحظ، المشكلة اتحلت قبل رحلتها، بس ليلى اتعلمت درس مهم."], ["In Paris, she was careful. She turned off her location and posted photos only after she had left each place.", "في باريس، كانت حريصة. قفلت الموقع ونزّلت الصور بس بعد ما سابت كل مكان."], ["When she got home, she checked every app on her phone. Seventeen of them had access to her location!", "لما رجعت البيت، راجعت كل أبلكيشن على موبايلها. ١٧ منهم كان عندهم صلاحية للموقع!"], ["She deleted half of them and changed all her passwords — not one of them was her birthday anymore.", "مسحت نصهم وغيرت كل الباسوردات — ولا واحد فيهم بقى عيد ميلادها."], ["Then she gave a short talk at her university about online privacy. \"I don't want other people to be hacked like I was,\" she said.", "بعدين قدمت محاضرة قصيرة في جامعتها عن الخصوصية أونلاين. \"مش عايزة ناس تانية تتهكر زيي،\" قالت."], ["Her final slide said: \"Share your memories — not your information.\"", "آخر سلايد كان مكتوب فيه: \"شارك ذكرياتك — مش معلوماتك.\""]], "quiz": [{"q": "What did Laila post?", "o": ["a photo of her boarding pass", "a photo of her house", "her passport number"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What could be read by anyone?", "o": ["the barcode", "her diary", "her emails"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What happened two hours later?", "o": ["Her flight was changed and her seat cancelled.", "She won a prize.", "She missed the plane."], "a": 0}, {"q": "How many apps had access to her location?", "o": ["seventeen", "seven", "seventy"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What did her final slide say?", "o": ["Share your memories — not your information.", "Never travel abroad.", "Delete all apps."], "a": 0}]}, "challenge": {"title": "Who's Watching You?", "ar": "مين بيراقبك؟ — جاوب وسجّل", "qs": ["What personal information do you think should never be shared online?", "Should CCTV cameras be put in every classroom? Why or why not?", "Describe a time when you felt your privacy was not respected.", "What rules should be introduced to protect children online?", "Would you accept being tracked by your employer during working hours?", "Should governments be allowed to read private messages to stop crime?", "How can people be protected from scams and hackers?", "Is it OK for parents to post photos of their children online?", "What could happen if your password were stolen?", "Is privacy more or less important than security?"]}, "games": {"pairs": [["🔐", "privacy"], ["📹", "surveillance"], ["🧑‍💻", "hacker"], ["🔏", "encrypt"], ["📢", "consent"], ["🚨", "scam"]], "spell": [["📂", "personal data"], ["✅", "permission"], ["📍", "location"], ["🔑", "password"], ["🛡️", "secure"], ["📡", "track"], ["👁️", "monitor"], ["🕵️", "anonymous"]], "speed": [["Our data should be protected.", true], ["Our data should protected.", false], ["Criminals can be caught by CCTV.", true], ["The account might have been hacked.", true], ["The account might been hacked.", false], ["I don't want to be watched.", true], ["Nobody likes to being tracked.", false], ["The law needs to be changed.", true], ["Passwords must not be shared.", true], ["It should have been reported earlier.", true], ["A data breach is when private data is stolen.", true], ["Consent means doing something without permission.", false], ["\"Let the cat out of the bag\" means to reveal a secret.", true], ["\"Hack into\" means to enter a system illegally.", true], ["\"TMI\" means Too Much Information.", true], ["An \"open book\" keeps everything secret.", false]]}, "test": {"pass": 60, "sections": [{"id": "voc", "title": "Vocabulary", "ar": "المفردات", "icon": "📚", "qs": [{"q": "Watching people, often with cameras = ___.", "o": ["surveillance", "consent", "privacy"], "a": 0, "pic": "📹"}, {"q": "Someone who breaks into computer systems = a ___.", "o": ["hacker", "monitor", "firewall"], "a": 0, "pic": "🧑‍💻"}, {"q": "Agreement / permission = ___.", "o": ["consent", "breach", "scam"], "a": 0, "pic": "📢"}, {"q": "A trick to steal money = a ___.", "o": ["scam", "setting", "regulation"], "a": 0, "pic": "🚨"}, {"q": "To follow where something goes = to ___.", "o": ["track", "encrypt", "opt out"], "a": 0, "pic": "📡"}, {"q": "\"الخصوصية\" in English is…", "o": ["privacy", "private", "priority"], "a": 0, "say": "Choose the correct word."}]}, {"id": "gra", "title": "Grammar", "ar": "القواعد", "icon": "📘", "qs": [{"q": "Personal data ___ without consent.", "o": ["shouldn't be collected", "shouldn't collected", "shouldn't be collect"], "a": 0}, {"q": "The files ___ stolen yesterday.", "o": ["might have been", "might be", "might been"], "a": 0}, {"q": "I hate ___ photographed.", "o": ["being", "to be", "be"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Our privacy needs ___.", "o": ["to be respected", "to respect", "being respect"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Your phone ___ from anywhere.", "o": ["can be tracked", "can tracked", "can be track"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Which is correct?", "o": ["The rules must be followed.", "The rules must followed.", "The rules must be follow."], "a": 0}]}, {"id": "con", "title": "Conversation", "ar": "المحادثة", "icon": "💬", "qs": [{"q": "\"Why do I see ads for things I just talked about?\" — Best answer:", "o": ["Your data might be tracked by apps.", "Ads are colourful.", "You talk a lot."], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"Should I accept all permissions?\" — Best answer:", "o": ["No, unnecessary ones should be turned off.", "Yes, always.", "Permissions are nice."], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"My password is my birthday.\" — Best answer:", "o": ["That's not safe. It should be changed.", "Happy birthday!", "Great password!"], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"I don't like being watched.\" — Best answer:", "o": ["Me neither. Privacy matters.", "Watch a film.", "I am watching."], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"I had a terrible stomach ache…\" — Best answer (joking):", "o": ["TMI!", "Ghost mode!", "Finsta!"], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"I told everyone about the surprise party by mistake.\" — Best answer:", "o": ["Oh no, you let the cat out of the bag!", "You are an open book.", "Big Brother!"], "a": 0}]}, {"id": "rea", "title": "Reading", "ar": "القراءة", "icon": "📖", "passage": ["Last year, a popular fitness app had a serious data breach.", "The names, addresses and running routes of millions of users were stolen.", "Experts said the problem could have been avoided if the data had been encrypted.", "The company apologised and promised that stronger security would be introduced.", "Users were advised to change their passwords and to turn off location sharing."], "qs": [{"q": "What kind of app had a data breach?", "o": ["a fitness app", "a game", "a bank app"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What was stolen?", "o": ["names, addresses and running routes", "only emails", "money"], "a": 0}, {"q": "How could the problem have been avoided?", "o": ["if the data had been encrypted", "if the app had been free", "if users had run less"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What did the company promise?", "o": ["stronger security", "free shoes", "to close the app"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What were users advised to do?", "o": ["change passwords and turn off location sharing", "delete their phones", "stop running"], "a": 0}]}, {"id": "wri", "title": "Writing", "ar": "الكتابة", "icon": "✍️", "writing": true, "prompt": "Write a short guide (80–120 words): \"How to protect your privacy online\". Use at least four passive structures with modals or infinitives (should be…, must be…, can be…, need to be…).", "promptAr": "اكتب دليل قصير (٨٠–١٢٠ كلمة): \"إزاي تحمي خصوصيتك أونلاين\". استخدم ٤ تراكيب مبني للمجهول على الأقل مع modals أو infinitives.", "checks": [["🔐", "Privacy words", "x", "\\b(privacy|private|data|password|passwords|location|app|apps|online|hacker|hackers|secure|settings|permission)\\b"], ["🔒", "Modal passive", "x", "\\b(should|must|can|could|may|might|need to|needs to|shouldn't|mustn't|can't)\\s+(not\\s+)?be\\s+\\w+(ed|en|wn|lt|ght|ne)\\b"], ["🔁", "to be / being + p.p.", "x", "\\b(to be|being)\\s+\\w+(ed|en|wn|lt|ght)\\b"], ["💬", "At least 70 words", "len70"]]}]}, "watch": [{"yt": "Z2xcl93o7F0", "title": "Can We Trust a Smart Speaker?", "ar": "نثق في السماعات الذكية؟ — 6 Minute English", "by": "BBC Learning English", "lines": [["Rob doesn't answer a phone call because he doesn't like the idea of someone eavesdropping on him.", "روب مش بيرد على مكالمة عشان مش حابب فكرة إن حد يتصنت عليه."], ["But Rob has a smart speaker at home. It answers questions, reads the news and plays music with a voice command.", "بس روب عنده سماعة ذكية في البيت. بترد على الأسئلة وتقرا الأخبار وتشغّل مزيكا بأمر صوتي."], ["Dan asks: if it can always hear you, how do you know it isn't listening to everything?", "دان بيسأل: لو هي سامعاك طول الوقت، إزاي تعرف إنها مش بتسمع كل حاجة؟"], ["The quiz: by what percentage did the number of smart speakers in US homes grow in one year?", "السؤال: عدد السماعات الذكية في البيوت الأمريكية زاد بنسبة كام في سنة واحدة؟"], ["A privacy expert says people are putting a kind of bug — a hidden listening device — in their homes.", "خبير خصوصية بيقول إن الناس بيحطوا نوع من أجهزة التصنت المستخبية في بيوتهم."], ["And it is in our most intimate space — the private, personal place where we live.", "وفي أكتر مكان خاص بينا — المكان الشخصي اللي عايشين فيه."], ["Companies say the speaker only listens after the wake word, but the microphone is on the whole time.", "الشركات بتقول إن السماعة بتسمع بس بعد كلمة التشغيل، بس المايك شغال طول الوقت."], ["It's also unclear whether a government could circumvent the security and listen in without permission.", "ومش واضح كمان إذا كانت حكومة ممكن تتحايل على الحماية وتسمع من غير إذن."], ["So why are smart speakers so popular? Research shows people accept the risk in exchange for convenience.", "طيب ليه السماعات الذكية منتشرة كده؟ الأبحاث بتقول إن الناس بتقبل المخاطرة مقابل الراحة."], ["People are resigned to the privacy trade-off: they accept something unpleasant that they feel they cannot change.", "الناس مستسلمين لمقايضة الخصوصية: بيقبلوا حاجة مش لطيفة حاسين إنهم مش قادرين يغيروها."], ["Dan adds that data companies already have so much of our data that a speaker may not matter much.", "دان بيضيف إن شركات البيانات عندها بياناتنا أصلًا لدرجة إن السماعة يمكن متفرقش كتير."], ["The answer: about 80% — from around 66 million to 118 million smart speakers in one year.", "الإجابة: حوالي ٨٠٪ — من حوالي ٦٦ مليون لـ١١٨ مليون سماعة ذكية في سنة."]], "words": ["eavesdropping", "smart speaker", "voice command", "percentage", "bug", "intimate", "microphone", "circumvent", "permission", "convenience", "resigned", "trade-off"], "quiz": [{"q": "Why doesn't Rob answer the call?", "o": ["He doesn't like the idea of someone eavesdropping.", "He is busy.", "His phone is broken."], "a": 0}, {"q": "What is a \"bug\" in this programme?", "o": ["a hidden listening device", "an insect", "a computer error"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What does \"intimate\" mean?", "o": ["private and personal", "very large", "public"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What is always on, according to the expert?", "o": ["the microphone", "the camera", "the music"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Why do people still use smart speakers?", "o": ["They accept the privacy risk for convenience.", "They are free.", "They are required by law."], "a": 0}, {"q": "By how much did smart speakers grow in US homes?", "o": ["about 80%", "about 40%", "about 10%"], "a": 0}]}]}, "6": {"n": 6, "title": "Gender Roles and Equality", "ar": "أدوار الرجل والست والمساواة — Participle Clauses", "icon": "⚖️", "cover": "img/b2p/u6.jpg", "intro": "ناقش أدوار الرجالة والستات في البيت والشغل والمجتمع، وإزاي الأدوار دي بتتغير، بأسلوب محترم يسمع كل الآراء، واستخدم الـ Participle Clauses عشان تكتب جمل مختصرة وراقية: Having finished… / Raised in… / Working full-time…", "videos": [{"id": "b2pv6", "title": "Who Does What?", "ar": "مين بيعمل إيه؟ — سارة وحسن", "src": "video/b2p/u6v1.mp4", "poster": "img/b2p/u6v1.jpg", "sp": {"a": {"n": "Sara", "g": "f"}, "b": {"n": "Hassan", "g": "m"}}, "lines": [["b", "Sara, congratulations on the new job! How are you managing everything?", "سارة، مبروك الشغل الجديد! بتعرفي توفقي بين كل حاجة إزاي؟"], ["a", "Thanks! Honestly, it's not easy. Working full-time and looking after the kids, I'm always tired.", "شكرًا! بصراحة مش سهل. وأنا شغالة دوام كامل وبراعي الأولاد، دايمًا تعبانة."], ["b", "Doesn't your husband help at home?", "جوزك مش بيساعد في البيت؟"], ["a", "He does now. Having seen how exhausted I was, he started cooking twice a week.", "بيساعد دلوقتي. بعد ما شاف قد إيه أنا مرهقة، بدأ يطبخ مرتين في الأسبوع."], ["b", "That's great. My father never cooked. Raised in a traditional family, he thought the kitchen was only for women.", "ده حلو. أبويا عمره ما طبخ. ولأنه اتربى في عيلة تقليدية، كان فاكر إن المطبخ للستات بس."], ["a", "Times have changed, though. Many young men today share housework without thinking twice.", "بس الزمن اتغير. شباب كتير النهارده بيشاركوا في شغل البيت من غير ما يفكروا مرتين."], ["b", "True. And at work? Do you think women and men have equal opportunities now?", "صح. وفي الشغل؟ شايفة إن الستات والرجالة عندهم فرص متساوية دلوقتي؟"], ["a", "Better than before, but not completely. Looking at our company, most managers are still men.", "أحسن من الأول، بس مش تمامًا. لو بصيت على شركتنا، أغلب المديرين لسه رجالة."], ["b", "Interesting. On the other hand, in my field — nursing — most of my colleagues are women. Some people find it strange that I'm a male nurse.", "مثير. من ناحية تانية، في مجالي — التمريض — أغلب زمايلي ستات. في ناس بيستغربوا إني ممرض راجل."], ["a", "That shows stereotypes affect men too. People should choose jobs based on talent, not gender.", "ده بيوضح إن الصور النمطية بتأثر على الرجالة كمان. الناس لازم تختار شغلها على حسب موهبتها، مش جنسها."], ["b", "Exactly. Respecting each other's choices, families and workplaces can only become stronger.", "بالظبط. لما نحترم اختيارات بعض، العيلات وأماكن الشغل هتبقى أقوى."], ["a", "Well said! Now, having finished my coffee, I have to go and pick up the kids!", "كلام جميل! ودلوقتي، بعد ما خلصت قهوتي، لازم أروح أجيب الأولاد!"]], "quiz": [{"q": "Why is Sara always tired?", "o": ["She works full-time and looks after the kids.", "She doesn't sleep.", "She studies at night."], "a": 0}, {"q": "What did her husband start doing?", "o": ["cooking twice a week", "working from home", "nothing"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Why didn't Hassan's father cook?", "o": ["He was raised in a traditional family.", "He was too busy.", "He couldn't cook."], "a": 0}, {"q": "What is Hassan's job?", "o": ["nurse", "manager", "teacher"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What does Sara think people should base job choices on?", "o": ["talent, not gender", "money only", "their parents' jobs"], "a": 0}], "fill": [[1, "Working full-time"], [2, "help at home"], [3, "Having seen"], [3, "exhausted"], [4, "Raised in a traditional family"], [5, "share"], [6, "equal opportunities"], [7, "Looking at our company"], [8, "male nurse"], [9, "stereotypes"], [9, "gender"], [10, "Respecting each other's choices"]]}], "vocab": [{"t": "Gender & roles", "ar": "الجنس والأدوار", "items": [["⚖️", "equality", "Gender equality is a global goal."], ["🚻", "gender", "Jobs should not depend on gender."], ["👨‍👩‍👧", "gender roles", "Traditional gender roles are changing."], ["🧠", "stereotype", "It's a stereotype that boys don't cry."], ["🏠", "housework", "They share the housework equally."], ["👶", "childcare", "Childcare is expensive in big cities."], ["🙅", "discrimination", "Discrimination at work is illegal."], ["🤝", "respect", "Respect is the basis of a good relationship."]]}, {"t": "Work & opportunity", "ar": "الشغل والفرص", "items": [["🎯", "equal opportunities", "Everyone deserves equal opportunities."], ["💰", "pay gap", "The gender pay gap still exists."], ["📈", "promotion", "She deserved the promotion."], ["🧱", "glass ceiling", "She broke the glass ceiling and became CEO."], ["🍼", "maternity leave", "She took three months of maternity leave."], ["👨‍🍼", "paternity leave", "More fathers now take paternity leave."], ["🗳️", "representation", "Women's representation in parliament is growing."], ["💼", "career", "He gave up his career to raise his children."]]}, {"t": "Society & change", "ar": "المجتمع والتغيير", "items": [["🏛️", "traditional", "My grandparents have traditional views."], ["🔄", "modern", "Modern families are more flexible."], ["🌱", "progress", "There has been real progress in education."], ["🗣️", "debate", "This topic always starts a debate."], ["🤔", "assumption", "Don't make assumptions about people."], ["🏫", "role model", "She is a role model for young girls."], ["🧩", "balance", "Work-life balance is important for parents."], ["🙌", "empower", "Education empowers women and men."]]}], "talk": [{"title": "Let's Talk · Student A", "ar": "الطالب A", "list": [["How are household jobs shared in your family?", "شغل البيت متقسم إزاي في عيلتك؟", "My parents share most things, but my mum cooks."], ["Are there jobs that are better for men or for women? Why?", "في وظايف أنسب للرجالة أو للستات؟ ليه؟", "I think talent matters more than gender."], ["How have gender roles changed since your grandparents' time?", "أدوار الرجالة والستات اتغيرت إزاي من أيام أجدادك؟", "Most women didn't work outside the home then."], ["Should fathers take time off when a baby is born?", "الأب ياخد إجازة لما الطفل يتولد؟", "Yes, babies need both parents."], ["Who is a woman or a man you see as a role model? Why?", "مين الشخص اللي بتشوفه قدوة؟", "My aunt — she's an engineer and a great mum."]]}, {"title": "Let's Talk · Student B", "ar": "الطالب B", "list": [["Do boys and girls get the same treatment at school?", "الولاد والبنات بيتعاملوا بنفس الطريقة في المدرسة؟", "Mostly yes, but sports are often different."], ["What stereotypes about men or women do you disagree with?", "إيه الصور النمطية اللي مش موافق عليها؟", "That men shouldn't show emotions."], ["Should men and women always be paid the same for the same job?", "الرجالة والستات ياخدوا نفس المرتب لنفس الشغل؟", "Of course, if they do the same work."], ["Is it easy to balance a career and a family?", "سهل توفق بين الشغل والعيلة؟", "Not easy, but possible with support."], ["How can schools help reduce stereotypes?", "المدارس تقدر تقلل الصور النمطية إزاي؟", "By giving everyone the same opportunities."]]}], "grammar": {"title": "Participle Clauses", "ar": "جمل التصريف — Having finished… / Raised in… / Working full-time…", "blocks": [{"type": "intro", "en": "Participle clauses are short clauses that start with a present participle (-ing), a past participle (-ed/3rd form) or \"having + past participle\". They make writing shorter and more elegant, replacing words like because, when, after and who.", "ar": "الـ Participle clauses جمل قصيرة بتبدأ بـ ing أو التصريف التالت أو having + p.p. بتخلي الكتابة أقصر وأشيك، وبتاخد مكان because / when / after / who."}, {"type": "big", "items": [{"v": "-ing (present participle)", "p": "active, same time / reason", "c": 1, "eg": ["Working full-time, I'm always tired.", "Looking at our company, most managers are men.", "Not knowing the answer, she stayed silent."]}, {"v": "-ed / 3rd form (past participle)", "p": "passive meaning", "c": 2, "eg": ["Raised in a traditional family, he never cooked.", "Built in 1900, the school is very old.", "Asked about the pay gap, the minister said nothing."]}, {"v": "Having + p.p. (perfect participle)", "p": "one action before another", "c": 3, "eg": ["Having seen how tired I was, he started cooking.", "Having finished my coffee, I left.", "Having lived abroad, she understands other cultures."]}]}, {"type": "table", "title": "🔄 Long → short", "head": ["Long sentence", "Participle clause"], "rows": [["Because I work full-time, I'm always tired.", "Working full-time, I'm always tired."], ["He was raised in a traditional family, so he never cooked.", "Raised in a traditional family, he never cooked."], ["After he had seen how tired I was, he started cooking.", "Having seen how tired I was, he started cooking."], ["The woman who is sitting there is my manager.", "The woman sitting there is my manager."], ["When I looked at the data, I was surprised.", "Looking at the data, I was surprised."]]}, {"type": "uses", "title": "💡 Meanings", "ar": "المعاني", "items": [["⏱️", "time", "Walking home, I saw an accident.", "وأنا ماشي"], ["❓", "reason", "Feeling tired, she went to bed early.", "عشان"], ["⏮️", "sequence", "Having finished work, he went to the gym.", "بعد ما"], ["👤", "description", "The man wearing a blue shirt is my father.", "اللي لابس"]]}, {"type": "tip", "en": "The subject of the participle clause must be the SAME as the main clause. ✖ 'Walking home, the rain started.' (the rain wasn't walking!) ✔ 'Walking home, I got caught in the rain.'", "ar": "الفاعل في الجزئين لازم يكون واحد. غلط: Walking home, the rain started (المطر مكانش ماشي!). صح: Walking home, I got caught in the rain."}]}, "exercises": [{"type": "mcq", "title": "Participle Clauses — 10 MCQs", "ar": "اختار الصح", "speak": true, "items": [{"q": "___ full-time, I'm always tired.", "o": ["Working", "Worked", "Having work", "To work"], "a": 0}, {"q": "___ in a traditional family, he never cooked.", "o": ["Raised", "Raising", "Having raise", "Raise"], "a": 0}, {"q": "___ how tired I was, he started cooking.", "o": ["Having seen", "Having see", "Seen", "Have seen"], "a": 0}, {"q": "___ at our company, most managers are men.", "o": ["Looking", "Looked", "Having looked at", "To look"], "a": 0}, {"q": "___ my coffee, I went to pick up the kids.", "o": ["Having finished", "Finished", "Have finished", "To finish"], "a": 0}, {"q": "___ in 1900, the school is very old.", "o": ["Built", "Building", "Having building", "Build"], "a": 0}, {"q": "The woman ___ next to the window is my manager.", "o": ["sitting", "sat", "having sit", "sits"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Not ___ the answer, she stayed silent.", "o": ["knowing", "known", "having know", "to know"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Which sentence is correct?", "o": ["Walking home, I got caught in the rain.", "Walking home, the rain started.", "Walked home, I got caught in the rain.", "Having walk home, I got wet."], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"Having lived abroad, she understands other cultures.\" means…", "o": ["Because she lived abroad before, she understands.", "She will live abroad.", "She is living abroad now and doesn't understand.", "She never lived abroad."], "a": 0}]}, {"type": "mcq", "title": "-ing, -ed or Having?", "ar": "ing ولا ed ولا Having؟", "items": [{"q": "Active, same time → ___", "o": ["-ing", "-ed"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Passive meaning → ___", "o": ["-ed (3rd form)", "-ing"], "a": 0}, {"q": "One action finished before another → ___", "o": ["Having + p.p.", "-ing"], "a": 0}, {"q": "___ by her parents, she became a doctor. (passive)", "o": ["Encouraged", "Encouraging"], "a": 0}, {"q": "___ the exam, he celebrated. (first)", "o": ["Having passed", "Passed"], "a": 0}]}, {"type": "ord", "title": "Make sentences", "ar": "رتّب الكلمات", "items": [{"c": ["Having finished", "my work,", "I", "went home"], "a": [0, 1, 2, 3]}, {"c": ["Raised", "in Cairo,", "she", "loves big cities"], "a": [0, 1, 2, 3]}, {"c": ["Working", "full-time,", "he", "rarely sees his friends"], "a": [0, 1, 2, 3]}, {"c": ["The man", "wearing", "a blue shirt", "is my father"], "a": [0, 1, 2, 3]}]}], "reading": {"title": "Changing Roles", "ar": "أدوار بتتغير", "g": "f", "lines": [["Not so long ago, in many parts of the world, family roles were clearly divided. Men worked outside the home and earned money, while women looked after the house and the children.", "من زمن مش بعيد، في أماكن كتير في العالم، أدوار العيلة كانت متقسمة بوضوح. الرجالة بيشتغلوا برة البيت ويكسبوا فلوس، والستات بيراعوا البيت والأولاد."], ["Today, the picture is far more varied. Having gained greater access to education, women now make up around half of university students in many countries, including Egypt.", "النهارده، الصورة متنوعة أكتر بكتير. وبعد ما الستات خدوا فرص تعليم أكبر، بقوا تقريبًا نص طلاب الجامعات في بلاد كتير، منها مصر."], ["Working in fields such as medicine, engineering and technology, they are changing what people imagine when they hear the word \"boss\".", "وهما شغالين في مجالات زي الطب والهندسة والتكنولوجيا، بيغيروا الصورة اللي الناس بتتخيلها لما تسمع كلمة \"مدير\"."], ["At the same time, men's roles are changing too. More fathers are taking an active part in raising their children, and some countries now offer paid paternity leave.", "وفي نفس الوقت، أدوار الرجالة كمان بتتغير. آباء أكتر بيشاركوا بشكل فعال في تربية أولادهم، وبعض الدول بقت بتدي إجازة أبوة مدفوعة."], ["Encouraged by these changes, young men are choosing careers such as nursing and teaching, which were once seen as \"women's jobs\".", "ومتشجعين بالتغييرات دي، شباب بقوا بيختاروا مهن زي التمريض والتدريس، اللي كانت زمان بتتشاف إنها \"شغل ستات\"."], ["However, real equality has not been fully achieved. Globally, women still earn less than men on average, and they remain under-represented in top leadership positions.", "لكن المساواة الحقيقية لسه متحققتش بالكامل. على مستوى العالم، الستات لسه بيكسبوا أقل من الرجالة في المتوسط، ولسه تمثيلهم قليل في المناصب القيادية العليا."], ["Many women also face a \"double shift\": having finished their paid work, they come home to most of the housework.", "ستات كتير كمان بيواجهوا \"وردية مزدوجة\": بعد ما يخلصوا شغلهم المدفوع، بيرجعوا البيت لأغلب شغل البيت."], ["Stereotypes affect men as well. Men are often expected to hide their emotions and to be the main earners, which can create a lot of pressure.", "الصور النمطية بتأثر على الرجالة كمان. الرجالة غالبًا متوقع منهم يخبّوا مشاعرهم ويكونوا المصدر الأساسي للفلوس، وده ممكن يعمل ضغط كبير."], ["Different families and cultures will always organise their lives in different ways, and that is their right.", "العيلات والثقافات المختلفة هتفضل دايمًا تنظم حياتها بطرق مختلفة، وده حقها."], ["Perhaps the goal is not for everyone to live the same way, but for every person — man or woman — to have the freedom and respect to choose.", "يمكن الهدف مش إن كل الناس تعيش بنفس الطريقة، لكن إن كل شخص — راجل أو ست — يبقى عنده الحرية والاحترام إنه يختار."]], "keys": [["🔀", "varied", "different in many ways"], ["🎓", "access", "the opportunity to use or get something"], ["👨‍🍼", "paternity leave", "time off work for a new father"], ["📉", "under-represented", "not present in fair numbers"], ["🔁", "double shift", "paid work plus most of the housework"], ["💸", "earner", "a person who earns money"]], "quiz": [{"q": "How were family roles divided in the past?", "o": ["Men worked outside; women looked after the home.", "Everyone worked at home.", "Children worked."], "a": 0}, {"q": "What percentage of university students are women in many countries?", "o": ["around half", "about ten percent", "almost none"], "a": 0}, {"q": "How are men's roles changing?", "o": ["More fathers take an active part in raising children.", "Men stopped working.", "Nothing has changed."], "a": 0}, {"q": "What is the \"double shift\"?", "o": ["paid work plus most of the housework", "working at night", "two jobs at the same company"], "a": 0}, {"q": "How do stereotypes affect men?", "o": ["They are expected to hide emotions and be the main earners.", "They are paid less.", "They cannot work."], "a": 0}, {"q": "What is the goal, according to the last paragraph?", "o": ["freedom and respect for everyone to choose", "everyone living the same way", "only women working"], "a": 0}]}, "idioms": {"items": [["wear the trousers", "To be the person who makes the decisions in a home.", "هو اللي ماسك البيت", "In my family, it's my grandmother who wears the trousers.", "في عيلتي، تيتة هي اللي ماسكة البيت."], ["break the glass ceiling", "To reach a top position despite unfair barriers.", "يكسر الحاجز ويوصل للقمة", "She broke the glass ceiling and became the first female CEO.", "كسرت الحاجز وبقت أول مديرة تنفيذية ست."], ["on an equal footing", "Having the same rights and chances.", "على قدم المساواة", "Men and women should compete on an equal footing.", "الرجالة والستات لازم يتنافسوا على قدم المساواة."], ["pull your weight", "To do your fair share of the work.", "يعمل نصيبه من الشغل", "Everyone in the house should pull their weight.", "كل اللي في البيت لازم يعمل نصيبه من الشغل."]], "quiz": [{"q": "My brother never helps at home. He doesn't ___.", "o": ["pull his weight", "wear the trousers", "break the ceiling", "stand equal"], "a": 0}, {"q": "She became the first woman to run the bank. She ___.", "o": ["broke the glass ceiling", "pulled her weight", "wore the footing", "equalled"], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"On an equal footing\" means…", "o": ["with the same rights and chances", "walking together", "wearing the same shoes", "standing still"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Who ___ in your house? Who makes the big decisions?", "o": ["wears the trousers", "pulls the weight", "breaks the ceiling", "equal footing"], "a": 0}]}, "phrasal": {"items": [["bring up", "To raise a child.", "يربّي", "She was brought up by her grandparents.", "اتربّت عند جدها وجدتها."], ["look after", "To take care of someone or something.", "يراعي / ياخد باله من", "He looks after the kids on Fridays.", "هو اللي بيراعي الأولاد يوم الجمعة."], ["take on", "To accept a responsibility or job.", "يتحمل / ياخد على عاتقه", "She took on more responsibility at work.", "خدت على عاتقها مسؤولية أكبر في الشغل."], ["stand up to", "To refuse to accept unfair treatment.", "يواجه / يقف قدام", "She stood up to her boss when he treated her unfairly.", "وقفت قدام مديرها لما عاملها بظلم."]], "quiz": [{"q": "My parents ___ me ___ to respect everyone.", "o": ["brought / up", "took / on", "looked / after", "stood / up"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Who ___ your little brother when your parents work?", "o": ["looks after", "brings up", "takes on", "stands up to"], "a": 0}, {"q": "You should ___ people who treat you unfairly.", "o": ["stand up to", "look after", "bring up", "take on"], "a": 0}, {"q": "He ___ the role of team leader last year.", "o": ["took on", "stood up to", "brought up", "looked after"], "a": 0}]}, "slang": {"items": [["girl boss", "A confident, successful woman in business.", "ست ناجحة وقوية في الشغل", "My aunt started three companies — total girl boss.", "خالتي عملت ٣ شركات — ست قوية بجد.", "إيجابي (بيتقال أحيانًا بسخرية)"], ["house husband", "A man who stays at home to look after the house and children.", "راجل بيراعي البيت", "He's a proud house husband while his wife runs a clinic.", "هو راجل بيراعي البيت بفخر ومراته بتدير عيادة.", "عادي"], ["mansplain", "When a man explains something to a woman in a condescending way.", "يشرح بتعالي لست", "He mansplained football to a professional coach!", "شرح الكورة بتعالي لمدربة محترفة!", "انتقاد — استخدمها بحذر"], ["equal vibes", "A relationship or team where everyone is treated fairly.", "جو فيه مساواة", "Our team has equal vibes — everyone gets heard.", "فريقنا فيه جو مساواة — الكل صوته مسموع.", "بين الصحاب"], ["call out", "To publicly criticise unfair behaviour.", "يكشف وينتقد علنًا", "She called out the sexist joke in the meeting.", "انتقدت النكتة اللي فيها تمييز في الاجتماع.", "شائعة على السوشيال ميديا"]], "quiz": [{"q": "A man who stays home with the kids = a ___.", "o": ["house husband", "girl boss", "mansplain", "call out"], "a": 0}, {"q": "She publicly criticised the unfair comment. She ___ it.", "o": ["called out", "mansplained", "girl bossed", "equal vibed"], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"Mansplain\" describes explaining something ___.", "o": ["in a condescending way", "very kindly", "in a foreign language", "with pictures"], "a": 0}, {"q": "A successful woman who runs a business = a ___.", "o": ["girl boss", "house husband", "stereotype", "role"], "a": 0}]}, "story": {"title": "The Two Engineers", "ar": "المهندسين الاتنين", "g": "m", "lines": [["Raised in a small village, Amal had always loved fixing things. By the age of ten, she could repair her father's old radio.", "أمل اتربّت في قرية صغيرة، وطول عمرها بتحب تصلّح الحاجات. وهي عندها ١٠ سنين، كانت بتعرف تصلح الراديو القديم بتاع أبوها."], ["\"Engineering isn't for girls,\" a neighbour once told her. Hearing this, Amal decided to prove him wrong.", "\"الهندسة مش للبنات،\" جار قالها مرة. ولما سمعت ده، أمل قررت تثبتله إنه غلطان."], ["Having worked hard for years, she was accepted into the engineering faculty in Cairo.", "وبعد ما ذاكرت جامد سنين، اتقبلت في كلية الهندسة في القاهرة."], ["There she met Tamer, who dreamed of becoming a primary school teacher. His friends laughed at him. \"Teaching little children? That's a woman's job!\"", "هناك قابلت تامر، اللي كان بيحلم يبقى مدرس ابتدائي. صحابه ضحكوا عليه. \"تدريس أطفال صغيرين؟ ده شغل ستات!\""], ["Feeling the same pressure from opposite directions, Amal and Tamer became close friends.", "ولأنهم حاسين بنفس الضغط من اتجاهين عكس بعض، أمل وتامر بقوا صحاب قريبين."], ["Ten years later, Amal was leading a team that designed solar power systems for villages like the one she grew up in.", "بعد ١٠ سنين، أمل كانت بتقود فريق بيصمم أنظمة طاقة شمسية لقرى زي القرية اللي اتربت فيها."], ["Tamer, meanwhile, had become the most popular teacher in his school, known for turning maths into games.", "وتامر، في نفس الوقت، بقى أشهر مدرس في مدرسته، معروف إنه بيحوّل الرياضة لألعاب."], ["One day, Amal visited Tamer's classroom to talk about engineering. A little girl raised her hand. \"Can girls really build things?\"", "في يوم، أمل زارت فصل تامر عشان تتكلم عن الهندسة. بنت صغيرة رفعت إيدها. \"هي البنات فعلًا يقدروا يبنوا حاجات؟\""], ["Smiling, Amal handed her a small solar-powered fan. \"We can build anything,\" she said. \"And boys can teach, cook and care too.\"", "أمل ابتسمت وادتها مروحة صغيرة بالطاقة الشمسية. \"نقدر نبني أي حاجة،\" قالت. \"والولاد كمان يقدروا يدرّسوا ويطبخوا ويراعوا.\""], ["Looking at the excited faces, Tamer knew that the next generation would have more choices than they ever had.", "وهو باصص على الوشوش المتحمسة، تامر عرف إن الجيل الجاي هيبقى عنده اختيارات أكتر من اللي هما كان عندهم."]], "quiz": [{"q": "What could Amal do at the age of ten?", "o": ["repair her father's radio", "drive a car", "build a house"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What did the neighbour say?", "o": ["Engineering isn't for girls.", "She should be a doctor.", "She was very smart."], "a": 0}, {"q": "What was Tamer's dream?", "o": ["to become a primary school teacher", "to become an engineer", "to become a footballer"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What was Amal's team designing ten years later?", "o": ["solar power systems for villages", "cars", "phones"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What did Amal give the little girl?", "o": ["a solar-powered fan", "a book", "a radio"], "a": 0}]}, "challenge": {"title": "Equal Chances", "ar": "فرص متساوية — جاوب وسجّل", "qs": ["Describe a woman or man who broke a stereotype. What did they achieve?", "Should housework be shared equally? How would you divide it in your future home?", "Are there still jobs that people think are \"for men\" or \"for women\"? Do you agree?", "Having grown up in your culture, what gender roles did you notice as a child?", "Should companies be required to pay men and women the same for the same job?", "What pressures do young men face in your society?", "What pressures do young women face in your society?", "How can parents raise children without stereotypes?", "Is it possible to respect tradition and support equality at the same time?", "What would an equal society look like to you?"]}, "games": {"pairs": [["⚖️", "equality"], ["🧠", "stereotype"], ["🧱", "glass ceiling"], ["💰", "pay gap"], ["🏠", "housework"], ["🍼", "maternity leave"]], "spell": [["🚻", "gender"], ["👶", "childcare"], ["🙅", "discrimination"], ["🤝", "respect"], ["📈", "promotion"], ["🏛️", "traditional"], ["🌱", "progress"], ["🙌", "empower"]], "speed": [["Working full-time, I'm always tired.", true], ["Raised in Cairo, she loves big cities.", true], ["Having seen the results, he smiled.", true], ["Walking home, the rain started.", false], ["Having finish my work, I left.", false], ["The man wearing a blue shirt is my father.", true], ["Built in 1900, the school is old.", true], ["Raising in a village, he loves nature.", false], ["Not knowing the answer, she stayed silent.", true], ["Having lived abroad, she understands cultures.", true], ["A stereotype is a fixed idea about a group of people.", true], ["The pay gap means everyone earns the same.", false], ["\"Pull your weight\" means to do your fair share.", true], ["\"Bring up\" means to raise a child.", true], ["\"Break the glass ceiling\" means to break a window.", false], ["Paternity leave is for new fathers.", true]]}, "test": {"pass": 60, "sections": [{"id": "voc", "title": "Vocabulary", "ar": "المفردات", "icon": "📚", "qs": [{"q": "A fixed, often wrong idea about a group = a ___.", "o": ["stereotype", "promotion", "balance"], "a": 0, "pic": "🧠"}, {"q": "Treating people unfairly because of who they are = ___.", "o": ["discrimination", "equality", "representation"], "a": 0, "pic": "🙅"}, {"q": "The difference in pay between men and women = the pay ___.", "o": ["gap", "ceiling", "footing"], "a": 0, "pic": "💰"}, {"q": "Time off work for a new mother = ___ leave.", "o": ["maternity", "paternity", "annual"], "a": 0, "pic": "🍼"}, {"q": "Cleaning, cooking and washing = ___.", "o": ["housework", "homework", "teamwork"], "a": 0, "pic": "🏠"}, {"q": "\"المساواة\" in English is…", "o": ["equality", "equal", "equation"], "a": 0, "say": "Choose the correct word."}]}, {"id": "gra", "title": "Grammar", "ar": "القواعد", "icon": "📘", "qs": [{"q": "___ the report, she sent it to her manager.", "o": ["Having written", "Written", "Having write"], "a": 0}, {"q": "___ in Alexandria, he loves the sea.", "o": ["Born", "Bearing", "Having born"], "a": 0}, {"q": "___ late, I took a taxi.", "o": ["Being", "Been", "Having be"], "a": 0}, {"q": "The girl ___ the piano is my cousin.", "o": ["playing", "played", "having play"], "a": 0}, {"q": "___ by her teacher, she applied to university.", "o": ["Encouraged", "Encouraging", "Having encourage"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Which is correct?", "o": ["Opening the door, I saw my old friend.", "Opening the door, my old friend was there.", "Opened the door, I saw my friend."], "a": 0}]}, {"id": "con", "title": "Conversation", "ar": "المحادثة", "icon": "💬", "qs": [{"q": "\"How do you share housework at home?\" — Best answer:", "o": ["We take turns cooking and cleaning.", "Housework is a noun.", "At home."], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"Are some jobs only for men?\" — Best answer:", "o": ["I think talent matters more than gender.", "Jobs are jobs.", "Yes, men."], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"My brother never helps at home.\" — Best answer:", "o": ["He should pull his weight!", "He should wear trousers.", "He should break the ceiling."], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"She became the first female director of the hospital.\" — Best answer:", "o": ["Wow, she broke the glass ceiling!", "Did she break a window?", "Ceilings are high."], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"People find it strange that I'm a male nurse.\" — Best answer:", "o": ["That's a stereotype. You should be proud.", "Nurses are women.", "Change your job."], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"Having finished my coffee, I have to go.\" means…", "o": ["I finished my coffee, so now I'm leaving.", "I will finish my coffee later.", "I have no coffee."], "a": 0}]}, {"id": "rea", "title": "Reading", "ar": "القراءة", "icon": "📖", "passage": ["Having grown up watching her mother run a small pharmacy, Rana always wanted her own business.", "Starting with only one shop, she now owns a chain of five pharmacies in Giza.", "Her husband, Karim, works part-time as a designer and looks after their two children in the afternoons.", "\"People were surprised at first,\" Karim says. \"But having tried it, I love spending time with my kids.\"", "Asked about their secret, Rana smiles: \"We don't think about whose job it is. We think about what our family needs.\""], "qs": [{"q": "What did Rana's mother run?", "o": ["a small pharmacy", "a school", "a restaurant"], "a": 0}, {"q": "How many pharmacies does Rana own now?", "o": ["five", "one", "ten"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What does Karim do in the afternoons?", "o": ["looks after the children", "works at the pharmacy", "plays football"], "a": 0}, {"q": "How does Karim feel about it now?", "o": ["He loves spending time with his kids.", "He hates it.", "He wants to stop."], "a": 0}, {"q": "What is their secret?", "o": ["thinking about what the family needs", "having a lot of money", "following tradition strictly"], "a": 0}]}, {"id": "wri", "title": "Writing", "ar": "الكتابة", "icon": "✍️", "writing": true, "prompt": "Write a balanced paragraph (80–120 words): \"How have gender roles changed in your country?\" Show different points of view respectfully. Use at least three participle clauses (Having…, -ing…, -ed…).", "promptAr": "اكتب فقرة متوازنة (٨٠–١٢٠ كلمة): \"أدوار الرجالة والستات اتغيرت إزاي في بلدك؟\" اعرض آراء مختلفة باحترام، واستخدم ٣ participle clauses على الأقل.", "checks": [["⚖️", "Equality words", "x", "\\b(gender|equality|equal|role|roles|men|women|traditional|work|housework|stereotype|stereotypes|opportunities|respect)\\b"], ["🔗", "Participle clause", "x", "(^|[.!?]\\s+)(having\\s+\\w+|\\w+ing|\\w+ed)\\b[^.!?]*,"], ["⚖️", "Balance", "x", "\\b(however|on the other hand|while|whereas|some people|others)\\b"], ["💬", "At least 70 words", "len70"]]}]}, "watch": [{"yt": "DaW-Kha9qAM", "title": "Women in the Workplace", "ar": "الستات في مكان الشغل — 6 Minute English", "by": "BBC Learning English", "lines": [["A boss asks a female colleague to buy a birthday card and order a cake, because she is \"great at organising\".", "مدير بيطلب من زميلة ست تشتري كارت عيد ميلاد وتطلب تورتة، عشان هي \"شاطرة في التنظيم\"."], ["Jobs like this keep the office running, but they do nothing to help her career or her chances of promotion.", "شغل زي ده بيمشّي المكتب، بس مش بيفيد مستقبلها المهني ولا فرصها في الترقية."], ["In many workplaces, men are seen as \"born leaders\" and promoted, while women get less important roles.", "في أماكن شغل كتير، الرجالة بيتشافوا \"قادة بالفطرة\" وبيترقّوا، والستات بياخدوا أدوار أقل أهمية."], ["Many women reach a point they cannot pass — an invisible barrier called the glass ceiling.", "ستات كتير بيوصلوا لنقطة مش بيقدروا يعدّوها — حاجز مش باين اسمه السقف الزجاجي."], ["The quiz: who was the first woman to become British Prime Minister?", "السؤال: مين أول ست بقت رئيسة وزراء بريطانيا؟"], ["A group of researchers wrote a book called The No Club about women saying \"no\" to this kind of work.", "مجموعة باحثات كتبوا كتاب اسمه \"نادي لأ\" عن ستات بيقولوا \"لأ\" للنوع ده من الشغل."], ["They call it non-promotable tasks: taking notes, organising parties, planning events.", "بيسموه مهام مش بترقّي: كتابة الملاحظات، وتنظيم الحفلات، وترتيب الفعاليات."], ["Research shows that most of these tasks are done by women.", "الأبحاث بتوضح إن أغلب المهام دي بتعملها الستات."], ["This contributes to bigger gaps in pay and promotion, and to more burn-out — exhaustion from working too hard.", "ده بيساهم في فجوات أكبر في المرتبات والترقيات، وفي إرهاق أكتر من الشغل الزيادة."], ["A businesswoman remembers being the team party organiser and taking notes in meetings when she started her career.", "سيدة أعمال بتفتكر إنها كانت منظمة حفلات الفريق وبتكتب الملاحظات في الاجتماعات في بداية شغلها."], ["Many women are expected to be good at multitasking, and working mums are always juggling work and family.", "ستات كتير متوقع منهم يكونوا شاطرين في عمل حاجات كتير مع بعض، والأمهات الشغالين دايمًا بيوفّقوا بين الشغل والعيلة."], ["The answer: Margaret Thatcher, who became Prime Minister in 1979 and broke the political glass ceiling in the UK.", "الإجابة: مارجريت تاتشر، اللي بقت رئيسة وزراء سنة ١٩٧٩ وكسرت السقف الزجاجي في السياسة البريطانية."]], "words": ["organising", "career", "promotion", "born leaders", "glass ceiling", "Prime Minister", "non-promotable tasks", "research", "burn-out", "meetings", "multitasking", "juggling"], "quiz": [{"q": "What does the boss ask the woman to do?", "o": ["buy a card and order a cake", "lead a big project", "give a presentation"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What is the \"glass ceiling\"?", "o": ["an invisible barrier that stops people advancing", "a roof made of glass", "a high salary"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What are non-promotable tasks?", "o": ["jobs that help the office but not your career", "jobs that get you promoted", "jobs done at home"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Who does most non-promotable tasks, according to research?", "o": ["women", "men", "managers"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What is \"burn-out\"?", "o": ["exhaustion from working too hard", "a fire in the office", "a promotion"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Who was the first female British Prime Minister?", "o": ["Margaret Thatcher", "Theresa May", "Nicola Sturgeon"], "a": 0}]}]}, "7": {"n": 7, "title": "The Generation Gap", "ar": "الفجوة بين الأجيال — Emphasis with do / does / did", "icon": "👴", "cover": "img/b2p/u7.jpg", "intro": "اتكلم عن الاختلاف بين جيلك وجيل أهلك وأجدادك: التكنولوجيا والشغل والقيم والعلاقات، واستخدم do / does / did للتأكيد: I do respect them! / He did try!", "videos": [{"id": "b2pv7", "title": "Grandpa's Phone", "ar": "موبايل جدو — منى وزياد", "src": "video/b2p/u7v1.mp4", "poster": "img/b2p/u7v1.jpg", "sp": {"a": {"n": "Mona", "g": "f"}, "b": {"n": "Ziad", "g": "m"}}, "lines": [["b", "Mona, Grandpa called me five times today. He wanted help with his new smartphone again.", "منى، جدو كلمني ٥ مرات النهارده. كان عايز مساعدة في الموبايل الجديد تاني."], ["a", "Ha! Did you help him?", "هههه! ساعدته؟"], ["b", "I did try! But he gets annoyed when I explain too fast. He says young people never have patience.", "حاولت فعلًا! بس بيتضايق لما بشرح بسرعة. بيقول إن الشباب عمرهم ما بيبقى عندهم صبر."], ["a", "Well, he does have a point. We're always in a hurry.", "بصراحة عنده حق. إحنا دايمًا مستعجلين."], ["b", "Maybe. But he does think we spend too much time on our phones.", "يمكن. بس هو فعلًا شايف إننا بنقضي وقت كتير على موبايلاتنا."], ["a", "We do! Last week at dinner, everyone was scrolling except him and Grandma.", "فعلًا بنقضي! الأسبوع اللي فات على العشا، كله كان بيعمل سكرول ماعدا هو وتيتة."], ["b", "True. But our generation faces different problems. Getting a job and an apartment is so much harder now.", "صح. بس جيلنا بيواجه مشاكل مختلفة. إنك تلاقي شغل وشقة بقى أصعب بكتير دلوقتي."], ["a", "I know. When Grandpa was 25, he already had a house and three children!", "عارفة. لما جدو كان عنده ٢٥ سنة، كان عنده بيت و٣ أولاد خلاص!"], ["b", "And he worked for the same company for forty years. Nobody does that today.", "واشتغل في نفس الشركة ٤٠ سنة. محدش بيعمل كده النهارده."], ["a", "But I do admire his loyalty. And his stories about the old days are amazing.", "بس أنا فعلًا معجبة بولائه. وحكاياته عن الأيام القديمة تحفة."], ["b", "That's true. Maybe we could learn from each other. I'll teach him WhatsApp, and he'll teach me patience!", "صح. يمكن نقدر نتعلم من بعض. أنا هعلمه الواتساب، وهو يعلمني الصبر!"], ["a", "Deal. And this Friday, phones off at dinner. Grandpa will love that.", "اتفقنا. والجمعة دي، الموبايلات مقفولة على العشا. جدو هيحب ده."], ["b", "He really will. He does love a good family dinner!", "أكيد هيحب. هو فعلًا بيحب العشا العائلي الحلو!"]], "quiz": [{"q": "Why did Grandpa call Ziad five times?", "o": ["He needed help with his new smartphone.", "He was ill.", "He wanted money."], "a": 0}, {"q": "What does Grandpa say about young people?", "o": ["They never have patience.", "They work too hard.", "They are very polite."], "a": 0}, {"q": "What happened at dinner last week?", "o": ["Everyone was scrolling except the grandparents.", "Grandpa was on his phone.", "Nobody came."], "a": 0}, {"q": "How long did Grandpa work for the same company?", "o": ["forty years", "four years", "ten years"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What will they do this Friday?", "o": ["turn their phones off at dinner", "buy Grandpa a new phone", "go to a restaurant"], "a": 0}], "fill": [[0, "smartphone"], [2, "I did try"], [2, "patience"], [3, "he does have a point"], [4, "he does think"], [5, "We do"], [6, "generation"], [8, "company"], [9, "I do admire"], [9, "loyalty"], [10, "learn from each other"], [12, "He does love"]]}], "vocab": [{"t": "Generations", "ar": "الأجيال", "items": [["👴", "generation", "Every generation has its own music."], ["🌉", "generation gap", "There is a big generation gap in our family."], ["👶", "Gen Z", "Gen Z grew up with smartphones."], ["🧑‍💻", "millennial", "Millennials were born between 1981 and 1996."], ["👵", "elderly", "We should respect elderly people."], ["🧒", "youth", "In his youth, he was a great footballer."], ["🧓", "senior citizen", "Senior citizens get cheaper tickets."], ["📆", "era", "It was a different era."]]}, {"t": "Values & attitudes", "ar": "القيم والمواقف", "items": [["🤝", "loyalty", "He showed great loyalty to his company."], ["⏳", "patience", "Patience is a rare quality today."], ["🙇", "respect", "Respect for elders is important in our culture."], ["🧭", "values", "Our values come from our family."], ["🔄", "old-fashioned", "My father's ideas are a bit old-fashioned."], ["🆕", "open-minded", "Young people tend to be open-minded."], ["🗣️", "disagree", "We often disagree about politics."], ["🏛️", "tradition", "Some traditions should be kept."]]}, {"t": "Life then & now", "ar": "الحياة زمان ودلوقتي", "items": [["📱", "digital native", "Digital natives learn technology fast."], ["☎️", "landline", "We used to have a landline phone."], ["🏠", "property", "Property is very expensive today."], ["💼", "job security", "Job security was higher in the past."], ["🧳", "independence", "Young people want more independence."], ["🎞️", "nostalgia", "Old songs fill me with nostalgia."], ["💡", "wisdom", "Grandparents have a lot of wisdom."], ["🔁", "pass down", "Recipes are passed down from generation to generation."]]}], "talk": [{"title": "Let's Talk · Student A", "ar": "الطالب A", "list": [["What is the biggest difference between you and your parents?", "إيه أكبر فرق بينك وبين أهلك؟", "Technology. They hate it; I love it."], ["What can young people learn from older people?", "الشباب يقدروا يتعلموا إيه من الكبار؟", "Patience and wisdom."], ["What can older people learn from young people?", "الكبار يقدروا يتعلموا إيه من الشباب؟", "How to use technology and be open-minded."], ["Was life easier for your grandparents' generation?", "الحياة كانت أسهل لجيل أجدادك؟", "In some ways, yes — houses were cheaper."], ["Which old tradition do you love?", "أنهي عادة قديمة بتحبها؟", "Family lunch every Friday."]]}, {"title": "Let's Talk · Student B", "ar": "الطالب B", "list": [["Do you think your parents understand your generation?", "شايف إن أهلك فاهمين جيلك؟", "They do try, but it's hard."], ["Should young people always follow their parents' advice?", "الشباب لازم يسمعوا نصيحة أهلهم دايمًا؟", "Listen, yes; always follow, not necessarily."], ["What will your generation be famous for?", "جيلك هيتعرف بإيه؟", "Technology and changing the world of work."], ["Is it better to live with your family or alone?", "أحسن تعيش مع عيلتك ولا لوحدك؟", "With family, at least until marriage."], ["What old-fashioned thing do you secretly like?", "إيه الحاجة القديمة اللي بتحبها في السر؟", "I do love old black-and-white films!"]]}], "grammar": {"title": "Emphasis with do / does / did", "ar": "التأكيد بـ do / does / did", "blocks": [{"type": "intro", "en": "In positive sentences, we can add do, does or did before the main verb to make it stronger. We use it to show strong feeling, to contrast with what someone thinks, or to insist that something is true.", "ar": "في الجمل المثبتة، ممكن نحط do أو does أو did قبل الفعل الأساسي عشان نقويه. بنستخدمها عشان نبيّن مشاعر قوية، أو نعارض كلام حد، أو نأكد إن حاجة صح."}, {"type": "big", "items": [{"v": "do / does + base verb", "p": "present simple emphasis", "c": 1, "eg": ["I do respect my grandparents!", "He does have a point.", "We do spend too much time on our phones."]}, {"v": "did + base verb", "p": "past simple emphasis", "c": 2, "eg": ["I did try to help him!", "She did call you — check your phone.", "They did warn us about the traffic."]}, {"v": "Do + imperative", "p": "polite insistence", "c": 3, "eg": ["Do sit down!", "Do come again soon.", "Do call me if you need anything."]}]}, {"type": "table", "title": "🔊 Normal → Emphatic", "head": ["Normal", "Emphatic (stronger)"], "rows": [["I respect them.", "I do respect them!"], ["He loves family dinners.", "He does love family dinners!"], ["I tried to help.", "I did try to help!"], ["Sit down, please.", "Do sit down!"], ["You look tired.", "You do look tired."]]}, {"type": "uses", "title": "💡 When do we use it?", "ar": "بنستخدمها إمتى؟", "items": [["🙅", "contradict", "\"You never listen!\" — \"I do listen!\"", "اعتراض"], ["💪", "insist", "I did lock the door — I'm sure.", "إصرار"], ["❤️", "strong feeling", "I do love this song!", "مشاعر قوية"], ["☕", "polite invitation", "Do have some more tea.", "عزومة بأدب"]]}, {"type": "tip", "en": "After do/does/did, the main verb is always in the BASE form: He does loves ✖ → He does love ✔. I did tried ✖ → I did try ✔. In speaking, we stress the auxiliary: I DO like it!", "ar": "بعد do / does / did الفعل الأساسي يرجع لأصله: He does love مش does loves، وI did try مش did tried. وفي الكلام بنضغط على do: I DO like it!"}]}, "exercises": [{"type": "mcq", "title": "Emphatic do — 10 MCQs", "ar": "اختار الصح", "speak": true, "items": [{"q": "I ___ try to help him! He just didn't listen.", "o": ["did", "do", "does", "done"], "a": 0}, {"q": "He ___ have a point. We are always in a hurry.", "o": ["does", "do", "did has", "is"], "a": 0}, {"q": "We ___ spend too much time on our phones.", "o": ["do", "does", "did spent", "are"], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"You never call me!\" — \"I ___ call you last week!\"", "o": ["did", "do", "does", "was"], "a": 0}, {"q": "She does ___ old films.", "o": ["love", "loves", "loved", "loving"], "a": 0}, {"q": "I did ___ the door. I'm sure.", "o": ["lock", "locked", "locks", "locking"], "a": 0}, {"q": "___ sit down and have some tea!", "o": ["Do", "Does", "Did", "Done"], "a": 0}, {"q": "My grandfather ___ understand technology — he just prefers books.", "o": ["does", "do", "did understood", "is"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Which sentence is correct?", "o": ["He does love family dinners.", "He does loves family dinners.", "He do love family dinners.", "He did loved family dinners."], "a": 0}, {"q": "Emphatic \"do\" is used to ___.", "o": ["make a positive statement stronger", "make a question", "make a negative", "talk about the future"], "a": 0}]}, {"type": "mcq", "title": "do, does or did?", "ar": "do ولا does ولا did؟", "items": [{"q": "She ___ like you — she just doesn't show it.", "o": ["does", "do"], "a": 0}, {"q": "I ___ finish my homework yesterday!", "o": ["did", "do"], "a": 0}, {"q": "They ___ want to come, but they were busy.", "o": ["did", "does"], "a": 0}, {"q": "After did, the verb is ___.", "o": ["base form", "past form"], "a": 0}, {"q": "We ___ appreciate your help.", "o": ["do", "does"], "a": 0}]}, {"type": "ord", "title": "Make sentences", "ar": "رتّب الكلمات", "items": [{"c": ["I", "do", "respect", "my grandparents"], "a": [0, 1, 2, 3]}, {"c": ["He", "did", "try", "to help"], "a": [0, 1, 2, 3]}, {"c": ["She", "does", "love", "old songs"], "a": [0, 1, 2, 3]}, {"c": ["Do", "come", "again", "soon"], "a": [0, 1, 2, 3]}]}], "reading": {"title": "Talking Across the Gap", "ar": "الكلام عبر الفجوة", "g": "m", "lines": [["For the first time in history, as many as five generations may be working side by side in the same company — from people in their seventies to teenagers on their first internship.", "لأول مرة في التاريخ، ممكن ٥ أجيال يشتغلوا جنب بعض في نفس الشركة — من ناس في السبعينات لمراهقين في أول تدريب ليهم."], ["Each generation has been shaped by very different experiences. Older people remember a world without the internet, when news came from newspapers and friends met face to face.", "كل جيل اتشكل بتجارب مختلفة جدًا. الكبار فاكرين عالم من غير إنترنت، لما الأخبار كانت بتيجي من الجرايد والصحاب بيتقابلوا وش لوش."], ["Younger people, by contrast, are \"digital natives\" who have never known life without smartphones.", "وفي المقابل، الأصغر \"مولودين في العالم الرقمي\" وعمرهم ما عرفوا الحياة من غير موبايلات."], ["These different backgrounds can lead to misunderstandings. Older workers sometimes see young people as impatient and unwilling to stay in one job.", "الخلفيات المختلفة دي ممكن تسبب سوء فهم. الموظفين الأكبر أحيانًا بيشوفوا الشباب قليلين صبر ومش عايزين يستقروا في شغلانة واحدة."], ["Young workers, on the other hand, may see their older colleagues as resistant to change.", "والموظفين الشباب، من ناحية تانية، ممكن يشوفوا زمايلهم الأكبر رافضين التغيير."], ["However, research does suggest that these stereotypes are often exaggerated. When people from different generations work together, they tend to learn a great deal from each other.", "لكن الأبحاث فعلًا بتقول إن الصور النمطية دي غالبًا مبالغ فيها. لما ناس من أجيال مختلفة بيشتغلوا مع بعض، غالبًا بيتعلموا من بعض كتير."], ["Some companies now run \"reverse mentoring\" programmes, in which young employees teach senior managers about technology and social media, while the managers share their experience and contacts.", "بعض الشركات دلوقتي بتعمل برامج \"التوجيه العكسي\"، اللي فيها الموظفين الشباب بيعلّموا المديرين الكبار التكنولوجيا والسوشيال ميديا، والمديرين بيشاركوهم خبرتهم وعلاقاتهم."], ["The same is true in families. Grandparents can pass down traditions, recipes and wisdom, while grandchildren can help them stay connected in a digital world.", "ونفس الكلام في العيلات. الأجداد يقدروا ينقلوا العادات والوصفات والحكمة، والأحفاد يقدروا يساعدوهم يفضلوا متواصلين في عالم رقمي."], ["Of course, disagreements will always exist. But as one grandmother put it, \"We don't have to see the world in the same way. We do have to listen to each other.\"", "طبعًا، الخلافات هتفضل موجودة. بس زي ما قالت جدة: \"مش لازم نشوف الدنيا بنفس الطريقة. بس لازم فعلًا نسمع بعض.\""]], "keys": [["👥", "side by side", "next to each other"], ["🧱", "shaped by", "influenced and formed by"], ["📱", "digital native", "a person who grew up with digital technology"], ["🙅", "resistant to change", "not wanting things to change"], ["📈", "exaggerated", "made to seem bigger or worse than it is"], ["🔄", "reverse mentoring", "young people teaching older people"]], "quiz": [{"q": "How many generations may work in the same company today?", "o": ["as many as five", "only two", "one"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What do older people remember?", "o": ["a world without the internet", "only smartphones", "nothing"], "a": 0}, {"q": "How do older workers sometimes see young people?", "o": ["as impatient", "as too loyal", "as very old-fashioned"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What does research suggest about these stereotypes?", "o": ["They are often exaggerated.", "They are always true.", "They do not exist."], "a": 0}, {"q": "What happens in \"reverse mentoring\"?", "o": ["Young employees teach senior managers about technology.", "Managers teach children at school.", "Nobody teaches anyone."], "a": 0}, {"q": "What is the grandmother's message?", "o": ["We must listen to each other.", "We must agree on everything.", "Young people are always right."], "a": 0}]}, "idioms": {"items": [["set in your ways", "Not wanting to change your habits or opinions.", "متمسك بعاداته / مش بيتغير", "My grandfather is set in his ways — he still writes letters.", "جدي متمسك بعاداته — لسه بيكتب جوابات."], ["in my day", "When I was young (used by older people).", "في أيامنا", "\"In my day, we walked to school!\" Grandpa said.", "\"في أيامنا، كنا بنروح المدرسة مشي!\" جدو قال."], ["bridge the gap", "To reduce the difference between two groups.", "يقرّب المسافة", "Family dinners help bridge the generation gap.", "العشا العائلي بيساعد يقرّب المسافة بين الأجيال."], ["old school", "Traditional or old-fashioned (often in a positive way).", "على الطريقة القديمة", "I love his old school manners.", "بحب أخلاقه اللي على الطريقة القديمة."]], "quiz": [{"q": "Teaching Grandma to video call can help ___.", "o": ["bridge the gap", "set in your ways", "old school", "in my day"], "a": 0}, {"q": "He refuses to use a smartphone. He's very ___.", "o": ["set in his ways", "bridged", "in his day", "gap"], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"___, we didn't have the internet,\" said my father.", "o": ["In my day", "Old school", "Set in my ways", "Bridge the gap"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Writing thank-you letters by hand is a bit ___, but lovely.", "o": ["old school", "in my day", "bridge", "set"], "a": 0}]}, "phrasal": {"items": [["look up to", "To admire and respect someone.", "يعتبره قدوة", "I really look up to my grandmother.", "أنا فعلًا بعتبر تيتة قدوة."], ["grow up", "To change from a child to an adult.", "يكبر", "My parents grew up without mobile phones.", "أهلي كبروا من غير موبايلات."], ["take after", "To look or behave like an older family member.", "طالع لـ", "Ziad takes after his grandfather — they're both stubborn!", "زياد طالع لجده — الاتنين عنديين!"], ["get on with", "To have a good relationship with someone.", "متفاهم مع", "I get on well with my parents.", "أنا متفاهم كويس مع أهلي."]], "quiz": [{"q": "She ___ her mother — they both love painting.", "o": ["takes after", "grows up", "looks up", "gets on"], "a": 0}, {"q": "I ___ in a small town near Luxor.", "o": ["grew up", "took after", "got on", "looked up"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Do you ___ your older brother?", "o": ["get on with", "take after", "grow up", "look up"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Many young people ___ their grandparents for their wisdom.", "o": ["look up to", "grow up", "take after", "get on"], "a": 0}]}, "slang": {"items": [["OK boomer", "A joking reply to an older person's old-fashioned opinion.", "ماشي يا حاج (بهزار)", "\"Phones are ruining your generation!\" — \"OK boomer.\"", "\"الموبايلات بتبوّظ جيلكم!\" — \"ماشي يا حاج.\"", "ممكن تبقى قلة أدب — متقولهاش لكبير في الحقيقة!"], ["cheugy", "Out of date and trying too hard (Gen Z slang).", "قديم ومش مواكب", "Wearing that is a bit cheugy now.", "لبس ده بقى قديم شوية دلوقتي.", "سلانج Gen Z"], ["throwback", "Something that reminds you of the past.", "رجوع للماضي / ذكرى", "This song is such a throwback!", "الأغنية دي بترجعني لزمان!", "عادي جدًا"], ["vintage", "Old in a cool, stylish way.", "قديم وشيك", "Grandpa's old camera is so vintage.", "كاميرا جدو القديمة شيك جدًا.", "إيجابي"], ["no cap, respect", "Honestly, I respect that.", "بجد، احترامي", "You worked 40 years in one place? No cap, respect.", "اشتغلت ٤٠ سنة في مكان واحد؟ بجد، احترامي.", "لطيفة"]], "quiz": [{"q": "Something old but cool and stylish = ___.", "o": ["vintage", "cheugy", "boomer", "throwback"], "a": 0}, {"q": "A song that reminds you of your childhood is a ___.", "o": ["throwback", "cheugy", "boomer", "vintage"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Is \"OK boomer\" polite to say to your grandfather?", "o": ["No, it can be rude.", "Yes, always.", "Only on Fridays.", "Only in writing."], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"Cheugy\" means…", "o": ["out of date and trying too hard", "very cheap", "very cool", "very old and expensive"], "a": 0}]}, "story": {"title": "The Recipe Book", "ar": "كتاب الوصفات", "g": "f", "lines": [["Every Friday, sixteen-year-old Ziad visited his grandmother, Teta Nadia. And every Friday, he spent most of the visit on his phone.", "كل جمعة، زياد اللي عنده ١٦ سنة كان بيزور جدته، تيتة نادية. وكل جمعة، كان بيقضي أغلب الزيارة على موبايله."], ["\"In my day,\" Teta would say, \"young people talked to their grandparents.\" Ziad would roll his eyes. \"OK, Teta.\"", "\"في أيامنا،\" تيتة كانت بتقول، \"الشباب كانوا بيتكلموا مع أجدادهم.\" وزياد كان بيقلب عينيه. \"حاضر يا تيتة.\""], ["One Friday, Teta took out an old notebook with a torn cover. \"These are my recipes,\" she said. \"My mother taught me some of them. I've never written the others down.\"", "في جمعة، تيتة طلّعت كشكول قديم غلافه مقطوع. \"دي وصفاتي،\" قالت. \"أمي علمتني شوية منهم. والباقي عمري ما كتبته.\""], ["Ziad looked at the faded pages. Suddenly, he had an idea. \"Teta, let's film you cooking. I'll put the videos online.\"", "زياد بص على الصفحات الباهتة. فجأة، جاتله فكرة. \"يا تيتة، تعالي نصورك وإنتي بتطبخي. هنزّل الفيديوهات أونلاين.\""], ["At first she refused. \"Who would want to watch an old woman cook?\" But he did manage to persuade her.", "في الأول رفضت. \"مين هيحب يتفرج على ست عجوزة بتطبخ؟\" بس هو فعلًا قدر يقنعها."], ["Every Friday after that, they cooked together. Teta explained every step, adding stories about her childhood in Alexandria. Ziad filmed, edited and added music.", "كل جمعة بعدها، كانوا بيطبخوا مع بعض. تيتة بتشرح كل خطوة، وبتحكي حكايات عن طفولتها في إسكندرية. وزياد بيصور ويمنتج ويحط مزيكا."], ["Within six months, \"Teta's Kitchen\" had 200,000 followers. People from all over the world commented: \"She reminds me of my own grandmother!\"", "في خلال ٦ شهور، \"مطبخ تيتة\" بقى عنده ٢٠٠ ألف متابع. ناس من كل حتة في العالم علّقوا: \"بتفكرني بجدتي!\""], ["But the biggest change was not online. Ziad had learned to make twenty traditional dishes, and Teta had learned to reply to comments by herself.", "بس أكبر تغيير مكانش أونلاين. زياد اتعلم يعمل ٢٠ أكلة تقليدية، وتيتة اتعلمت ترد على التعليقات بنفسها."], ["More importantly, they had finally started talking — really talking.", "والأهم، إنهم أخيرًا بدأوا يتكلموا — يتكلموا بجد."], ["\"You see,\" Teta said one Friday, smiling, \"I did tell you that young people should talk to their grandparents.\" Ziad laughed. \"You did, Teta. You really did.\"", "\"شفت،\" تيتة قالت في جمعة وهي بتبتسم، \"أنا فعلًا قلتلك إن الشباب لازم يتكلموا مع أجدادهم.\" زياد ضحك. \"فعلًا قلتي يا تيتة. فعلًا.\""]], "quiz": [{"q": "What did Ziad usually do during his visits?", "o": ["He spent most of the time on his phone.", "He cooked.", "He slept."], "a": 0}, {"q": "What did Teta take out one Friday?", "o": ["an old recipe notebook", "a photo album", "a new phone"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What was Ziad's idea?", "o": ["to film her cooking and put the videos online", "to sell the notebook", "to open a restaurant"], "a": 0}, {"q": "How many followers did \"Teta's Kitchen\" have after six months?", "o": ["200,000", "2,000", "20 million"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What was the biggest change?", "o": ["They finally started really talking.", "They became rich.", "Teta moved to Cairo."], "a": 0}]}, "challenge": {"title": "Bridging the Gap", "ar": "نقرّب المسافة — جاوب وسجّل", "qs": ["Describe the oldest person in your family. What can you learn from them?", "What is one thing your parents' generation did better than yours?", "What is one thing your generation does better?", "Use emphatic do: tell me something you DO believe, even if others don't.", "Should grandparents live with their children and grandchildren?", "How has technology changed the relationship between generations?", "What traditions would you like to pass down to your children?", "Describe a disagreement you had with an older person. How did you solve it?", "What will your generation be like when it is old?", "If you could ask your grandparents one question, what would it be?"]}, "games": {"pairs": [["🌉", "generation gap"], ["👵", "elderly"], ["⏳", "patience"], ["🎞️", "nostalgia"], ["💡", "wisdom"], ["📱", "digital native"]], "spell": [["👴", "generation"], ["🤝", "loyalty"], ["🧭", "values"], ["🏛️", "tradition"], ["🧳", "independence"], ["📆", "era"], ["🧒", "youth"], ["🙇", "respect"]], "speed": [["I do respect my grandparents.", true], ["He does loves family dinners.", false], ["I did try to help him.", true], ["I did tried to call you.", false], ["We do spend too much time online.", true], ["Do sit down and have some tea!", true], ["She do like old films.", false], ["They did warn us about it.", true], ["He does have a point.", true], ["You does look tired.", false], ["A digital native grew up with technology.", true], ["Nostalgia is a love of the future.", false], ["\"Take after\" means to be like an older family member.", true], ["\"Set in your ways\" means you don't like change.", true], ["\"Vintage\" means old in a cool way.", true], ["\"OK boomer\" is a polite thing to say to elders.", false]]}, "test": {"pass": 60, "sections": [{"id": "voc", "title": "Vocabulary", "ar": "المفردات", "icon": "📚", "qs": [{"q": "The difference between young and old people = the generation ___.", "o": ["gap", "era", "wisdom"], "a": 0, "pic": "🌉"}, {"q": "Knowledge from experience = ___.", "o": ["wisdom", "youth", "nostalgia"], "a": 0, "pic": "💡"}, {"q": "A happy, sad feeling about the past = ___.", "o": ["nostalgia", "loyalty", "patience"], "a": 0, "pic": "🎞️"}, {"q": "Not modern; from an older time = ___.", "o": ["old-fashioned", "open-minded", "independent"], "a": 0, "pic": "🔄"}, {"q": "Staying faithful to someone or something = ___.", "o": ["loyalty", "era", "property"], "a": 0, "pic": "🤝"}, {"q": "\"صبر\" in English is…", "o": ["patience", "patient", "passion"], "a": 0, "say": "Choose the correct word."}]}, {"id": "gra", "title": "Grammar", "ar": "القواعد", "icon": "📘", "qs": [{"q": "\"You never help!\" — \"I ___ help! I washed the dishes.\"", "o": ["do", "does", "am"], "a": 0}, {"q": "She ___ call you yesterday — check your phone.", "o": ["did", "does", "do"], "a": 0}, {"q": "My dad does ___ jazz.", "o": ["like", "likes", "liked"], "a": 0}, {"q": "___ come and visit us again!", "o": ["Do", "Does", "Did"], "a": 0}, {"q": "He ___ understand — he just disagrees.", "o": ["does", "do", "did understands"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Which is correct?", "o": ["I did finish my project on time.", "I did finished my project on time.", "I does finish my project on time."], "a": 0}]}, {"id": "con", "title": "Conversation", "ar": "المحادثة", "icon": "💬", "qs": [{"q": "\"Young people never listen!\" — Best answer:", "o": ["We do listen — we just see things differently.", "We did listened.", "Listen is a verb."], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"Who do you take after?\" — Best answer:", "o": ["My father — we're both very calm.", "I take a bus.", "After you."], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"In my day, we had no phones!\" — Polite answer:", "o": ["That must have been very different!", "OK boomer.", "Phones are cheugy."], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"Grandpa still writes letters by hand.\" — Best answer:", "o": ["That's so old school — I love it.", "He is vintage.", "He is a throwback."], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"How can we bridge the generation gap?\" — Best answer:", "o": ["By spending time together and learning from each other.", "By building a bridge.", "By ignoring each other."], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"Did you call Grandma?\" — Best answer (insisting):", "o": ["I did call her — twice!", "I do called her.", "I did called her."], "a": 0}]}, {"id": "rea", "title": "Reading", "ar": "القراءة", "icon": "📖", "passage": ["Nabil is 72, and his granddaughter Jana is 17. They live in the same house in Mansoura.", "At first, they often argued. Nabil thought Jana spent too much time online, and Jana thought her grandfather was set in his ways.", "Then Jana started teaching him how to use video calls, so he could talk to his brother in Canada.", "In return, Nabil taught her to play chess and told her stories about his youth.", "\"He does drive me crazy sometimes,\" Jana laughs, \"but I do love him. He's my best friend.\""], "qs": [{"q": "How old is Nabil?", "o": ["72", "17", "27"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What did Jana think about her grandfather at first?", "o": ["He was set in his ways.", "He was very modern.", "He was rude."], "a": 0}, {"q": "What did Jana teach him?", "o": ["how to use video calls", "how to cook", "how to drive"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What did Nabil teach Jana?", "o": ["to play chess", "to use social media", "to swim"], "a": 0}, {"q": "How does Jana feel about him now?", "o": ["He's her best friend.", "She hates living with him.", "She never talks to him."], "a": 0}]}, {"id": "wri", "title": "Writing", "ar": "الكتابة", "icon": "✍️", "writing": true, "prompt": "Write a letter to an older member of your family (80–120 words). Tell them what you have learned from them and what you could teach them. Use emphatic do/does/did at least three times.", "promptAr": "اكتب جواب لحد كبير في عيلتك (٨٠–١٢٠ كلمة): اتعلمت منه إيه، وتقدر تعلمه إيه. استخدم do/does/did للتأكيد ٣ مرات على الأقل.", "checks": [["👴", "Generation words", "x", "\\b(grandfather|grandmother|grandpa|grandma|teta|parents|generation|young|old|family|wisdom|respect|learn|learned|teach)\\b"], ["🔊", "Emphatic do", "x", "\\b(i|you|we|they|he|she|it)\\s+(do|does|did)\\s+(really\\s+)?(love|respect|appreciate|remember|try|tried|understand|miss|admire|want|believe|thank|learn|listen|care|enjoy|hope|feel)\\b"], ["💌", "Letter phrases", "x", "\\b(dear|love|best wishes|yours|with love)\\b"], ["💬", "At least 70 words", "len70"]]}]}, "watch": [{"yt": "h-NZcQF7jgI", "title": "Learning from Different Generations", "ar": "نتعلم من الأجيال المختلفة — 6 Minute English", "by": "BBC Learning English", "lines": [["Phil and Georgie talk about generations — groups of people born around the same time.", "فيل وجورجي بيتكلموا عن الأجيال — مجموعات ناس اتولدوا في نفس الفترة تقريبًا."], ["Georgie sings in a choir with people of many different ages, and she loves it.", "جورجي بتغني في كورال فيه ناس من أعمار مختلفة كتير، وبتحب ده جدًا."], ["The quiz: if you were born in 1982, are you Generation X, a millennial or Gen Z?", "السؤال: لو اتولدت سنة ١٩٨٢، تبقى من جيل إكس ولا الألفية ولا جيل زد؟"], ["The programme visits a nursery inside a retirement village in Chester, in the north-west of England.", "البرنامج بيزور حضانة جوه قرية للمتقاعدين في تشيستر، في شمال غرب إنجلترا."], ["Older residents join the children every day, and the children call them their \"grandfriends\".", "السكان الكبار بيشاركوا الأطفال كل يوم، والأطفال بيسموهم \"أصحابهم الأجداد\"."], ["They share a library, a café and a garden, and do activities like dancing, crafts and making paper planes.", "بيتشاركوا مكتبة وكافيه وجنينة، وبيعملوا أنشطة زي الرقص والأشغال اليدوية وعمل طيارات ورق."], ["Ian, a former fighter pilot, felt a huge emptiness after his wife died.", "إيان، طيار حربي سابق، حس بفراغ كبير بعد ما مراته ماتت."], ["The nursery invited him to join in, and spending time with the children helped him fill the void.", "الحضانة عزمته يشارك، وقضاء الوقت مع الأطفال ساعده يملا الفراغ ده."], ["Research shows that mixing generations reduces loneliness, improves health and well-being, and boosts creativity.", "الأبحاث بتوضح إن خلط الأجيال بيقلل الوحدة ويحسّن الصحة والإحساس بالراحة ويزوّد الإبداع."], ["The project also helps break down stereotypes about old age.", "المشروع كمان بيساعد يكسر الصور النمطية عن الكبر في السن."], ["We expect young children to be lively, but staff found that the older people are just as energetic — sometimes even more!", "إحنا متوقعين إن الأطفال يبقوا مليانين حيوية، بس الموظفين لقوا إن الكبار نشيطين زيهم — وأحيانًا أكتر!"], ["The answer: someone born in 1982 is a millennial.", "الإجابة: اللي اتولد سنة ١٩٨٢ يبقى من جيل الألفية."]], "words": ["generations", "choir", "millennial", "retirement", "residents", "activities", "former", "fill the void", "loneliness", "well-being", "break down stereotypes", "lively"], "quiz": [{"q": "What is a \"generation\"?", "o": ["a group of people born around the same time", "a type of school", "a family name"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Where is the nursery?", "o": ["inside a retirement village in Chester", "in a big hospital", "in London city centre"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What do the children call the older residents?", "o": ["grandfriends", "teachers", "neighbours"], "a": 0}, {"q": "How did the nursery help Ian?", "o": ["It helped him fill the void after his wife died.", "It gave him a job as a pilot.", "It taught him to dance."], "a": 0}, {"q": "What does mixing generations do, according to research?", "o": ["reduces loneliness and boosts creativity", "makes children tired", "costs a lot of money"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Someone born in 1982 is…", "o": ["a millennial", "Generation X", "Gen Z"], "a": 0}]}]}}, "final": {"pass": 60, "sections": [{"id": "lis", "title": "Listening", "ar": "الاستماع", "icon": "🎧", "listen": true, "qs": [{"audio": "It could be argued that using AI for homework is not cheating, provided that students do the thinking themselves.", "g": "m", "q": "When is using AI not cheating, according to the speaker?", "o": ["when students do the thinking themselves", "always", "never"], "a": 0}, {"audio": "The rapid growth of international chains has led to the disappearance of many small local shops.", "g": "f", "q": "What has the growth of international chains led to?", "o": ["the disappearance of small shops", "more local shops", "lower wages"], "a": 0}, {"audio": "Never have I worked with such a supportive manager. Not only does she listen, but she also gives us credit.", "g": "f2", "q": "What does the manager do?", "o": ["She listens and gives credit.", "She shouts a lot.", "She takes all the credit."], "a": 0}, {"audio": "What really convinced the investors wasn't the technology. It was the story about a real student.", "g": "m2", "q": "What convinced the investors?", "o": ["a story about a real student", "the technology", "the low price"], "a": 0}, {"audio": "Your location can be tracked by many apps, so permissions should be checked regularly.", "g": "f", "q": "What should be checked regularly?", "o": ["app permissions", "the weather", "emails"], "a": 0}, {"audio": "Having finished her degree in engineering, Amal started designing solar systems for villages.", "g": "m", "q": "What did Amal do after her degree?", "o": ["designed solar systems for villages", "became a teacher", "moved abroad"], "a": 0}, {"audio": "I do respect my grandfather's opinions, even though we don't always agree.", "g": "f2", "q": "How does the speaker feel about her grandfather's opinions?", "o": ["She respects them.", "She ignores them.", "She hates them."], "a": 0}, {"audio": "The company kept the data breach under wraps for months before finally admitting it.", "g": "m2", "q": "What did the company do with the data breach?", "o": ["kept it secret for months", "reported it immediately", "never had one"], "a": 0}]}, {"id": "voc", "title": "Vocabulary", "ar": "المفردات", "icon": "📚", "qs": [{"q": "The inner voice telling you right from wrong = your ___.", "o": ["conscience", "consent", "charisma"], "a": 0, "pic": "🧭"}, {"q": "A disadvantage = a ___.", "o": ["drawback", "credit", "pitch"], "a": 0, "pic": "📉"}, {"q": "Understanding how others feel = ___.", "o": ["empathy", "scarcity", "nostalgia"], "a": 0, "pic": "🌈"}, {"q": "A short, catchy advertising phrase = a ___.", "o": ["slogan", "firewall", "stereotype"], "a": 0, "pic": "🏷️"}, {"q": "Agreement or permission = ___.", "o": ["consent", "loyalty", "trade"], "a": 0, "pic": "📢"}, {"q": "A fixed, unfair idea about a group = a ___.", "o": ["stereotype", "tradition", "regulation"], "a": 0, "pic": "🧠"}, {"q": "Knowledge from experience = ___.", "o": ["wisdom", "logic", "hype"], "a": 0, "pic": "💡"}, {"q": "\"Break the glass ceiling\" means…", "o": ["reach a top position despite barriers", "break a window", "fix a roof"], "a": 0, "pic": "🧱"}]}, {"id": "gra", "title": "Grammar", "ar": "القواعد", "icon": "📘", "qs": [{"q": "It could be ___ that social media does more harm than good.", "o": ["argued", "argue", "arguing"], "a": 0}, {"q": "The rapid ___ of technology has changed our lives. (develop)", "o": ["development", "developing", "developance"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Rarely ___ such a talented student.", "o": ["have I met", "I have met", "I met"], "a": 0}, {"q": "___ I need is a long holiday.", "o": ["What", "That", "It"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Personal data ___ without permission.", "o": ["shouldn't be shared", "shouldn't shared", "shouldn't be share"], "a": 0}, {"q": "___ the exam, she celebrated with her friends.", "o": ["Having passed", "Passed", "Having pass"], "a": 0}, {"q": "\"You never help me!\" — \"I ___ help you yesterday!\"", "o": ["did", "do", "was"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Not only ___ the race, but he also broke the record.", "o": ["did he win", "he won", "did he won"], "a": 0}]}, {"id": "rea", "title": "Reading", "ar": "القراءة", "icon": "📖", "passage": ["Having worked for thirty years as a bank manager, Hoda decided to retire early and start something new.", "What she really wanted was to teach young women how to manage money.", "Not only did her free online course attract thousands of students, but it was also shared by several famous influencers.", "Some people warned her that her personal data could be stolen if she became famous online, so she does protect her privacy carefully.", "It could be argued that Hoda has achieved more since retiring than in her whole career."], "qs": [{"q": "What was Hoda's job for thirty years?", "o": ["bank manager", "teacher", "doctor"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What did she really want to do?", "o": ["teach young women to manage money", "travel the world", "open a bank"], "a": 0}, {"q": "Who shared her course?", "o": ["several famous influencers", "her bank", "the government"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What did some people warn her about?", "o": ["her personal data could be stolen", "her course was too expensive", "she was too old"], "a": 0}, {"q": "What could be argued about Hoda?", "o": ["She has achieved more since retiring.", "She should go back to the bank.", "Her course failed."], "a": 0}]}, {"id": "wri", "title": "Writing", "ar": "الكتابة", "icon": "✍️", "writing": true, "prompt": "Write an essay (120–180 words): \"Technology has done more to divide generations than to bring them together.\" Discuss both sides and give your opinion. Use at least four B2+ grammar points.", "promptAr": "اكتب مقال (١٢٠–١٨٠ كلمة): \"التكنولوجيا فرّقت الأجيال أكتر ما قرّبتهم.\" ناقش الرأيين وقول رأيك، واستخدم ٤ قواعد على الأقل من مستوى B2+.", "checks": [["🌫️", "Hedging", "x", "\\b(it could be argued|tends? to|seems?|appears?|arguably|may|might)\\b"], ["🔄", "Inversion / cleft", "x", "\\b(not only|never have|rarely do|seldom|what\\s+\\w+\\s+\\w*\\s*is|it is\\s+\\w+\\s+that)\\b"], ["🔗", "Participle / nominalisation", "x", "\\b(having\\s+\\w+|\\w+(tion|ment|ance|ity)\\s+of)\\b"], ["🔊", "Emphatic do / passive", "x", "\\b(do|does|did)\\s+(really\\s+)?\\w+\\b|\\b(should|must|can)\\s+be\\s+\\w+"], ["💬", "At least 70 words", "len70"]]}]}, "cert": "B2+ – Upper-Intermediate Plus Level", "home": "<span dir=\"rtl\" style=\"display:block\">مستوى <bdi dir=\"ltr\">B2+</bdi> — اتكلم عن الأخلاق والعولمة والقيادة والإقناع والخصوصية والمساواة والفجوة بين الأجيال، ومعاهم Idioms وPhrasal Verbs وSlang وقصص مع Wisy.</span>", "sub": "Upper-Intermediate Plus", "spr": 70, "ch": "img/char-wisy.png"};
